om":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T10:49:30-07:00","id":1243549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1243406#post1243406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue that the Deceived are the most heroic of the assorted mummy variants (though not quite &quot;actually heroic.&quot;) Actually being Deceived is pretty awful, even compared to the standard model &quot;Curse&quot;, but you are at least outside of machinations of Shan'iatu and Ammut. (and still better a Deceived than a Shuankshen)</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm. You are DIRECTLY under the influence of one of seven Shan'iatu, all of whom suffer a ravaging tug-of-war between their desire to cultivate culture and DESTROY CIVILIZATION.<br /> <br /> The Arisen are directed by fuckers and come from a society of fuckers, but to their credit, maintaining the Law of Suffering still contributes to keeping the ball rolling, vs both the Deceived and the Shuankhsen who, at the end of the day, aspire for the end of humanity, or at least crueler methods of reaping the Remet.<br /> <br /> In a game of immortal fucks, the Arisen are the protagonist base because the forces that guide them are depressingly the least of fucks outside of those who attain Apotheosis.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1243451#post1243451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Fasad, full stop.</div> </div> </div> </div>Counter: you can KILL a Fasad, completely. the Shuankhsen have no such repreive.<br /> <br /> This game is kind of fucked up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-07-2018, 01:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T13:40:02-07:00","id":1243585,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1243549#post1243549\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Uhm. You are DIRECTLY under the influence of one of seven Shan'iatu, all of whom suffer a ravaging tug-of-war between their desire to cultivate culture and DESTROY CIVILIZATION.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but arguably the seven least successful Shan'iatu, whose connection to the others is more backstory than a practical reflection where they fit into the whole &quot;Rite of Return&quot; shinanigans, and the Deceived have a marginally better idea as to what the score is when it comes to the competing Powers-That-Be.<br /> <br /> (Doesn't make having a shattered God-being in your soul any better, mind you.)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T13:46:23-07:00","id":1243588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1243585#post1243585\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, but arguably the seven least successful Shan'iatu, whose connection to the others is more backstory than a practical reflection where they fit into the whole &quot;Rite of Return&quot; shinanigans, and the Deceived have a marginally better idea as to what the score is when it comes to the competing Powers-That-Be.<br /> <br /> (Doesn't make having a shattered God-being in your soul any better, mind you.)</div> </div> </div> </div>All of that is true, and all that also does not obviate the fact that the guild on the whole is, you figure, half of the time trying to end the world we live in, and while arguments can be made about whether or not that's ultimately a good thing or not, I* object on the grounds on being one of the idiots who lives in it.<br /> <br /> *I as in a ficitionalized concept of myself who lives in this fictional universe, because we do not live in a world with tyrant-judges who we escape from by wearing the corpse-face of a sandstorm-snake god and Tex-Mex with all the essential ingredients for reals on each corner.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T13:57:57-07:00","id":1243593,"title":"","content":"Well, I am operating on scale relative to &quot;Semi-unwitting slaves to Wannabe Gods&quot; and &quot;Actual slaves to one of the least* ambiguously evil things in the whole Chronicles of Darkness&quot; If any of the Mummy Groups really had their way the world would be a far be different place, and not a good one for us. (With possible exceptions of Ascended and Apotheotic mummies if you want to treat them as their own splinter group.)<br /> <br /> Edit: *Thats &quot;least&quot; in terms of ambiguity, not evil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","user":"schizoPOP","date":". 08-07-2018, 05:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T15:29:34-07:00","id":1243622,"title":"","content":"&quot;Semi-unwitting&quot; and &quot;actual&quot; apply to both, and I really think there's a difference between &quot;Assholes who think they should chuck in whoever to keep Ammut from snapping her mouth shut but have agreed to play by Will God's edicts&quot; and &quot;Assholes who think civilaztion should be destroyed and are predominantly stopped by their counter-urges towards culture creation.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Judges are assholes who should have their hands in the world removed via Apotheosis, but at least nominally they still play the game of &quot;Humanity and their endeavors deserve to be around and maybe even find their way into the heaven that could be theirs.&quot; That's why the Arisen are the shallow end of the pool.<br /> <br /> EDIT: I mean, really, the arithmetic is simple. One side wants to keep humanity around since it's a benefit to their goals, the other has the goal of wanting to destroy humanity.<br /> <br /> Even if they are both assholes, the one not wanting us all to go back to the stone age is better than the one that does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-07-2018, 07:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T17:45:27-07:00","id":1243656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1243622#post1243622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: I mean, really, the arithmetic is simple. One side wants to keep humanity around since it's a benefit to their goals, the other has the goal of wanting to destroy humanity.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think we're using different arithmetic here. As far as &quot;Sides&quot; go, the individual mummy, the local mummy culture, the agenda that they are directly progressing, and the actual desires of their patrons may all be on different pages. All other factors being either equal, or at least too removed from every-century affairs to be of consequence, the most &quot;heroic&quot; group is the one most likely come to the informed conclusion: &quot;this is terrible.&quot; (and therefore have any motivation to act on any not-so-evil agenda, limited though one's agency in practice may be.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T18:08:27-07:00","id":1243665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>schizoPOP</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1243656#post1243656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think we're using different arithmetic here. As far as &quot;Sides&quot; go, the individual mummy, the local mummy culture, the agenda that they are directly progressing, and the actual desires of their patrons may all be on different pages. All other factors being either equal, or at least too removed from every-century affairs to be of consequence, the most &quot;heroic&quot; group is the one most likely come to the informed conclusion: &quot;this is terrible.&quot; (and therefore have any motivation to act on any not-so-evil agenda, limited though one's agency in practice may be.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but that group is also the ones who literally have fragments of their distant gods riding shotgun where a geist would be for a Sin-Eater and has death cycles that reinforce just How Bad An Idea it would be for them to try anything crazy (implementation beyond that is debateable).<br /> <br /> PLus, you gotta remember, a lot of the Deceived <i>agree</i> with the Shan'iatu on some level, <i>and</i> are still prone to the biases of the Nameless Empire as a result of cultural upbringing before you account for the supernatural relationships.<br /> <br /> It's <i>tempting</i> to romanticize the Deceived, but it is a mistake to do so-these are not people who lighten up most of the time as a result of their position, these are folks who double down because of it. They are highly informed, yes, but they are informed several times over at different stages of their lives and at different levels of intimacy by proto-Egyptian fallen angels whose idea of a temper tantrum includes the end of civilization.<br /> <br /> Their predicament makes them more likely to be villains, not less. Again, there's a reason these guys <i>are the bad guys</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T18:28:53-07:00","id":1243668,"title":"","content":"Sorry for the very late reply, so what's the bed result of this (interesting) argument? I'm just wondering how they can be portrayed when actually used as player characters","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T18:56:00-07:00","id":1243675,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's sufficient evidence without a bunch of case-by-case storycraft to say that they are more prone to evil than your standard model Arisen (especially since part of the reasoning here is &quot;still from Irem&quot;). And their book puts way, way too much effort into developing them for them to exist purely in the realm of antagonists. (and quite frankly, a lot of their animosity is pointed in the right direction, even if their means and reasoning are suspect.)<br /> <br /> Ultimately, their standing relative to Guilds is the sum total of what I'm arguing about here. Ultimately the existence of Deceived is bad for the world* as a whole, and presence of even a benign, ascended Deceived is not good news, much less the presence of one grappling with a mad god shard.<br /> <br /> *does anyone else missing being able to use &quot;the world of darkness&quot; to summarize the setting?<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1243668#post1243668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry for the very late reply, so what's the bed result of this (interesting) argument? I'm just wondering how they can be portrayed when actually used as player characters</div> </div> </div> </div>Thwarting other mummies mostly, in terms of story plot. Grappling with the agony of one's own existence for personal plot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":526,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","user":"schizoPOP","date":". 08-07-2018, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T19:45:38-07:00","id":1243681,"title":"","content":"Ahh ok, so villain protagonist in the nemesis vein, while as a character portrayed as a tragic villain, trapped into something he has to do, no matter the slippery slope he falls","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T20:08:39-07:00","id":1243685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1243681#post1243681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ahh ok, so villain protagonist in the nemesis vein, while as a character portrayed as a tragic villain, trapped into something he has to do, no matter the slippery slope he falls</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the megalomaniacal God-Monster-Fragment stappled to their soul, Villain Protagonist is a pretty good descriptor. The <i>Temakh</i> gives you ample excuse to engage in Evil Overlord behavior, and Deceived cultists are fanatically loyal mooks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T20:18:16-07:00","id":1243687,"title":"","content":"So being a deceived means having great power, at a price so terrible you wish it never happened.<br /> <br /> Last two questions. Are there any themes to be explored as deceived, and do cultist take pretty much any sentence you say as one of divine meaning, basically being idiotic in their faith for you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T20:30:38-07:00","id":1243691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1243687#post1243687\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So being a deceived means having great power, at a price so terrible you wish it never happened.<br /> <br /> Last two questions. Are there any themes to be explored as deceived, and do cultist take pretty much any sentence you say as one of divine meaning, basically being idiotic in their faith for you</div> </div> </div> </div>To certain degree, that's just a theme of mummy, but it tends to be more overt with the deceived. Its also notable that Name magic and Artistry are a big part of Deceived, as that was their vocation as a proper guild.<br /> <br /> Being a deceived cultist isn't a complete mind rewrite, but having even 1-dot in the merit makes you immune to any attempts to force you to betray your cult, and costs a willpower to do so voluntarily. (You get supernatural powers at higher levels!)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T20:36:33-07:00","id":1243692,"title":"","content":"Ok, thanks for the answers and the cultist power gain sounds really Cool, the wait will be long but much worth it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T02:48:06-07:00","id":1243737,"title":"","content":"So the Deceived have reasons to be the villains, but are they forced to it or is it rather just that they just are more likely to be villains? Sin-Eaters, Forsaken and Renegades are all subgroups of various official splats that are the intended heroic playable protagonists where their larger groups (Bound, werewolves and deviants, respectively) can vary wildly between altruistic or duty-bound heroes to tyrannical or sadistic villains. The Pure and the loyalists do have some mechanical differences, but Sin-Eaters are only defined by their goal to help the dead move on.<br /> Not that playing villains is undesirable. I personally find villain protagonists to have great potential to be interesting characters.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T09:02:19-07:00","id":1243814,"title":"","content":"Well, part of it comes down to the not-so-secret that standard mummies are pawns of some of the more villanous elements of the gameline, which the the Deceived are pretty firmly against. As the game's primary focus is not actually about the Deceived, this puts them in them in an antagonistic role towards the PCs by default. That said, their philosophies on how to act against the Shan'iatu can be pretty suspect (&quot;Civilization purifies humanity. Unmake it.&quot;)<br /> <br /> Mechanically, they get an altered list of &quot;Sekhem Sins&quot;, are more prone to derangements, and suffer a bane reflecting the mad God-Shard in their soul. (and some have some benefits to being weird and alien in general)<br /> <br /> Ultimately all deathless are victims of a theocratic slave state and the otherworldly beings that guided it. Even the most callously destructive Deceived (or Shuankhsen for that matter) is a tragedy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T10:45:10-07:00","id":1243847,"title":"","content":"How do you you cultivate culture? But destroy civilization?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T19:43:06-07:00","id":1244028,"title":"","content":"Simple, you hit the restart button. Humble humanity by bringing down their ivory towers and dismantling their high tech weaponry. From there, be worshipped as a god and influence a new beginning of the human race","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T12:58:31-07:00","id":1244253,"title":"","content":"Did Irem have a version of Sobek?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 08-09-2018, 04:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-09T13:14:15-07:00","id":1244256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1244253#post1244253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did item have a version of sobek</div> </div> </div> </div>Not as noted so far, no. THere was a fan splat for Crocodile-headed Decrees that built on an Iremite Sobek, but no such thing exists in canon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T14:14:12-07:00","id":1244619,"title":"","content":"How would the temkahs react to promtheans?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T15:26:20-07:00","id":1244639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1244619#post1244619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would the temkahs react to promtheans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on which Temakh and circumstance. Between Disquiet and the general regard of the temakhs, though, &quot;they would be assholes&quot; is always a good baseline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T15:49:05-07:00","id":1244647,"title":"","content":"What would they make of Pyros ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T16:27:26-07:00","id":1244655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1244647#post1244647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would they make of Pyros ?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I don't think there's a particularly meaningful &quot;steeped in canon&quot; answer to this question. Mummy doesn't have particularly deep cross-over rules for things not called Mage, and when dips a toe in other metaphysics it tends to stick to the necromantic side of things. (Which, despite appearances, is not Promethean's bread and butter.) What do you, the person running this hypothetical scenario, think Pyros looks like in the context of Fate and Sekhem and those sorts of things, and extrapolate from there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/526-schizopop","name":"schizoPOP","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"108"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T17:07:51-07:00","id":1244667,"title":"","content":"Azar is iremd version of Osiris right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T17:19:59-07:00","id":1244671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1244667#post1244667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Azar is iremd version of Osiris right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically, yes.<br /> Irem came first though; it should be noted it is not same one from Promthean though.<br /> <br /> It should be noted there is an entire social splat (Guild) that deals with alchemy. Plus like pyros, sekham is distinct physical source of magic. If you want cross-over material then it is not hard to have an Arisen cult of alchemists; with the added benefit that the Mummy might not be happy with the 'distraction' of all this pyros nonsense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-10T17:22:50-07:00","id":1244673,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m imagining a mummy being really pissed that while they where asleep there cult has wasted there resources trying to catch a cheap parody of them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar