]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T09:51:01-07:00","id":1249162,"title":"","content":"What where irems gender roles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T10:11:41-07:00","id":1249164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1249162#post1249162\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What where irems gender roles</div> </div> </div> </div>In Irem, largely, though I suppose they exported their gender roles to subjugated territories as well.<br /> <br /> As for what they <i>were</i>, I think it was stated that at least in the &quot;favored servant&quot; level that the future-Arisen occupied, they were somewhat egalitarian - if you could do the work, you had the job. I'm guessing there was at least some Patriarchal leanings, though, considering the Shan'Iatu all decided to be male.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":7212,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","user":"Vent0","date":". 08-27-2018, 01:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T16:04:47-07:00","id":1249230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1249164#post1249164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for what they <i>were</i>, I think it was stated that at least in the &quot;favored servant&quot; level that the future-Arisen occupied, they were somewhat egalitarian - if you could do the work, you had the job. I'm guessing there was at least some Patriarchal leanings, though, considering the Shan'Iatu all decided to be male.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure that's only the Lost Guild. There's at least one reference to the Deceived Shan'iatu's &quot;brothers and sisters&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T17:35:02-07:00","id":1249237,"title":"","content":"Ancient Egypt well not a feminist paradise was much more equalitan then its Roman and Greek neighbors","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T18:01:07-07:00","id":1249241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1249237#post1249237\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ancient Egypt well not a feminist paradise was much more equalitan then its Roman and Greek neighbors</div> </div> </div> </div>To utter once more the timeless chant: Irem was not Ancient Egypt.<br /> <br /> But the egalitarianism is (probably) largely a conceit for less-baised modern gaming sensibilities. So players can play male or female (or other) Mummies without sweating demographics.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-27T18:19:39-07:00","id":1249242,"title":"","content":"To by fair it\u2019s not like the mummies where the elites of Irem society or something","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T10:49:42-07:00","id":1249485,"title":"","content":"Just adding with Vent0-while a patriarchical society, the demands of the Empire were such that it just wasn't practical to not use people who were effective, regardless of gender. The sexism of later cultures weren't quite present in the Empire out of sheer practicality, which you need when you inevitably need to build an immortal empire monument to the god you killed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T11:22:13-07:00","id":1249496,"title":"","content":"Did Irem have any domesticated animals?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T11:58:47-07:00","id":1249504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1249496#post1249496\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Irem have any domesticated animals?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably all the same of within the era that other societies had. Cattle, horses, cats, dogs, certain reptiles and birds, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T13:07:12-07:00","id":1249511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1249485#post1249485\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just adding with Vent0-while a patriarchical society, the demands of the Empire were such that it just wasn't practical to not use people who were effective, regardless of gender. The sexism of later cultures weren't quite present in the Empire out of sheer practicality, which you need when you inevitably need to build an immortal empire monument to the god you killed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Especially if they were operating on a time table set by Sothis's next visit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-28T13:24:49-07:00","id":1249515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1249511#post1249511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Especially if they were operating on a time table set by Sothis's next visit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Doubling down on this is the problem of not knowing just how much of the current Sothic Cycle they had to work with. They sure didn't have the whole 1,421 years to work with, and it was still some time more into the Empire that the Rite of Return became the mission statement. Even if it started 500 years before the Rite, that's not a lot of time to create an engine capable of breaking time.<br /> <br /> You know, if we could find a reasonably suitable enough timeframe for the conflict with the Awakened of Kish that would have worked as a talking stage for Ammut, we might be able to settle more of the timeline with them, maybe get a better sense of when explicit work started.<br /> <br /> Anyways, between time and resources, they really did not have a good reason to let things like gender fuck around with the plan, and that's before you remember that the Shan'iatu had, at that time, an added layer of seperation for that kind of crap in that they were temakh and the citizens were literally sacrifices*, in that grand scheme of things. Once some of them got stuck in their servants, it became more of an issue, but the Empire really did not care.<br /> <br /> *Humans were called Remet in Irem, which translates out to &quot;sacrifice&quot;. THe term goes about as far back in Iremite mythology as the creation of humanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T15:02:47-07:00","id":1312830,"title":"","content":"Any of you played a Deceived?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T15:52:52-07:00","id":1312839,"title":"","content":"What does uter mean?<br /> <br /> Like, literal translation. I know what the relics are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-17T17:37:50-07:00","id":1312851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1312839#post1312839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does uter mean?<br /> <br /> Like, literal translation. I know what the relics are.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as I can find it's derived from a Proto-Indo-European word meaning, mostly, &quot;either or&quot;. A hieratic dictionary I found has &quot;tr&quot; (seeing as the language has next to no written vowels and they're often context driven) as &quot;time/season&quot;, &quot;just so&quot;, and &quot;respect/adoration/worship&quot;.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T14:09:50-07:00","id":1313017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vent0</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1249241#post1249241\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To utter once more the timeless chant: Irem was not Ancient Egypt.<br /> <br /> But the egalitarianism is (probably) largely a conceit for less-baised modern gaming sensibilities. So players can play male or female (or other) Mummies without sweating demographics.</div> </div> </div> </div>Irem is indeed not Egypt. For example, if a player came to me with an idea inspired by an ancient egyptian goddess I could let him run with it. But if that player came to me with the same idea set in canon Irem, I'd have to say sorry the Iremites were super patriarchical and didn't worship any of the dozens of cool Egyptian goddesses because they gotta be darker and edgier than their descendants. Or some fucking reason like that.<br /> <br /> Can you tell this is one of the very few additions to the Irem backstory I thought was a big ass misstep and cheerfully ignore at every possible opportunity? It also doesn't jive with the theme well for me. These are literal asexual or at least hermphroditic cthonic cosmic horrors doing the whole lovecraftian indifference to the suffering of mankind thing who send a punch of god-sorcerers to build this city who are all on record as regarding the human race as a whole as literal animals who at best show a dim promise when properly trained. Neither of these forces strikes me as likely to decide that one important factor in who has the power in their new society should rest on if they got a penis. <br /> <br /> Also...totally personal bias here but...its so boring. Bronze age patriarchies are a dime a dozen in regular history. Egypt always stood out to me by not following the model of its peers. Making Irem just like everywhere else in early history felt like a reduction more than anything. It took away goddesses, limited character backgrounds, and left me uninspired. <br /> <br /> My opinion on the subject, obviously. You feel different, more power to you. Its not a direction I can say I got behind, and if second edition wants to maybe down play that aspect I'd be fine with that decision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-18T16:47:49-07:00","id":1313036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1313017#post1313017\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Irem is indeed not Egypt. For example, if a player came to me with an idea inspired by an ancient egyptian goddess I could let him run with it. But if that player came to me with the same idea set in canon Irem, I'd have to say sorry the Iremites were super patriarchical and didn't worship any of the dozens of cool Egyptian goddesses because they gotta be darker and edgier than their descendants. Or some fucking reason like that.<br /> <br /> Can you tell this is one of the very few additions to the Irem backstory I thought was a big ass misstep and cheerfully ignore at every possible opportunity? It also doesn't jive with the theme well for me. These are literal asexual or at least hermphroditic cthonic cosmic horrors doing the whole lovecraftian indifference to the suffering of mankind thing who send a punch of god-sorcerers to build this city who are all on record as regarding the human race as a whole as literal animals who at best show a dim promise when properly trained. Neither of these forces strikes me as likely to decide that one important factor in who has the power in their new society should rest on if they got a penis.<br /> <br /> Also...totally personal bias here but...its so boring. Bronze age patriarchies are a dime a dozen in regular history. Egypt always stood out to me by not following the model of its peers. Making Irem just like everywhere else in early history felt like a reduction more than anything. It took away goddesses, limited character backgrounds, and left me uninspired.<br /> <br /> My opinion on the subject, obviously. You feel different, more power to you. Its not a direction I can say I got behind, and if second edition wants to maybe down play that aspect I'd be fine with that decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing you are responding to was an issue that was responded to the better part of a year ago.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T11:07:43-07:00","id":1313340,"title":"","content":"This question has two parts to it:<br /> <br /> When invoking the Rite of Return and assigning a purpose to your Arisen patron/servant-<br /> <br /> 1. Must you assign a singular purpose, or can you ask for several small tasks to be performed?<br /> <br /> 2. Can the purpose be open ended and somewhat endless, such as &quot;Attend to the needs of your Guild and assist your fellow Arisen who come your aid&quot; or some such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T11:18:37-07:00","id":1313341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1313036#post1313036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing you are responding to was an issue that was responded to the better part of a year ago.</div> </div> </div> </div>And? I didn't see anyone else expressing an alternative opinion to what had already been said and thought a different perspective might be worth hearing. Its not intended to call out or provoke a response from the ones who originally expressed the idea, its simply putting other ideas out there. Unless there's a statute of limitations on responding to threads I'm okay with coming in after the fact. Not like we have a huge influx of new posts coming in to keep up with to begin with.<br /> <br /> Besides, Second Edition is getting finalized. If talking about the strengths and weaknesses of the old edition aren't something we should be doing now, when the heck should we?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T11:34:38-07:00","id":1313345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1313341#post1313341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides, Second Edition is getting finalized. If talking about the strengths and weaknesses of the old edition aren't something we should be doing now, when the heck should we?</div> </div> </div> </div>Timeframe is not the issue so much as placement. This isn't the &quot;share your opinion about aspects of First Edition basically unprompted&quot; thread and so you would be better served making a thread for that topic if you want to start beef with another poster over a thing they said nine months ago in response to a question that existed as a battery of unqualified questions about everyday life in Irem.<br /> <br /> Like, seriously, we had &quot;What Do You Want To See?&quot; threads for half the gamelines that now possess Second Editions, there's no need to further derail a thread already cluttered away from its notional purpose when it's barely into double-digit pagecount.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T14:40:58-07:00","id":1313381,"title":"","content":"&quot;This isn't the &quot;share your opinion about aspects of First Edition basically unprompted&quot; thread and so you would be better served making a thread for that topic if you want to start beef with another poster over a thing they said nine months ago in response to a question that existed as a battery of unqualified questions about everyday life in Irem.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm gonna go ahead and assume I'm just not being fully understood and that you are not in fact calling me a liar in a backhanded way. Either way, the statement your making doesn't apply to me or my intentions. Sorry if that wasn't made clear in my last post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T14:51:34-07:00","id":1313383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1313381#post1313381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;This isn't the &quot;share your opinion about aspects of First Edition basically unprompted&quot; thread and so you would be better served making a thread for that topic if you want to start beef with another poster over a thing they said nine months ago in response to a question that existed as a battery of unqualified questions about everyday life in Irem.&quot;<br /> <br /> I'm gonna go ahead and assume I'm just not being fully understood and that you are not in fact calling me a liar in a backhanded way. Either way, the statement your making doesn't apply to me or my intentions. Sorry if that wasn't made clear in my last post.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T15:45:28-07:00","id":1313402,"title":"","content":"Please don't. I have enough people in my life who happily assume they know me and my intentions better than I do. I assure you, I have a pretty firm grasp of my motivations and desires. I don't need your help figuring it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-20T16:28:42-07:00","id":1313415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1313402#post1313402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please don't. I have enough people in my life who happily assume they know me and my intentions better than I do. I assure you, I have a pretty firm grasp of my motivations and desires. I don't need your help figuring it out.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your intentions are not the thing under discussion here and nobody is making a claim to having better Self-Knowledge Of OPP Forum Poster Nothri than you. Your intentions are also not the things coming out of your keyboard, which is the issue.<br /> <br /> It's <i>the execution</i> that is under discussion, and so far the execution is you making a reply to a post from last year in a thread with a purpose that's not pure opinion-broadcasting using second-person pronouns, broadly inflammatory language, and the same bad-faith appeal to flexibility that other contentious arguments on this board in particular have made use of, then presenting the claim that you did this purely for the sake of sharing your opinion when there are at least four other means of doing so that are better suited to that activity than making a very strong show of picking a fight in an established general Q&amp;A thread eight months past the defensible window for doing so (because while timeframe is not the issue, it would have been pretty much the only thing that could have justified the rest of that approach).<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bNow, to return to the actual function of this thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1313340#post1313340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Must you assign a singular purpose, or can you ask for several small tasks to be performed?</div> </div> </div> </div>While Mummy is presently a First Edition gameline and therefore does not have Aspirations as a game mechanic, I suspect that similar &quot;these should be pretty broadly-stated&quot; advice applies to the first and final purposes of one of the Arisen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. Can the purpose be open ended and somewhat endless, such as &quot;Attend to the needs of your Guild and assist your fellow Arisen who come your aid&quot; or some such. </div> </div> </div>Similarly to the above, I get the feeling that in a game about timelessness and entropy, the things keeping mummies active should be specifically finite and limited, if only because the fiction establishes the relative freedom of the Sothic Turns as unusual times when the Arisen <i>aren't</i> constrained by their purposes; &quot;set your cult's protector a vague task that basically doesn't limit their empowered activities at all&quot; is very clearly gaming the system compared to, say, setting out a multi-stage plan that requires separate Descents that still bind you further to your cult through the toll on your Memory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T06:12:22-07:00","id":1313827,"title":"","content":"<br /> I'd like to respond to the criticism I have received, but I am mindful of the original purpose of this thread and will try to keep my comments brief and resist the urge to keep this conversation going after this.<br /> <br /> &quot;Your intentions are not the thing under discussion here and nobody is making a claim to having better Self-Knowledge Of OPP Forum Poster Nothri than you. Your intentions are also not the things coming out of your keyboard, which is the issue.&quot;<br /> <br /> All well and good, except I don't believe there was ever an effort to distinguish my intent from my execution until you made this post. And more to the point, I think it is fair to say your assumptions about my intent have colored prior criticism about what I said and unfortunately what you say in this post. More on that below<br /> <br /> (Apologies, there is clearly a way to get the forum to quote individual lines of text, but it is yet another mystery I cannot solve before my morning caffeine, so I'm doing it all manually)<br /> <br /> &quot;It's <i>the execution</i> that is under discussion, and so far the execution is you making a reply to a post from last year in a thread with a purpose that's not pure opinion-broadcasting using second-person pronouns, broadly inflammatory language, and the same bad-faith appeal to flexibility that other contentious arguments on this board in particular have made use of,&quot;<br /> <br /> Some of that I agree with. It was a strong opinion back when I first came across the idea in Avarice, and its been a strong opinion whenever it has come back up over the years (few and far between as discussing the topic has been). So my language probably was more inflammatory than it needed to be, so I'll own that part. I reject that I am making a bad faith argument out of hand- I don't believe I've seen any of these prior arguments you mention, but that aside I certainly wasn't involved with them. While I can see hypothetical ways the flexibility argument could be used in bad faith I don't think it is intrinsic to the argument itself that it must be made in bad faith, and I don't believe I am doing so here. As for second person pronouns...yeah, I have no comment one way or another. I am firmly missing whatever the point of your criticism is on that one.<br /> <br /> And while I again appreciate the original point of the thread, I will note that I am FAR from the first to go on a tangent here, nor even started the tangent I commented on. Beyond that, while I do want to respect the original intent of this topic, I'll also just put out there that I for one don't see the tangents that have evolved out of discussing the answers made to the original questions as detrimental to that intent as others seem to think they are.<br /> <br /> &quot;then presenting the claim that you did this purely for the sake of sharing your opinion when there are at least four other means of doing so that are better suited to that activity&quot;<br /> <br /> I will usually post new thoughts and opinions in the thread whose discussions inspired them. I will probably do so in the future as well. Sorry I'm not sorry about that.<br /> <br /> &quot;than making a very strong show of picking a fight in an established general Q&amp;A thread eight months past the defensible window for doing so (because while timeframe is not the issue, it would have been pretty much the only thing that could have justified the rest of that approach).&quot;<br /> <br /> I appreciate that you are trying not to make direct accusations after I objected to you doing so, but this in particular tells me this is absolutely not solely and objectively about the execution of my post. You are still insinuating what my intentions were, based on your false assumptions. You are still implying I was looking for a fight when I've stated I was not. While I appreciate the efforts to somewhat downplay that narrative after I raised objections to it, I think the assumptions are still very much there and are continuing to color your impressions and your approach to this conversation. As I hope I've made clear, my execution was far from flawless and some of your criticism is certainly fair. But I have objections of my own to how you've characterized the situation, so my response has been mixed. But I believe I've said all I wanted to say, so I'll leave it at that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T06:49:33-07:00","id":1313837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd just ignore that person honestly.</div> </div> </div> </div>See, the thing is, I can't fault someone for a bad first impression. Attention Deficit kinda makes those inevitable. You miss social cues, you fail to question what your actions or words might imply in a given context, etc. Having to explain yourself becomes par for the course. Its the people that double down on their assumptions I have no patience with. The ones that don't respond with &quot;Well, you said this which made me believe this&quot; or something along those lines (the ones who are at least slightly ready to entertain the possibility that you've been misunderstood) but instead say &quot;No, we have put you in this box and in this box you shall stay no matter what you say) that I lose all patience with. I know its a psychological thing- people get a negative impression in their heads and instinctively cling to it. It just often surprises and disappoints me how many seemingly intelligent and nuanced people I meet turn out to be close minded in this particular way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-23T18:16:38-07:00","id":1313958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1313827#post1313827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(Apologies, there is clearly a way to get the forum to quote individual lines of text, but it is yet another mystery I cannot solve before my morning caffeine, so I'm doing it all manually)</div> </div> </div> </div>It's simply manually inserting the [*quote][*/quote] tags before and after the text you want formatted as a quote, for the record.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I have objections of my own to how you've characterized the situation, so my response has been mixed. </div> </div> </div>The situation is that you came across as extremely confrontational and are continuing to fixate on the fact that I've been saying your presentation has been confrontational as though I'm making insinuations about who you are as a person instead of that I would like you to not do that or act as though doing that is defensible. I could not care less what your intentions are, because your intentions are not your posts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But I believe I've said all I wanted to say, so I'll leave it at that. </div> </div> </div>Please actually do this next time instead of immediately following it with a post about how you're so disappointed that people misunderstand you in a way that directly states your belief that this is a personal failing of theirs. It's very galling to see that in the same paragraph as you've characterized the response that is not the one you want as making assumptions about you as a person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T04:45:12-07:00","id":1325549,"title":"","content":"How often can an Arisen be called by their cult to another Descent? Is there a &quot;cooldown period&quot;, or could they be called back again almost immediately if something else demanded the Arisen's attention?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16-cielle","name":"Cielle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T05:53:16-07:00","id":1325572,"title":"","content":"Typically it takes several months for the artifact used to power the Rite of Return to become functional again, give or take a few weeks. Your average descent takes longer than a vessel does to recharge- barring a simple mission or a Mummy that really really pisses of the judges a lot. Other than that the only limit is how many magical artifacts are available or cultists willing to sacrifice themselves in a soul merger. Of course there is the ever present danger that something goes wrong and the Mummy becomes shusnkhsen but that\u2019s not exactly the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-07-18T14:40:47-07:00","id":1325736,"title":"","content":"Becoming a Shuankhsen is not exactly an ever present danger either, since it only really occurs in the case of making a Twice-Arisen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-10-15T10:56:13-07:00","id":1341474,"title":"","content":"I am just curious on the reason why the game rules limit the under of Affinities a mummy can have to their rank in the particular Pillar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T10:22:17-08:00","id":1347946,"title":"","content":"Actual mechanics question. I don't understand the Pillar Points/Turn chart if the number after the slash relating to Turns is always 1. (The number before the slash means the maximum Pillar rank a mummy can have at that Sekhem rating, right?)<br /> <br /> If it never rises above one point per turn then why have the chart at all? This chart is both in 1e and 2e in the Sekhem rules btw.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T10:56:06-08:00","id":1347960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LordHeru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1347946#post1347946\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actual mechanics question. I don't understand the Pillar Points/Turn chart if the number after the slash relating to Turns is always 1. (The number before the slash means the maximum Pillar rank a mummy can have at that Sekhem rating, right?)<br /> <br /> If it never rises above one point per turn then why have the chart at all? This chart is both in 1e and 2e in the Sekhem rules btw.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a valid point and we'll probably be removing it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T11:09:49-08:00","id":1347964,"title":"","content":"Is it possible to declare a supernatural being an Inheritor?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-12T12:47:22-08:00","id":1347986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1347964#post1347964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it possible to declare a supernatural being an Inheritor?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is indeed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T15:41:27-08:00","id":1348346,"title":"","content":"Okay, reading over the appendix and seeing what kind of nastiness the fiends of Duat can unleash:<br /> <br /> How do they get into the world? I can see extreme Sybaris opens a doorway, assuming they can possess the Desecrated from Duat, but do sorcerers call them, do they just show up around mummies and emanations of the Judges?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T16:19:25-08:00","id":1348356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1348346#post1348346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, reading over the appendix and seeing what kind of nastiness the fiends of Duat can unleash:<br /> <br /> How do they get into the world? I can see extreme Sybaris opens a doorway, assuming they can possess the Desecrated from Duat, but do sorcerers call them, do they just show up around mummies and emanations of the Judges?</div> </div> </div> </div>I can\u2019t wait for everyone to learn the answer to that question. Finding ways to get them out where they could cause trouble in the world was something I gave a lot of thought to when I wrote them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-13T18:57:43-08:00","id":1348388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1348346#post1348346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, reading over the appendix and seeing what kind of nastiness the fiends of Duat can unleash:<br /> <br /> How do they get into the world? I can see extreme Sybaris opens a doorway, assuming they can possess the Desecrated from Duat, but do sorcerers call them, do they just show up around mummies and emanations of the Judges?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good questions!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T15:34:10-08:00","id":1348564,"title":"","content":"Fingers crossed the reason has to do with the devourer and those mysteriuous Maws of hers alluded to in the Book of the Deceived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T17:40:59-08:00","id":1348585,"title":"","content":"So I was wondering if the Judge that a player picks for his mummy character have any mechanical oomph?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-14T21:41:17-08:00","id":1348611,"title":"","content":"In the Cult section, it says that it costs 6 Experiences to improve a Cult Attribute. But it says that each dot of the Cult Merit adds one to a Cult Attribute. Doesn't that mean, practically speaking, that it only costs 1 Experience to increase a Cult Attribute? Or is the 6 value only if you're spending Cult Beasts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T01:45:31-08:00","id":1348626,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1348611#post1348611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the Cult section, it says that it costs 6 Experiences to improve a Cult Attribute. But it says that each dot of the Cult Merit adds one to a Cult Attribute. Doesn't that mean, practically speaking, that it only costs 1 Experience to increase a Cult Attribute? Or is the 6 value only if you're spending Cult Beasts?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be Cult Experiences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T03:33:28-08:00","id":1348635,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1348626#post1348626\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That would be Cult Experiences.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so to increase Cult Attributes you can basically either spend one regular Experience (on the Merit) or six Cult Experiences directly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T06:25:38-08:00","id":1348655,"title":"","content":"Makes sense since Cult Experiences are inherently less valuable than regular ones due to their limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Revlid wrote:<br /> Yes, hollowing out your humanity to become an utterly utilitarian asura is the exact suggestion I would expect from you, Aiden.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/168-aiden","name":"Aiden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T07:17:53-08:00","id":1348665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1348635#post1348635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so to increase Cult Attributes you can basically either spend one regular Experience (on the Merit) or six Cult Experiences directly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Per the Cult Merit, you need to spend Cult Experiences to raise an Attribute higher than 5, but yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-15T13:14:00-08:00","id":1348720,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aiden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1348655#post1348655\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Makes sense since Cult Experiences are inherently less valuable than regular ones due to their limits.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also an entirely separate experience pool that builds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-19T21:26:56-08:00","id":1349777,"title":"","content":"Does the line &quot;Vestiges provide a number of Pillar points equal to their rating&quot; on page 71 of Preview # 3 refer to draining them from their Pillars? I'm assuming so, but it's not really clear what that line refers to.<br /> <br /> Edit: Never mind, it gets spelled out later in the section. Not 100% sure if that line feels redundant in retrospect, it definitely confused me reading the rules in order.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1059,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","user":"Azahul","date":". 11-20-2019, 01:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-20T05:06:50-08:00","id":1349842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Azahul</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1349777#post1349777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the line &quot;Vestiges provide a number of Pillar points equal to their rating&quot; on page 71 of Preview # 3 refer to draining them from their Pillars? I'm assuming so, but it's not really clear what that line refers to.<br /> <br /> Edit: Never mind, it gets spelled out later in the section. Not 100% sure if that line feels redundant in retrospect, it definitely confused me reading the rules in order.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I went through the same confusion. Simply adding &quot;when harvested/destroyed/whatever they provide&quot; in there should fix it, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T10:18:41-08:00","id":1362441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1312839#post1312839\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does uter mean?<br /> <br /> Like, literal translation. I know what the relics are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Much belated, but I think it's <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/uter#Noun\" target=\"_blank\">a thing in the same vein as the Su-Menent being priests of &quot;the Shell&quot;</a> \u2014 &quot;vessel&quot; is obviously already taken as a term relating to relics (as is &quot;relic,&quot; for that matter), but &quot;thing made of Dead Stuff that holds supernatural power&quot; is a bit more particular than we've got other common words available for.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T11:05:06-07:00","id":1375650,"title":"","content":"Are supernatural splats effected by sybaris?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-19T12:45:49-07:00","id":1375669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heroofthemists</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1375650#post1375650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are supernatural splats effected by sybaris?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T17:08:10-07:00","id":1376449,"title":"","content":"What happens if a mummy is called into a new body in the future that has extensive cybernetic implants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-03-24T18:53:30-07:00","id":1376464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exthalion</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1376449#post1376449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens if a mummy is called into a new body in the future that has extensive cybernetic implants?</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally, I\u2019d let them have a body with cybernetic implants, up until they were damaged. Once it was broken, the sahu would heal it back to a \u201cnormal\u201d limb. Really, it\u2019s whatever you\u2019d need for your table, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T03:43:59-07:00","id":1384819,"title":"","content":"1) In 1st edition, frequent evocations by cults cause side effects to an Arisen's memory. In the second edition is the same?<br /> <br /> 2) Also, in the 1st edition, a fresh awakened Arisen is a walking mummy until she don't lose some sekhem. How it works in the second edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2457,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","user":"Ipergigio","date":". 04-30-2020, 06:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-18T20:49:01-07:00","id":1389834,"title":"","content":"Dumb question but I can't find an explicit answer as I look over the 2e manuscript: Supernatural beings aren't explicitly exempted from Sybaris as far as I can find, but I recall in 1e they were. Does that still hold true and I'm just missing a line? Or now do vampires and mages and changelings need to be concerned with the fear sickness around Arisen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12596-alpharius","name":"Alpharius","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12596_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-19T03:17:37-07:00","id":1389907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alpharius</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1389834#post1389834\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dumb question but I can't find an explicit answer as I look over the 2e manuscript: Supernatural beings aren't explicitly exempted from Sybaris as far as I can find, but I recall in 1e they were. Does that still hold true and I'm just missing a line? Or now do vampires and mages and changelings need to be concerned with the fear sickness around Arisen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Subtle Utterances only impose Sybaris on supernatural beings (i.e. those with a Supernatural Resistance trait), implying that Sybaris generally affects everyone who aren't explicitly immune.<br /> Similarly, Beast Companion specifically mentions the animal companion as being immune to Sybaris, implying animals also generally suffers from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-14T09:21:22-07:00","id":1396407,"title":"","content":"What happens to bound Seba when a Mummy dies with them attached, and they're not Keshina?<br /> <br /> In 1e, I should add.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-15T17:02:34-07:00","id":1396752,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1396407#post1396407\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to bound Seba when a Mummy dies with them attached, and they're not Keshina?<br /> <br /> In 1e, I should add.</div> </div> </div> </div>They become manifest at the site of the death for a scene then all become unbound according to their normal schedule. (See Book of the Deceived p. 108 section Extraction)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1144-exthalion","name":"Exthalion","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1144_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-03T13:05:32-07:00","id":1416638,"title":"","content":"So I just randomly got back into Mummy the Curse, mostly through the lens of the immortals and from them the Reborn, and I had a question. The Resplendent Soul merit can be taken by an immortal with Sekhem 3. It gives them a Pillar. It says they can do all the things the Arisen can do with Pillars. <br /> <br /> This means Physical Attribute Boost, Seal the Flesh, Vessels, and Utterances. It also technically means Favored Attribute Boost and Corpse Form but immortals don't have either so whatever (hehe). <br /> <br /> But the thing that gets me is Utterances. They can activate an Utterance. Buuuut can they purchase an Utterance? If not how do they activate something they don't have. <br /> <br /> I really like the idea of a supremely potent Reborn having access to some Utterances. I think that is like woah nifty. <br /> <br /> (I plan on removing the limit of only one version of Resplendent Soul as I want to enable a Reborn player, if interested, and through the normal expenditure of experience as a cost, to be able to get all five Pillars.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T07:49:51-07:00","id":1416726,"title":"","content":"I would treat as an Arisen who donated a pillar to them. Just pick the Utterance from the ether instead of the Arisen's collection.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-10-04T08:29:10-07:00","id":1416730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1416726#post1416726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would treat as an Arisen who donated a pillar to them. Just pick the Utterance from the ether instead of the Arisen's collection.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey thanks for this. Your idea is totally supported by the book, hehe. (I searched invested, totally should have done that before so my bad.)<br /> <br /> But yeah basically, immortals that have a Pillar (be it from investment or resplendent soul) get access to Tier 1 Utterances. <br /> <br /> So I was thinking that maybe the Pillar an immortal first chooses could be described as their Defining Pillar for rules purposes. I have to think on whether the benefit is worth it. <br /> <br /> I do think maybe there is the potential to allow for an immortal merit that would let them purchase Soul Affinities, like Sadikh can.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T06:06:30-08:00","id":1429614,"title":"","content":"<i>The Pack</i> mentions a rumor about certain mummies being unable to enter the Shadow. Is that a direct reference to something? I know the Arisen only have limited access to the Underworld, but I can't recall any mention of their potential interactions with the <i>Hisil</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-23T07:41:41-08:00","id":1429624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1429614#post1429614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>The Pack</i> mentions a rumor about certain mummies being unable to enter the Shadow. Is that a direct reference to something? I know the Arisen only have limited access to the Underworld, but I can't recall any mention of their potential interactions with the <i>Hisil</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Deceived cannot be transported, body or soul, to any other dimension than the material one, Neter-Khertet notwithstanding, as part of their being barred from Duat and anchored to the sunlit lands. (Book of the Deceived, p.43)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T11:13:32-08:00","id":1434502,"title":"","content":"I might be cheating cuz it's not a single question, so no obligation to answer them, but i've got these questions:<br /> <br /> -What is the purpose of the Arisen? I mean, serving their Judges yes. But is there a general goal they usually have beyond recovering their memory?<br /> <br /> -What would you consider the biggest differences between the Arisen from The Curse and the Undying from The Resurrection?<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, I would like to thank the people that put their efforts in answering the questions from folk here, you people rock!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T11:30:00-08:00","id":1434507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1434502#post1434502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-What is the purpose of the Arisen? I mean, serving their Judges yes. But is there a general goal they usually have beyond recovering their memory?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gathering relics, mostly, with a side of maintaining cults that carry on Irem's legacy in civilization.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-04T13:06:03-08:00","id":1434519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1434502#post1434502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-What is the purpose of the Arisen? I mean, serving their Judges yes. But is there a general goal they usually have beyond recovering their memory?</div> </div> </div> </div>The directives baked into the Rite of Return instinctively draw the Arisen to retrieve vessels of Sekhem and offer them to the Duat. This is the fundamental quest from which most action flows, and it is the root of their eternal slavery. Beyond this, each Judge charges its Arisen servants to seek out particular sins and punish them, each Guild shares its own philosophy of what is the best means of upholding the glory inherited from the Nameless Empire, and a heretical mummy could always choose to turn her back on the Judges of Life and Death to pursue a personal apotheosis and escape their eternal Curse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1434502#post1434502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">-What would you consider the biggest differences between the Arisen from The Curse and the Undying from The Resurrection?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Undying, unlike the Arisen, are principally modern souls mended by their union with the vestiges of ancient spirits.<br /> <br /> The Arisen, unlike the Undying, are evil.*<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:9px\">* Deliberately hyperbolic, but with an underlying truth.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T17:58:59-08:00","id":1434653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1434502#post1434502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> -What is the purpose of the Arisen? I mean, serving their Judges yes. But is there a general goal they usually have beyond recovering their memory?<br /> <br /> -What would you consider the biggest differences between the Arisen from The Curse and the Undying from The Resurrection?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>1. Somewhat. Recovering vessels of Sekhem has been mentioned, as has hunting to remember who they were. A big third one would be killing entities like Amkhata and Shuankhsen that directly hunt the Arisen. Some like to manipulate the construction of their cities to promote the flow of Sekhem according to the designs of Pre-Egyptian architecture, since such things often yield power when correctly aligned. Others promote the crafts of their Guilds, generally encouraging the building of relics under assumption that the more monkeys with typewriters the greater the odds someone will get it right. Some punish the sins sacred to their Judges. And others interact with the affairs of immortals and Lifeless creatures like Ghosts, craving allies and enemies that can reliably last from one awakening into the next. Guilds also have their own agendas...one of which is TO TAKE OVER THE WORLD! Sort of, anyway.<br /> <br /> 2. Too many to name. It reminds me of Changeling: The Lost...a game that takes many of the setting ideas from its previous incarnation and then goes in hard and dark on revisioning the setting. Resurrection was a game about finding some hope, salvation and forgiveness after a life of vice and failure. The Curse is about suffering through the servitude of cruel, lovecraftian gods that have chosen you to be their middle managers for all eternity. I think it is in the end superior to Resurrection, even though I miss a lot the themes of Hope in the original game (also, non-egyptiant mummies). Really, while it takes inspiration from Resurrection this game is more a spiritual successor to the 2nd edition of Mummy in the old world of Darkness. It takes a lot of themes of being burdened by history and memory loss and refines them, with in my opinion a much better society than any of the Mummy games in the OWOD provided. But its definitely darker in tone by a mile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-05T21:59:53-08:00","id":1434667,"title":"","content":"!!Thanks!!<br /> @<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel\">Satchel</a></b><br /> @<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman\">Stupid Loserman</a></b><br /> @<b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri\">nothri</a></b><br /> <br /> It helped a lot to understand them more, and while reading Resurrection I can see some good differences and ways to reach a common point. Cuz what I'm doing is studying some Chronicles of Darkness lines and the WoD ones and combining and picking up the ones I most like to make my own world of dakness (well, with the chronicles i've already ran there already is, but since some supernatural races haven't been mentioned or appeared I still can change them). And the Mummy game was the one with the most refined differences from the ones I meshed together, but now with your help I'm getting them down. And yeah, Resurrection really has some good vibes comparatively with others WoD games, but it doesn't lose the world of darkness edge either. <br /> Also, mummies not only from Egypt is a real good bonus from Mummy Res. even if one could say the Nameless Empire isn't Egypt. I really like to find out there were the other ones.<br /> <br /> Funny how Mummy Res. always had this Werewolf of the undead feel, except with more agency. The Curse has a bit of a Technocracy vibe to it, which is cool, and I like the tones of it a bit better. And I think Hope can be made part of it, as if the Arisen made it their job in a way that they could make the world better instead of just as the Judges wish. Like the steward of the wanton king who feed and donate to the poor with the remains and excess of the castle. Of course, there is always the danger, but there is always hope (like the way the Technocracy played out in my games according to my players).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Strange... When coincidence seems too convenient, I prefer to call it fate.</i><br /> <br /> <b><sup>-Blood Omen: Legacy of Kain</sup> </b>d=","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25534-banu_saulot","name":"Banu_Saulot","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25534_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-02-07T12:05:27-08:00","id":1434771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Banu_Saulot</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1434667#post1434667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">!!Thanks!!<br /> @<b><a href=\"http://&quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Satchel</a></b><br /> @<b><a href=\"http://&quot;&#91;url\" target=\"_blank\">http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman&quot;]Stupid</a> Loserman[/URL]</b><br /> @<b><a href=\"http://&quot;http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">nothri</a></b><br /> <br /> It helped a lot to understand them more, and while reading Resurrection I can see some good differences and ways to reach a common point. Cuz what I'm doing is studying some Chronicles of Darkness lines and the WoD ones and combining and picking up the ones I most like to make my own world of dakness (well, with the chronicles i've already ran there already is, but since some supernatural races haven't been mentioned or appeared I still can change them). And the Mummy game was the one with the most refined differences from the ones I meshed together, but now with your help I'm getting them down. And yeah, Resurrection really has some good vibes comparatively with others WoD games, but it doesn't lose the world of darkness edge either. <br /> Also, mummies not only from Egypt is a real good bonus from Mummy Res. even if one could say the Nameless Empire isn't Egypt. I really like to find out there were the other ones.<br /> <br /> Funny how Mummy Res. always had this Werewolf of the undead feel, except with more agency. The Curse has a bit of a Technocracy vibe to it, which is cool, and I like the tones of it a bit better. And I think Hope can be made part of it, as if the Arisen made it their job in a way that they could make the world better instead of just as the Judges wish. Like the steward of the wanton king who feed and donate to the poor with the remains and excess of the castle. Of course, there is always the danger, but there is always hope (like the way the Technocracy played out in my games according to my players).</div> </div> </div> </div>There are ways to get a lot of inspiration from M:tR into the Curse, if you look into it. For example, while Geist seems much more to be a spiritual successor of Ressurection, MtR isn't entirely absent. For example, in MtC 1e there was a MICH stronger leaning towards Iremite mummies being a vast majority,while in 2e they outright say in the book that much fewer mummies still have their original bodies intact from Irem. Because of memory bleed and memory in general, I take that to mean that many mummies are indeed an MtR style combination of Old and New. Even the sample character creation is a mummy who took over the life of a Chinese detective, and that the memories it harbors are a mix of the new host and the old soul. While MtC doesn't share the open mindedness if the actual ORIGIN point of Mummies, 2e goes out of its way to address mummies from south America, China, bog mummies, and even a lovecraftian lost city in Antarctica. In the days of 1e I made a post about various mummies that are no longer &quot;Egyptian&quot;, or never even were exactly. <br /> <br /> As for Hope, that still exists, though still viewed through CoDs darker angles of things. In 1e, I played a mummy bereft of hope that had given up by 1999, attempted to destroy himself, was tormented by his memories, and was stripped of his high rank in his guild. 2e made Timelessness an interesting twist, with him Ascending in 1912 and his closest memories being of his degraded state in 1999. Now, he holds onto hope that he can find enough memory to both escape his plight AND help all of humanity become &quot;good enough&quot; for A'aru. <br /> <br /> Hope is very strongly tied to Memory, as is regret. While in 1999 he wanted to forget everything, his next life in 1912 gives him the hope that he CAN avoid his fate, that if the Shaniatu did something terrible to him, that maybe he can undo it, if he finds a way to be true to both himself and his Gods. <br /> <br /> Either way, the Curse still holds true to the idea that your current self can be better than who you used to be. That Heaven IS real, even if it's painfully hard to get to. Touchstones and Memory help anchor you to that hope even as the Judges do their job at.. well, judging everyone as not being good enough. You made a Decree, you ARE good enough. You don't get to go to A'aru but you've got an eternity to find out how to do so. As bad as this Descent was, or as found wanting you've been every time before that, maybe THIS lifetime or the next will be the one when no Judge finds you wanting, or Azar or Sutekh lifts their dead hand to silence the Judges, smiles,and allows you to finally move on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":935,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","user":"Cleverest of Things","date":". 02-07-2021, 03:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T18:35:32-07:00","id":1441178,"title":"","content":"So, I'm a little unsure of what's meant to happen with the Rite of Investment. Is the idea that the Mummy gives a Pillar <i>point</i> or a pillar <i>dot</i>? Because the text says points, but they seem very... enduring? In a way that I'm a little surprised is the case if they're 'just' supernatural fuel. Just looking for a little clarification.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-23T20:01:05-07:00","id":1441187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1441178#post1441178\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I'm a little unsure of what's meant to happen with the Rite of Investment. Is the idea that the Mummy gives a Pillar <i>point</i> or a pillar <i>dot</i>? Because the text says points, but they seem very... enduring? In a way that I'm a little surprised is the case if they're 'just' supernatural fuel. Just looking for a little clarification.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's points. They're reclaimable in a way that Vitae and Satiety aren't, but the principle of &quot;invest soul-stuff in a person for later returns&quot; is roughly equivalent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-01T19:05:31-07:00","id":1462379,"title":"","content":"Can a mummy gain Reminisce Beats from their Touchstones fulfilling their cults' Virtues and Vices?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T14:53:02-07:00","id":1462933,"title":"","content":"Are there mechanics for Apotheosis as described in the back of the core book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T15:09:48-07:00","id":1462934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1462933#post1462933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there mechanics for Apotheosis as described in the back of the core book?</div> </div> </div> </div>That should be the 'Escaping the Cycle' sidebar, though the mechanics are a bit flat in my opinion. MtC 1e core, pages 172-174 has some more detailed mechanics which you should be able to use more or less wholesale, or with relatively minimal adaptation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T15:14:58-07:00","id":1462935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1462934#post1462934\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That should be the 'Escaping the Cycle' sidebar, though the mechanics are a bit flat in my opinion. MtC 1e core, pages 172-174 has some more detailed mechanics which you should be able to use more or less wholesale, or with relatively minimal adaptation.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The lacklustre sidebar is exactly why I asked! I'm aware of some of the 1e mechanics to them, but I heard that things might have been changed in 2e, such as regaining Sekhem after Apotheosis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26024-distant-choir","name":"Distant Choir","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26024_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T16:50:30-07:00","id":1462942,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Distant Choir</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1462935#post1462935\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The lacklustre sidebar is exactly why I asked! I'm aware of some of the 1e mechanics to them, but I heard that things might have been changed in 2e, such as regaining Sekhem after Apotheosis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know about official mechanics, but my approach to the thing is that Apotheosized mummies arise at Sekhem 1, but don't naturally fall below 1 (though it can be stolen from them, they can sacrifice it and so on). Because they're not bound to the Judges anymore, they're exempt from the causes of Descent rolls which are manifestations of the Judges' displeasure.<br /> <br /> Apart from that, they use their Memory rating for Supernatural Tolerance (e.g. for resisting other powers, in Clash of Wills), though Sekhem is still used to determine what Utterances they can cast, become capable of performing mortal sorcery (notably including Vestige- and Relic-making), and can raise their Sekhem temporarily through the normal means (draining Relics etc) - but obviously, getting high Sekhem is something of an uphill battle for them, and naturally tends to draw enemies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":10397,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","user":"ajf115","date":". 10-06-2021, 08:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T16:56:03-07:00","id":1462943,"title":"","content":"A question of my own: For the purpose of 'mortals only' magic like most Supernatural Merits, do Sadikh count as mortals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-06T17:42:10-07:00","id":1462946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1462943#post1462943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A question of my own: For the purpose of 'mortals only' magic like most Supernatural Merits, do Sadikh count as mortals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d say no. They\u2019re <i>immortal</i> AND undead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T20:09:17-08:00","id":1472221,"title":"","content":"Less of a mechanics question and more a probe into the aggregate headspace:<br /> <br /> The nature of their affinity relics makes it easy to say the sorts of archetypal places that you could use to describe the tombs of Sesha-Hebsu and Su-Menent mummies (libraries/archives and mausolea/literal tombs, respectively); the Tef-Aabhi role as architects likewise it easy to see a certain category of building or monolith housing their bodies in repose. The Mesen-Nebu that lives in your head can probably be put to rest in some sort of bank or company building, largely because their general shtick lends itself well to Enterprise-type cults, and the Maa-Kep have the same thing going on with Conspiracy-type cults\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026but I'm having trouble identifying what &quot;a building associated with conspiracy&quot; is in general terms, and the alternatives that spring to mind are basically just bureaucratic offices and The Halls Of Power\u2122, which kind of blend into the other four guilds' headspace except with extra badges and seals around. This might be the point, but I figured I'd put it to the forums:<br /> <br /> How would you describe the quintessential Maa-Kep Tomb, as a structure summed up in a small handful of words?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T20:28:12-08:00","id":1472222,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1472221#post1472221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How would you describe the quintessential Maa-Kep Tomb, as a structure summed up in a small handful of words?</div> </div> </div> </div>Understated but dignified, like something designed by Iremite Martha Stewart. Spaces to place interchangeable symbols and accents depending on the mummy's current loyalties. Locations connected to the Deep State.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-10T23:10:35-08:00","id":1472225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1472221#post1472221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Less of a mechanics question and more a probe into the aggregate headspace:<br /> <br /> The nature of their affinity relics makes it easy to say the sorts of archetypal places that you could use to describe the tombs of Sesha-Hebsu and Su-Menent mummies (libraries/archives and mausolea/literal tombs, respectively); the Tef-Aabhi role as architects likewise it easy to see a certain category of building or monolith housing their bodies in repose. The Mesen-Nebu that lives in your head can probably be put to rest in some sort of bank or company building, largely because their general shtick lends itself well to Enterprise-type cults, and the Maa-Kep have the same thing going on with Conspiracy-type cults\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026but I'm having trouble identifying what &quot;a building associated with conspiracy&quot; is in general terms, and the alternatives that spring to mind are basically just bureaucratic offices and The Halls Of Power\u2122, which kind of blend into the other four guilds' headspace except with extra badges and seals around. This might be the point, but I figured I'd put it to the forums:<br /> <br /> How would you describe the quintessential Maa-Kep Tomb, as a structure summed up in a small handful of words?</div> </div> </div> </div>Schools. Apartment complexes. Gated communities. (And bureaucratic offices, too, of course)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-11T15:37:03-08:00","id":1472273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1472221#post1472221\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Less of a mechanics question and more a probe into the aggregate headspace:<br /> <br /> The nature of their affinity relics makes it easy to say the sorts of archetypal places that you could use to describe the tombs of Sesha-Hebsu and Su-Menent mummies (libraries/archives and mausolea/literal tombs, respectively); the Tef-Aabhi role as architects likewise it easy to see a certain category of building or monolith housing their bodies in repose. The Mesen-Nebu that lives in your head can probably be put to rest in some sort of bank or company building, largely because their general shtick lends itself well to Enterprise-type cults, and the Maa-Kep have the same thing going on with Conspiracy-type cults\u2026<br /> <br /> \u2026but I'm having trouble identifying what &quot;a building associated with conspiracy&quot; is in general terms, and the alternatives that spring to mind are basically just bureaucratic offices and The Halls Of Power\u2122, which kind of blend into the other four guilds' headspace except with extra badges and seals around. This might be the point, but I figured I'd put it to the forums:<br /> <br /> How would you describe the quintessential Maa-Kep Tomb, as a structure summed up in a small handful of words?</div> </div> </div> </div>Community centers, town halls, military bases, court houses and government buildings; their role as ambassadors might also imply resting beneath old extravagant hotels, restaurants, coffee shops (the sterotypical centers of conspiring revolutionaries), etc. Train stations, bus terminals, airports (or their ancient equivalent, the gates in and out of the city, basically any place that allows a mummy or a cultist to take note of who enters and who leaves a Nome without drawing undue attention); any major hub along an established communication network, from court footmen to postal workers to telegraph/telephone stations into the modern radio towers, TV stations, satellite communication monitoring stations, etc.<br /> <br /> As an aside, I set my game in a city that had a long and tragic history of class conflict and labor clashes. Since Arisen like to shape human history and end up being shaped by history (for example, the ways in which their cults evolve with the times) I assigned a Mesen-Nebu cult to represent the rich and industrial factions of the city while the Maa-Kep represented the poor and the labor unions. It just seemed like the logical choice under the circumstances.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-17T10:06:29-08:00","id":1472620,"title":"","content":"to enhanced phisical attribute the Arisen spending 1 single point Pillar (exemple with sekhem 10, spending 1 single point Pillar and boost Strength to +4, its right?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12210-ulisses","name":"Ulisses","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T05:07:43-08:00","id":1473964,"title":"","content":"In second edition, the apperanc eof the mummy is still affected by its Sekhem ratings, I mean does they still look like an actual mummified corpse at higher Sekhem levels and as Sekhem drops they got progressively more human-like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25516-pinkhaunt","name":"PinkHaunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T15:02:46-08:00","id":1473998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PinkHaunt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1473964#post1473964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In second edition, the apperanc eof the mummy is still affected by its Sekhem ratings, I mean does they still look like an actual mummified corpse at higher Sekhem levels and as Sekhem drops they got progressively more human-like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Second item under &quot;Effects of Sekhem,&quot; on page 159:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Burning Bright</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">At the start of most Descents, mummies begin with Sekhem 10. Time, certain supernatural attacks, death, and disobedience to the Judges erode a mummy\u2019s Sekhem rating until it reaches 0. A mummy at Sekhem 10 and 9 appears as a monstrous mummy, crackling and glowing with power. At Sekhem 8 and 7 this stabilizes and the Arisen appears as a walking, but regal mummified body. By Sekhem 6 and 5, the mummy appears as a walking cadaver dead for between a year and a decade. Only from Sekhem 5 and lower does the mummy easily pass for a healthy human. This is all an illusion maintained over the sahu.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-04T16:41:58-08:00","id":1474010,"title":"","content":"Belatedly found a change in the Final Download version of 2e Core that I'd like to get extra eyes on, since it seems some related sections weren't updated to match it:<br /> <br /> Rather than reiterating the contents of the Death Cycles section from page 319, the section on Death and Resurrection on page 165 now says that mummies that return to life must roll their highest Pillar rating and gain dots of Memory up to a maximum of 3. The section on Memory on page 160 still says that a mummy who returns to life from Memory 0 is restored to a rating of 1 (which is admittedly still the most likely result for most characters rolling their highest Pillar rating, particularly if the -1 from failing the initial Memory roll from the Death Cycle still applies); the Death Cycles section still describes it as &quot;roll Memory to find Anpu, then roll Memory again to resurrect and see how much Sekhem you lose from doing so.&quot;<br /> <br /> Given that this is the only new element out of the three, it seems reasonable to conclude that that's the one that's supposed to be there, particularly given that losing up to two dots of Sekhem at the end of a Death Cycle based on a roll that low Memory penalizes twice is effectively a death spiral that you can't remedy for the rest of your Descent if coming back from Memory 0 only gives you Memory 1 \u2014 the process basically becomes an elaborate prelude to henet at low Sekhem at that point.<br /> <br /> That said, is the following takeaway solid?<br /> <br /> \u2022 When a mummy dies with more than one dot of Sekhem, they enter a death cycle, wherein they must navigate their memories to find Anpu, rolling Memory to determine how well they manage.<br /> \u2022 Once the mummy has reached the akhet leading to their body, they roll their highest Pillar rating modified by the result of the Memory roll, adding their successes to their Memory rating if it is less than 3, to a maximum increased total of 3, though this does not lower the mummy's Memory rating if it is higher than 3.<br /> \u2022 The mummy then takes an amount of time determined by their Memory rating to resurrect (which, for Memory 3 and below, is instantaneous), at which point all pre-death damage is healed. No Sekhem is mechanically lost in the process, but the Descent timer is still counting down as it always is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T11:05:47-08:00","id":1474810,"title":"","content":"Sorcery questions:<br /> <br /> Do Supernatural Merits that require activation count as Open Rites? Parsed literally, they meet the description of being an \u201caction that a character without a supernatural template can do that causes a supernatural effect\u201d. But I\u2019m not positive that\u2019s the intention, seeing as all the example Open Rites are things that that don\u2019t have to be purchased with dots. <br /> <br /> Similarly, I\u2019ve seen it intimated that Ceremonies from Geist could be considered Open Rites. It seems to line up in that theoretically any mortal can perform a Ceremony, but, again, they have dot ratings and have to be purchased to use.<br /> <br /> Each type of mortal interaction with Ephemeral entities is considered a separate Open Rite, including Summoning. This makes it sound like if you Master Summoning, it applies to anything and everything you might try to summon\u2026except akathartoi, which are called out as having a separate rite for each individual fiend. It feels a little weird how broad this makes generic Summoning in comparison. Am I reading this right?<br /> <br /> And a metaphysics question that may be less than simple: by my reading, Sorcery isn\u2019t really a unified system with a particular metaphysical origin (as compared to, say, Obcasus Rites), and as such it isn\u2019t really derived from or dependent on the Arisen, The Judges, Sekhem, whatever. Rather, a particular Rite is just a way of pulling on the lose threads of reality, taking advantage of specific loopholes in the inherently spooky nature of the setting, and may or may not interact with other supernatural ecosystems (kinda like Occult Matrixes come to think of it). It just so happens that Sekhem/Pillars is a particularly good \u201cfuel\u201d for expediting the use of these loopholes, hence why Sorcerers and Arisen tend to cross paths so often (and also a lot of sorcerous knowledge originates with Iremite culture). Does that sound about right? <br /> <br /> And, while I\u2019m here, any ideas what Sekhem and/or Pillar points look like to Mage Sight? The Player\u2019s Guide to the Contagion only refers to the Mummy Core, which itself only covers using Fate and Time on Arisen directly. I\u2019m particularly interested in how Pillars relate to the Awakened understanding of the soul. Inquiring Tremere want to know. \ud83d\ude00","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-16T19:47:03-08:00","id":1474833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1474810#post1474810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each type of mortal interaction with Ephemeral entities is considered a separate Open Rite, including Summoning. This makes it sound like if you Master Summoning, it applies to anything and everything you might try to summon\u2026except akathartoi, which are called out as having a separate rite for each individual fiend. It feels a little weird how broad this makes generic Summoning in comparison. Am I reading this right?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. &quot;Summoning&quot; an ephemeral being, per the section of Chronicles Core cited in that part of Mummy 2e, creates a Manifestation Condition capable of supporting a given ephemeral being, but\u2026<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For a solitary occultist attempting to force a ghost to appear, or a shaman inviting a spirit to Influence an area, <b>occult libraries are filled with summoning rites. None of them, strictly speaking, actually work,</b> in that without supernatural power it\u2019s impossible to compel an ephemeral entity to appear, but <b>the rituals and practices of a summoning can often, by accident or design, create the Conditions an entity would need to appear if it were so inclined.</b> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And a metaphysics question that may be less than simple: by my reading, Sorcery isn\u2019t really a unified system with a particular metaphysical origin (as compared to, say, Obcasus Rites), and as such it isn\u2019t really derived from or dependent on the Arisen, The Judges, Sekhem, whatever. Rather, a particular Rite is just a way of pulling on the lose threads of reality, taking advantage of specific loopholes in the inherently spooky nature of the setting, and may or may not interact with other supernatural ecosystems (kinda like Occult Matrixes come to think of it). It just so happens that Sekhem/Pillars is a particularly good \u201cfuel\u201d for expediting the use of these loopholes, hence why Sorcerers and Arisen tend to cross paths so often (and also a lot of sorcerous knowledge originates with Iremite culture). Does that sound about right?<br /> <br /> And, while I\u2019m here, any ideas what Sekhem and/or Pillar points look like to Mage Sight? The Player\u2019s Guide to the Contagion only refers to the Mummy Core, which itself only covers using Fate and Time on Arisen directly. I\u2019m particularly interested in how Pillars relate to the Awakened understanding of the soul. Inquiring Tremere want to know. \ud83d\ude00 </div> </div> </div>Sekhem is the stuff of existence as it manifests, differentiating into the Pillars as it goes.<br /> <br /> The Pillars are the powers that correspond to the same parts of the soul as Mage aligns paired Subtle and Gross Arcana to the Paths by, such that Arisen can use their Pillars to substitute for Arcana ratings when operating certain magical objects (see &quot;Crossover in the Conquered Land&quot; in the Dark Eras Companion, pages 137-138), so that's a hard &quot;yes&quot; for &quot;Sekhem and its divided Pillars are useful extra/alternative components for ritual magic that's just part of the way the world works.&quot;<br /> <br /> Occult matrices exploit similar quirks in reality's arrangement and so do Ceremonies, to the point where the Demon Storyteller's Guide suggests the Underworld's Old Laws somehow operate on inverted occult physics. Geist 2e's sidebar on where the power of Ceremonies comes from points to the same class of activities that Mummy does as examples of Ceremonies that have become such common knowledge that they functionally don't have dot ratings anymore; while Ceremonies have dot ratings and &quot;have to be purchased to be used,&quot; one of the main benefits of belonging to a Krewe is that you know how to use every Ceremony the Krewe knows whose dot rating is less than or equal to your Mystery Cult Initiation rating, which isn't much more of an investment of experience than buying Sorcery Merits and Occult dots to become a sorcerer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-21T15:36:31-08:00","id":1475156,"title":"","content":"&quot;Do Supernatural Merits that require activation count as Open Rites? Parsed literally, they meet the description of being an \u201caction that a character without a supernatural template can do that causes a supernatural effect\u201d. But I\u2019m not positive that\u2019s the intention, seeing as all the example Open Rites are things that that don\u2019t have to be purchased with dots.&quot;<br /> <br /> So this is less a rules mechanics answer and more of a suggestion. Sothis Ascends has this to say about Sorcery in the time of the first Sothic Turn, which was more or less the first reappearance of the Arisen since Irem vanished:<br /> <br /> Kemetic magic<br /> does not depend on weaving spells out of will and<br /> imagination, however. Spells are carefully crafted<br /> rituals performed to exacting standards. They draw<br /> upon gods, secret names, and metaphysical principles<br /> to either accomplish a single, mighty feat or craft<br /> a relic. Most mortal magicians perform one or two<br /> effective rituals after a lifetime of study, though many<br /> develop passive abilities, such as the abilities to sense<br /> Sekhem and perceive the dead. With always-opened<br /> eyes, they see past the veil of life. This leaves most of<br /> them more than a little unhinged.<br /> <br /> Based on this statement I would allow the following in my games. There are Open Rites per the Sorcery rules that open up the mind and soul of the one performing the ritual. The Rite itself doesn't do anything mechanically EXCEPT allows someone potentially to buy merits that would otherwise only be available at character creation. He still has to pay the cost for the supernatural merit, but as long as the merit is not restricted to a particular type of entity (werewolf, vampire, etc) I would allow them to develop the merit as one example of a &quot;passive ability&quot; spoken of above. For both the power and horror such a thing will no doubt cause in the sorcerer's life.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-12T19:10:53-07:00","id":1478727,"title":"","content":"A couple of questions I'm not entirely clear on:<br /> <br /> Do mummies have to be awakened in their tomb or in an emergency can a cult awaken them somewhere else? As long as they have an inheritor, and some vessels could they summon the mummy in a Walmart parking lot?<br /> <br /> If the mummy is risen in an inheritor or canoptic jar while his sahu still exists, can he be called back to his original sahu on his next descent?<br /> <br /> Can a mummy have multiple tombs with multiple sahu prepared for him?<br /> <br /> Does a mummy retain his memory rating at the end of henet, unlike a death-cycle resurrection?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-04-23T12:42:09-07:00","id":1479362,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jeremysbrain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1478727#post1478727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A couple of questions I'm not entirely clear on:<br /> <br /> Do mummies have to be awakened in their tomb or in an emergency can a cult awaken them somewhere else? As long as they have an inheritor, and some vessels could they summon the mummy in a Walmart parking lot?<br /> <br /> If the mummy is risen in an inheritor or canoptic jar while his sahu still exists, can he be called back to his original sahu on his next descent?<br /> <br /> Can a mummy have multiple tombs with multiple sahu prepared for him?<br /> <br /> Does a mummy retain his memory rating at the end of henet, unlike a death-cycle resurrection?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They can awaken from their corpse, from one of the four canopic jars containing one of their body organs, from a Talisman they created, or within the body of an individual invested with one of their pillars. It's easier to do in the tomb, but it will happen depending on which of the above is present at the Call.<br /> <br /> His sahu, if it has not previously been destroyed, would theoretically still exist, but the implication for rising in an inheritor is that the inheritor's body becomes the new sahu, rather than an additional one. I don't know that I've seen anything saying either way directly.<br /> <br /> There can be multiple tombs, and you can store the sahu, talisman, and canopic jars in one tomb, multiple tombs, or not in tombs at all. <br /> <br /> Memory is generally retained if you die and resurrect in the middle of a Descent. At the start of a Descent, what happens to your memory is determined in large part by what happens during the Arisen's experience in Duat. There are systems in place to determine the outcome, but it is partially up to the storyteller what benefits, or penalties, result from their experiences.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2096-willywonka","name":"willywonka","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"45"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T14:35:38-07:00","id":1482663,"title":"","content":"Has there somewhere been a write-up or reference to a type of Immortal that prolongs their life by consuming Sekhem from relics? It seems like a really obvious idea, and I\u2019m wondering if I\u2019m remembering it from somewhere, or if I should write it up myself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">The longer I study science the more I am convinced that it is <span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\">functionally indistinguishable from what our ancestors would refer to as sorcery</span>. And I would know, being both scientist and sorcerer.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23730-scriptorian","name":"Scriptorian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23730_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-01T15:14:33-07:00","id":1482668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Scriptorian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1482663#post1482663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has there somewhere been a write-up or reference to a type of Immortal that prolongs their life by consuming Sekhem from relics? It seems like a really obvious idea, and I\u2019m wondering if I\u2019m remembering it from somewhere, or if I should write it up myself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Other than the Arisen themselves, I don\u2019t think so.<br /> <br /> Some combination of an Eternal and a Body Snatcher, perhaps?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-02T10:20:07-07:00","id":1482788,"title":"","content":"At one point, LostLight posted homebrew he wrote about <i>Aegis Kai Doru</i>. It's inspired by both <i>Mummy</i> and <i>Hunter</i>. It's a hefty collection containing <i>Daktyloi</i>, who are essentially what you're asking about, but also <i>Pharmakoi</i> and <i>Hem Khet</i>, who interact with Relics in a different manner.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/1459681-into-the-labyrinth-akd-expansion-fanbook\">Into the Labyrinth - AKD Expansion Fanbook</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T10:18:09-07:00","id":1483152,"title":"","content":"How are there still relics from the Nameless Empire after (roughly) 8,000 years?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T14:59:27-07:00","id":1483177,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1483152#post1483152\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are there still relics from the Nameless Empire after (roughly) 8,000 years?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, 1) We can find normal human artifacts that are that old here in the real world. And 2) Relics are supernaturally durable in addition to their other magical properties, so there is a better than average chance they would survive to the modern era.<br /> <br /> Has this question been answered?- How does a cultist survive long enough to enter a mummy's tomb and perform the Call over their body when entering the mummy's tomb is supposed to trigger the monster to animate and kill the invader the moment they enter?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T16:26:11-07:00","id":1483184,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised any artifacts from Egypt are still being discovered in the real world, frankly.<br /> <br /> I'm asking about Irem because, afaik, Egyptian artifacts aren't being targeted by actual Mummies, cults of Mummies, and enemies of Mummies like the Lifeless or the Deceived.<br /> <br /> Not to mention nosy Mages, elder Vampires, or Prometheans...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-05T18:50:44-07:00","id":1483199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1483177#post1483177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has this question been answered?- How does a cultist survive long enough to enter a mummy's tomb and perform the Call over their body when entering the mummy's tomb is supposed to trigger the monster to animate and kill the invader the moment they enter?</div> </div> </div> </div>Entering a mummy's Tomb is a Sybaris trigger, which cultists are immune to; waking from a disturbed tomb is not guaranteed; the section on the Sarcophagus Text specifies that sometimes the cult simply <i>doesn't</i> survive the entry; and most of the text around waking from disturbance involves tomb robbers and/or the contents of the tomb actually being disturbed.<br /> <br /> Also, you can perform the Call without being in the mummy's Tomb \u2014 there's a not-insubtantial bonus for doing it there, but you don't need to play with fire to quite that degree to wake up a mummy whose cult you belong to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-30T07:29:07-07:00","id":1485371,"title":"","content":"Can a Arisen invest pillars into a supernatural splat?<br /> <br /> Where would a supernatural splat fall on the list if they were able.to become inheritors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8177-heroofthemists","name":"Heroofthemists","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-01T09:35:40-07:00","id":1485513,"title":"","content":"It took me a while to find it, but I have a partial answer to your question. On the 84th page of the Corebook, it is stated that Vampires and Abmortals are treated as Immortals for the purpose of Investment. This means they can carry up to four Pillars. The Halifax setting has a Hollow Mekhet Inheritor as a notable character, described on page 295. Page 84 also implies that all major templates can be Invested, but doesn't clarify at which level, and also suggests that Pillars may interact with them in unpredictable ways.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T12:22:54-07:00","id":1487928,"title":"","content":"Is Shezmu a fiend? Or something else entirely. Indeed, the Duat section of the corebook mentions gods other than the Judges living there, but that they have no interest in the Arisen. What would you count these things as? Fiends? Inactive Judges?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T21:22:06-07:00","id":1487972,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1487928#post1487928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Shezmu a fiend? Or something else entirely. Indeed, the Duat section of the corebook mentions gods other than the Judges living there, but that they have no interest in the Arisen. What would you count these things as? Fiends? Inactive Judges?</div> </div> </div> </div>Stuff that's not coming outside in any context where that matters.<br /> <br /> The only thing out of Mummy's cosmology from that neck of the woods that isn't in an established mechanical category answers &quot;is this a Supernal god, a demon, a creature of death, or something else?&quot; with &quot;Yes,&quot; and there's precious little reason to expect things that aren't Anpu to read any differently if they ever showed up above the topmost layer of Duat.<br /> <br /> The gods aren't fiends or Judges, they're gods. They're plot devices mechanically and their own thing narratively. What they do is make the world work the way it does (and occasionally the way it's not supposed to, when Sutek's place in their makeup asserts itself) and produce phenomena more relevant to the story than themselves.<br /> <br /> They're metaphors. This is very much a &quot;Supernal beings don't usually appear in the world when they haven't had bodies fashioned for them by magic or occult confluence&quot; sort of thing mixed with a &quot;beings of godlike power tend to need circumstances that take entire stories to prepare to bring them out of their home dimensions.&quot; Ostensibly Shezmu being The Wine-Press Of The Gods means those of them who aren't Anpu or Re are just getting drunk on human suffering, and if they want to poke the twitching carcass they express themselves more subtly through the things they are.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T07:31:53-07:00","id":1488020,"title":"","content":"Thanks, Satchel!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T16:24:32-07:00","id":1488109,"title":"","content":"That being said, I say feel free to treat any given Nameless God you feel inspired by from Egyptian Mythology as a Judge if you need to assign any powers or stats for any reason. There is a vague reference to the Devourer herself sending a Herald to Ubar during the destruction of that city in Book of the Deceived, open ended but with enough detail to assume she can create avatars on Earth just like the Judges when conditions are right. The lore places the Judges as supreme over most other gods of Egypt, although their relationship and power compared to entities like Anpu, Azar, Sutekh and especially the Devourer is vague and undefined. But in the end none of that matters to the players- the least among the gods could drive a mummy into a death cycle with little trouble so power levels aren't sort of irrelevant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T16:52:29-07:00","id":1488112,"title":"","content":"I just really like the idea of Irem\u2019s non-Judge gods being sinister bodyhorror monsters with an Egyptian overlay. Mummy has a subtle Mythos vibe to it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T06:57:26-07:00","id":1492293,"title":"","content":"How does the Investigation for Learning Utterances interact with the 4 Experience cost on the Quick Reference Sheet? Is it necessary to spend the 4 Experiences before the Investigation begins, or, given the interval of the Investigation, is the Experience cost just for purchasing Utterances with starting Experiences?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-04T15:27:47-07:00","id":1492322,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1492293#post1492293\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does the Investigation for Learning Utterances interact with the 4 Experience cost on the Quick Reference Sheet? Is it necessary to spend the 4 Experiences before the Investigation begins, or, given the interval of the Investigation, is the Experience cost just for purchasing Utterances with starting Experiences?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe the Exp cost is supposed to \u2018seal\u2019 the learned Utterance after the Investigation (in addition to being the price at Character Creation)? Not spending the Exp after learning an Utterance could represent how the mummy now \u2018knows\u2019 it but still doesn\u2019t really \u2018get\u2019 it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T12:38:57-07:00","id":1492382,"title":"","content":"Hello, does anyone know/have a ruling on if Eternals special Relics have abilities beyond keeping the the eternal alive blessing / killing the eternal on death curse? Is there a point to having a 5 dot relic ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24579-jjbooklord42","name":"JJBooklord42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-05T18:42:47-07:00","id":1492406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JJBooklord42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1492382#post1492382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, does anyone know/have a ruling on if Eternals special Relics have abilities beyond keeping the the eternal alive blessing / killing the eternal on death curse? Is there a point to having a 5 dot relic ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that Eternals are very much your Picture Of Dorian Gray-type immortals and their relics are basically constantly doing their jobs with no real reference to the systems for what extra dots do besides the benefits of cannibalizing it, the main advantage of having a more powerful anchor is that it's harder to find through kepher and you can theoretically use it to further amplify an active vestige.<br /> <br /> If the secondary effects of an Eternal relic are relevant, I'd be inclined to draw from the general Power/Curse list unless something more unusual is relevant to the plot, but by and large the nature of the Eternals' immortality and the requirements of their anchors are such that they're a weak point more than a magical artifact unto themselves \u2014 the thing that makes them special is that they've made someone immortal (and maybe capable of reading omens or channeling the dead), with their value as spell components or magical focuses being a secondary concern.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T20:14:58-07:00","id":1496148,"title":"","content":"Are the Visitors\u2019 origins spelt out anywhere? The Book of Lasting Death is purposely vague about their origins, but it feels like it\u2019s a answer buried in one of the books I don\u2019t have. <br /> <br /> When the Book of Lasting Death says that a Visitor is \u201cdrifting helplessly through time\u201d, does that mean linearly through time? Or can they be drawn to different timelines?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T20:47:04-07:00","id":1496150,"title":"","content":"Is there any specific reason that Purified need to abandon their bodies to use Numina and Dread Powers? It wasn't a restriction on them in 1E and they aren't exactly the most insanely powerful things around even with all their powers available. Durable? Yes. Insanely powerful, not by comparison to a lot of what is floating around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11422-maskedone","name":"MaskedOne","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T20:59:36-07:00","id":1496152,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1496148#post1496148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are the Visitors\u2019 origins spelt out anywhere? The Book of Lasting Death is purposely vague about their origins, but it feels like it\u2019s a answer buried in one of the books I don\u2019t have.</div> </div> </div> </div>As with all the immortals given a 2e update in Mummy 2e, they were first introduced in <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/62318/World-of-Darkness-Immortals\" target=\"_blank\">World of Darkness: Immortals</a>. They're the first type of &quot;lesser immortal&quot; covered in that book's fourth chapter; Blood Bathers, Body Thieves, and the Purified each got an entire chapter to themselves, being the most mechanically involved templates of the bunch, whereas the Visitors are sharing pagespace with the Patchwork People, the Reborn, and the Eternals (along with Wardens, who are immortal but bound to a place and age rapidly outside of it, and Harvesters, who steal immortality from other immortals through an attuned ritual weapon whose destruction causes any Harvester who's used that &quot;scythe&quot; and not picked up a replacement to swiftly return to their chronological age).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When the Book of Lasting Death says that a Visitor is \u201cdrifting helplessly through time\u201d, does that mean linearly through time? Or can they be drawn to different timelines? </div> </div> </div>They're weirdo psychic pseudo-spirits who're convinced of the origins they've assimilated from the human zeitgeist, as described in BoLD. The modern batch can ostensibly be traced to the atomic bomb tests at White Sands and other nuclear sites warping local spirits in combination with human fear and imagination to create Visitors, but it's deliberately unclear if that means the specimens showing up during the Fall of Isereion are time-slipping from the future, the Trinity specimens are products of a novel or recurring means of creating or summoning new Visitors, or something stranger yet, because the pompous brainworms think they know exactly what they are even when that information is pulled from pulp magazines and B-movies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-02T21:33:04-07:00","id":1496155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MaskedOne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1496150#post1496150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any specific reason that Purified need to abandon their bodies to use Numina and Dread Powers? It wasn't a restriction on them in 1E and they aren't exactly the most insanely powerful things around even with all their powers available. Durable? Yes. Insanely powerful, not by comparison to a lot of what is floating around.</div> </div> </div> </div>In 1e the list of Numina the Purified could draw from was limited and required a willing teacher who had the power you wanted, whereas in 2e every Purified can make spirits do what they want through Shadow Dominion and the breadth of Numina and Dread Powers includes several that are specifically the product of bodily aspects or modifications \u2014 Dread Powers in Mummy are how Amkhata and Judge avatars manifest a not-insignificant portion of their abilities, and so the Purified's spiritual body needs to be able to facilitate those changes since their physical body can't obviously warp in that fashion. From there, the Disembodied Condition limits a character's ability to affect the material world already. The most overt Numina available in 1e were Blast and Telekinesis, since Speed only worked when you weren't in a material state.<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that having more Essence from Rank than Chi gave them in 1e as well as starting with the ability to summon, materialize, and command spirits and being recontextualized into a game where there's all manner of sources of secondary power, means the Purified don't exactly lack for options if they want to go loud for some reason; they just have reason to go to relics or spirit minions for those options instead of spitting fire while looking like a normal person or being a mage by another name, just like Werewolf 2e's design philosophy for Gifts <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/the-giver-of-gifts-1-werewolf-the-forsaken/\" target=\"_blank\">specifically avoids</a> &quot;Killing You Facets.&quot;<br /> <br /> tl;dr It's a thematic requirement moreso than a game-balance requirement.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-09T11:14:13-08:00","id":1496615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MaskedOne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1496150#post1496150\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any specific reason that Purified need to abandon their bodies to use Numina and Dread Powers? It wasn't a restriction on them in 1E and they aren't exactly the most insanely powerful things around even with all their powers available. Durable? Yes. Insanely powerful, not by comparison to a lot of what is floating around.</div> </div> </div> </div>I imagine it\u2019s because Purification is a substandard form of immortality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T08:42:14-08:00","id":1498308,"title":"","content":"As per the core book:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each type of immortal has a favored Attribute. They gain<br /> a free dot in this Attribute and their first dot of the Endless<br /> Potency Merit for the same Attribute. </div> </div> </div>But I see the sample immortals have different attributes that its category for the Endless Potency merit, has this been fixed in an errata?<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T16:32:33-08:00","id":1499917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1498308#post1498308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As per the core book:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> But I see the sample immortals have different attributes that its category for the Endless Potency merit, has this been fixed in an errata?<br /> <br /> Thanks,</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing here?<br /> <br /> Also, now that there is a second edition book, which content on the Dark Eras (1, 2, and Companion) is 2ed compatible? The Merits? (Interstitial Lives from DE is different from the one of the 2e Core book) The Affinities? Certainly the Utterances do not follow the 2e model.<br /> <br /> Another content that merits review is the crossover with Mage, specifically the artificial Vessels that Mages can create transferring Pillar points to a new object. Do these vestiges get their own Power, Curse, Virtue and Vice?<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T17:40:37-08:00","id":1499919,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1499917#post1499917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing here?<br /> <br /> Also, now that there is a second edition book, which content on the Dark Eras (1, 2, and Companion) is 2ed compatible? The Merits? (Interstitial Lives from DE is different from the one of the 2e Core book) The Affinities? Certainly the Utterances do not follow the 2e model.<br /> <br /> Another content that merits review is the crossover with Mage, specifically the artificial Vessels that Mages can create transferring Pillar points to a new object. Do these vestiges get their own Power, Curse, Virtue and Vice?<br /> <br /> Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dunno about the errata one.<br /> <br /> For compatibility, the only one that I\u2019m sure of is that the Mage-Mummy one is 2e-compatible. Gonna have to look over the rest, but I presume that any of the individual Eras written after Mummy 2e core was out are compatible.<br /> <br /> For mages creating Vestiges, I suspect that by default they\u2019re \u2018simple\u2019 Vestiges that do nothing but hold Pillar points. Adding Reach options and/or Arcana might create true Vestiges. Similar to the Spirit 4 Craft Fetish spell, but more tiered/restricted. (At least, this is how I\u2019d rule it.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait, just checked the \u201cMummy: The Curse products\u201d sticky thread. It seems that Dark Eras 2 is 2e, while DE(1) and DEC are 1e. (Again, minus the Mutapa Empire one in DEC)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 12-16-2022, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-16T18:18:22-08:00","id":1499922,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1499917#post1499917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing here?</div> </div> </div> </div>An exercise in critical thinking:<br /> <br /> You are looking at a copy of the book which is either a PDF copy or a physical Print On Demand copy. You want to know if there has been a further errata of the book you are looking at.<br /> <br /> If it's a Print On Demand copy, you are looking at the final version of the book. There is no further errata.<br /> <br /> If it's a PDF, unless you have changed the name of the file, you can look at the filename to see if it contains some variation on the phrase &quot;Final Download.&quot; If it does, you are looking at the final version of the book. There is no further errata.<br /> <br /> If for some reason this information is not in the filename, you can search the PDF to see if &quot;p.XX&quot; is the only page number reference in the book (searching for &quot;XX&quot; will turn it up fairly quickly). If p.XX shows up in the PDF, you are not looking at the final version of the book, because correcting those to accurate page number references is a part of the final errata pass to such a degree that the errata collection form Onyx Path uses specifies that reports of those will be ignored because they know about them and are going to be fixing them anyway; you can download the final version of the PDF from DriveThruRPG through your Library or the item's page on the website.<br /> <br /> If you have gone through the above checklist and confirmed you are looking at the final version of the book and the discrepancy is still there*, then no, it has not been fixed in an errata, because nobody pointed it out when the book was going through its errata collection phase months and months ago.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">* It is.</span><br /> <br /> This particular facet of the generalized Timeless template was added between the KS draft and the Advance PDF that errata collection was done with \u2014 other changes include the removal of the Gift of Years Merit that was previously a required part of advancing certain parts of a Timeless character's template, which nevertheless was included in the sample characters' statblocks and referenced in the rules for Fasad characters in the Advance PDF and removed in the final version.<br /> <br /> By comparison, yes, it seems to have slipped through the cracks that the sample Timeless characters have an off-type Endless Potency in their Merit list and don't include the one they'd get a starting dot in for free. You will have to make your peace with this and/or use a reading of that statblock that makes sense to you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 12-16-2022, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T03:51:08-08:00","id":1499939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1499922#post1499922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An exercise in critical thinking:</div> </div> </div> </div>What should be added is the fact that OPP doesn't do errata (aside from the final editing pass before physical release). Otherwise, having a physical book, or even a pdf marked &quot;final download&quot; wouldn't preclude the possibility of errata released as a separate document, like how many other publishers do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T15:53:28-08:00","id":1499985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1499919#post1499919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Dunno about the errata one.<br /> <br /> For compatibility, the only one that I\u2019m sure of is that the Mage-Mummy one is 2e-compatible. Gonna have to look over the rest, but I presume that any of the individual Eras written after Mummy 2e core was out are compatible.<br /> <br /> For mages creating Vestiges, I suspect that by default they\u2019re \u2018simple\u2019 Vestiges that do nothing but hold Pillar points. Adding Reach options and/or Arcana might create true Vestiges. Similar to the Spirit 4 Craft Fetish spell, but more tiered/restricted. (At least, this is how I\u2019d rule it.)<br /> <br /> EDIT: Wait, just checked the \u201cMummy: The Curse products\u201d sticky thread. It seems that Dark Eras 2 is 2e, while DE(1) and DEC are 1e. (Again, minus the Mutapa Empire one in DEC)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> <br /> Do you think these simple Vestiges can store more than one type of Pillar points after creation? Let say I use a device that resonates with Ba and Ren, could I store 1 point of each on the new Vestige?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-17T16:42:09-08:00","id":1499989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1499985#post1499985\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thanks for the answer.<br /> <br /> <br /> Do you think these simple Vestiges can store more than one type of Pillar points after creation? Let say I use a device that resonates with Ba and Ren, could I store 1 point of each on the new Vestige?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Without further material, this is entirely homebrew territory\u2026 *I* would say No, but others may say Yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-04T14:32:39-08:00","id":1504383,"title":"","content":"So an odd question. In second edition all immortals, including body thieves, gain a dot or more of Sekhem as part of their template? Does this happen immdiately upon invoking the ritual, and does it apply to the anyone whose mind is swapped (in the event the ritual switches minds rather than simply destroying the psyche of the victim, of course)? I'm especially curious about the results of an oddity mind swap such as the Brown Acid described in WoD: Immortals. I'm picturing a scene in a nightclub where a Shuankhsen gives the tainted substance to party goers and then stands back and waits for the drugged up, newly disoriented from trading minds buffet line manifests to chow down.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T18:09:44-08:00","id":1504519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1504383#post1504383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So an odd question. In second edition all immortals, including body thieves, gain a dot or more of Sekhem as part of their template? Does this happen immdiately upon invoking the ritual, and does it apply to the anyone whose mind is swapped (in the event the ritual switches minds rather than simply destroying the psyche of the victim, of course)? I'm especially curious about the results of an oddity mind swap such as the Brown Acid described in WoD: Immortals. I'm picturing a scene in a nightclub where a Shuankhsen gives the tainted substance to party goers and then stands back and waits for the drugged up, newly disoriented from trading minds buffet line manifests to chow down.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per Mummy 2e, the body abandoned by a Mentally Talented Body Thief almost immediately dies, while Magically Talented Body Thieves' theft is temporary unless they kill their old body or are transferring to a body without a soul, which indicates to me that having your mind swapped doesn't give you the Body Thief template any more than a mage casting a spell to swap your mind with somebody else's would. Oddities in the vein of the Brown Acid or Death.com have their particulars handled at Storyteller discretion; some of them might not have the template's common features.<br /> <br /> Having enough of a substance that creates Oddity-type Body Thieves to be able to hand it out for the sake of harvesting Sekhem feels less like an isolated scene and more like the sort of thing that kicks off and/or rounds off a storyline, particularly given that in Mummy's metaphysics there's almost definitely Sekhem already in that stuff to begin with unless some very particular ritual is going down that the dosing is the culmination of. (A power hallucinogen containing or being used to generate the energy roused to escape Suffering is, of course, very apropos.)<br /> <br /> At present it's firmly in the &quot;figure out what you want it to be for your game&quot; category, but an easy enough explanation is that rituals and other circumstances that produce a form of immortality generate the new immortal's first dot of Sekhem in the same way that a mummy pursuing Apotheosis in 1e only has Sekhem 1 \u2014 it's the Sekhem of their own soul, concentrated in such a way as facilitates their immortality as long as the conditions that enable it are maintained. For Body Thieves, that means stealing a new body before the one they're in dies, which means they necessarily have one as soon as they've performed a swap with whatever method has given them transitional immortality.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-05T22:19:15-08:00","id":1504536,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1504519#post1504519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Per Mummy 2e, the body abandoned by a Mentally Talented Body Thief almost immediately dies, while Magically Talented Body Thieves' theft is temporary unless they kill their old body or are transferring to a body without a soul, which indicates to me that having your mind swapped doesn't give you the Body Thief template any more than a mage casting a spell to swap your mind with somebody else's would. Oddities in the vein of the Brown Acid or Death.com have their particulars handled at Storyteller discretion; some of them might not have the template's common features.<br /> <br /> Having enough of a substance that creates Oddity-type Body Thieves to be able to hand it out for the sake of harvesting Sekhem feels less like an isolated scene and more like the sort of thing that kicks off and/or rounds off a storyline, particularly given that in Mummy's metaphysics there's almost definitely Sekhem already in that stuff to begin with unless some very particular ritual is going down that the dosing is the culmination of. (A power hallucinogen containing or being used to generate the energy roused to escape Suffering is, of course, very apropos.)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Funny you should say that. The inspiration for that scenario comes more or less directly from an old World of Darkness supplement called Shades of Gray in the Orpheus line. Basically that game heavily involves ghosts and the underworld, and include a drug called Pigment that lets you see ghosts and turns you into a ghost if you die while taking the drug. The plot involves a batch of Pigment getting laced with arsenic to create a large mass of ghosts that are then attacked by Spectres (which are akin to ethereal Shuankhsen after a fashion, which serve a powerful entropic force called Oblivion that parallels Ammut enough to make it easy to adapt). The resultant slaughter allows the Spectres to create a 'hive', which was a combination of a homebase and a doorway into the underworld. I remember it being a fairly solid adventure like most of that line and I'm considering adapting it for a Chronicle, replacing the pigment with the Brown Acid and adjusting the rest of the scenario as appropriate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T21:52:33-07:00","id":1505226,"title":"","content":"Not sure I see a contradiction between the two. Mutapa states that mages can't damage permanent Pillar ratings or impose soul loss or similar effects. Nameless &amp; Accursed states that the souls of mummies are immune to all forms of theft or tampering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-03-12T22:18:41-07:00","id":1505228,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't either. What I am asking is, would you consider attempting to destroy the soul of a Deathless as tampering under those rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>Think that's about as tamper-y as you can possibly get, yes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T13:05:31-07:00","id":1508065,"title":"","content":"Maybe this was already debated, anyway, if an Arisen loses his original body and need a new one, the new vessel has to be a living person?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-11T17:59:44-07:00","id":1508092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1508065#post1508065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe this was already debated, anyway, if an Arisen loses his original body and need a new one, the new vessel has to be a living person?</div> </div> </div> </div>Invested ephemeral cultists explicitly can't be used to resurrect unless they've Claimed a host, and reincarnating into a vessel that isn't one of your canopic jars requires Investment, which requires the subject to be a part of a Scorpion Cult and swearing loyalty to the mummy that they mean on some level.<br /> <br /> Merging with/consuming/overpowering a cultist's soul inflicts the Memory Bleed Condition, and since the soul departs after death that necessarily implies the character must be alive for the mummy to take over their body. A case could be made for incarnating into the body of a vampire or other Invested monster resulting in no mechanical difference from taking over a mortal body \u2014 it's how the Unchained do the same basic thing calling in soul pacts with monsters \u2014 but the Memory Bleed Condition is pretty definitely written under the assumption that you're wrestling with the memories of someone that had Integrity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-15T19:10:20-07:00","id":1508505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> lol yeah. To explain that's why I said bear with me in the post. I was talking with someone who rather rudely was arguing against that and I started to feel a little like I was going crazy because like you said, that's about as tampery as it gets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically a mummy's soul has been shown in all other ways to be one of the most enduring and indestructible things in the Chronicles of Darkness, so yeah, it doesn't make much sense for it to be under these rules all of a sudden.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T06:47:57-07:00","id":1508881,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Mummy Core merit list.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TIMELESS MERITS</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">These Merits are only available to mummies and other immortal entities\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Would the merits be usable by:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li><b>Vampires?</b><br /> Not timeless but immortal.</li> <li><b>Mages using spells / legacy attainments / template changes to get (conditional) immortality?</b><br /> Spells like <i>Veil of Moments</i> or template changes like becoming a Tremere.</li> <li><b>Prometheans?</b><br /> AFAIK, while they keep on the Pilgrimage, they do not die (I might be wrong on this point).</li> </ol>I get that pillar, duat, and guild related merits make no sense, but things like <b>Enigma</b> and <b>Cult </b>would be useful to the supernaturals.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 04-19-2023, 11:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T10:16:56-07:00","id":1508904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1508881#post1508881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Mummy Core merit list.[*]<b>Prometheans?</b><br /> AFAIK, while they keep on the Pilgrimage, they do not die (I might be wrong on this point).[/LIST]I get that pillar, duat, and guild related merits make no sense, but things like <b>Enigma</b> and <b>Cult </b>would be useful to the supernaturals.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I know very little about Promethean and less about Mummy, but I was reading Promethean yesterday and saw they do die. They get around a century, which restarts when they die their one time, so they can only go up to about 2 centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T10:57:47-07:00","id":1508910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1508881#post1508881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that pillar, duat, and guild related merits make no sense, but things like <b>Enigma</b> and <b>Cult </b>would be useful to the supernaturals.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Default to &quot;immortals&quot; here meaning &quot;the immortals in the mummy book.&quot; Vampires in particular are referred to in Mummy parlance as Lifeless, not Endless. (Prometheans would probably be similar, being a sort of &quot;sub-mortal&quot; state. Their default state is to cheat death once, though an Osiran Bestowment can revivify a few more times.)<br /> <br /> Cult's non-mummy equivalent is Mystery Cult Initiation (and Mystery Cult Influence, found in Mage). At Storyteller's discretion, it could make sense for particular non-mummy characters to have some form of Enigma or Dead Celebrity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-19T16:23:09-07:00","id":1508936,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1508904#post1508904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know very little about Promethean and less about Mummy, but I was reading Promethean yesterday and saw they do die. They get around a century, which restarts when they die their one time, so they can only go up to about 2 centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> I wasn't sure of the status, but this parses.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Anything supernatural I'd personally not be inclined to give to an immortal supernatural like that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some thing do make sense for some characters like <b>Dead Celebrity</b> (pretty vampire/promethean that &quot;looks&quot; like a dead starlet is actually the starlet, or at least their body), or <b>Enigma</b> (Mekhet vampires just seem to fit here).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1508910#post1508910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Default to &quot;immortals&quot; here meaning &quot;the immortals in the mummy book.&quot; Vampires in particular are referred to in Mummy parlance as Lifeless, not Endless. (Prometheans would probably be similar, being a sort of &quot;sub-mortal&quot; state. Their default state is to cheat death once, though an Osiran Bestowment can revivify a few more times.)<br /> <br /> Cult's non-mummy equivalent is Mystery Cult Initiation (and Mystery Cult Influence, found in Mage). At Storyteller's discretion, it could make sense for particular non-mummy characters to have some form of Enigma or Dead Celebrity.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that Cult from Mummy had extra details/options that the Mystery Cult does not have (Reach and Grasp). And for a Mage legacy I was thinking it seems a fitting set of requirements to have Anonymity / Enigma / Occultation. The (socially and mystically) Invisible Men.<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T07:04:52-07:00","id":1509579,"title":"","content":"Can multiple mummies share a cult or can there be only one mummy per cult?<br /> <br /> Also, if a mummy is subordinate to another mummy, could the superior mummy gain the benefits of their subordinate's cult mechanics wise?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27678-cybirddude","name":"cybirddude","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"85"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-04-25T18:07:39-07:00","id":1509664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cybirddude</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1509579#post1509579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can multiple mummies share a cult or can there be only one mummy per cult?</div> </div> </div> </div>Multiple mummies can explicitly pool dots in the Cult Merit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if a mummy is subordinate to another mummy, could the superior mummy gain the benefits of their subordinate's cult mechanics wise? </div> </div> </div>Scorpion Cults' Dominance rating adds to their Arisen masters' Social rolls with members of their own guild, which makes it easier for mummies belonging to powerful cults to persuade their guildmates to direct their cults to do stuff on their behalf.<br /> <br /> Guild Status independent of your cult's prestige isn't so much a thing anymore, so being &quot;subordinate to&quot; another mummy amounts to having a less powerful cult and belonging to the same guild as another mummy who says they're your boss and can back that assertion up in some way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T11:28:53-07:00","id":1512292,"title":"","content":"Lots of Vestiges questions:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Does the<b> Willpower Refresh</b> effect of Vessels apply to any Anchor equivalent (Virtue, Vice, Needle, Thread, Mask, Dirge), or does it only apply to Balance and Burden?</li> <li>Can non-Sorcerer (mortals or other Supernaturals) create <b>Vessels </b>using the Open Rite?</li> <li>Can <b>Vessels </b>or <b>Relics </b>be also other supernatural object? A <b>Vessel </b>object that is also a <b>Fetish </b>or <b>Token</b>. (I am inclined to say No for Relics, Yes for Vestiges), and maybe for minor things like a Mysterium mage having a Text Relic as a Dedicated Magical Tool.</li> </ol>Thanks,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-21T13:49:24-07:00","id":1512298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1512292#post1512292\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the<b> Willpower Refresh</b> effect of Vessels apply to any Anchor equivalent (Virtue, Vice, Needle, Thread, Mask, Dirge), or does it only apply to Balance and Burden?</div> </div> </div> </div>The verbiage seems to indicate the former rather than the latter.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can non-Sorcerer (mortals or other Supernaturals) create <b>Vessels </b>using the Open Rite? </div> </div> </div>That is the definition of an Open Rite, yes.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can <b>Vessels </b>or <b>Relics </b>be also other supernatural object? A <b>Vessel </b>object that is also a <b>Fetish </b>or <b>Token</b>. (I am inclined to say No for Relics, Yes for Vestiges), and maybe for minor things like a Mysterium mage having a Text Relic as a Dedicated Magical Tool. </div> </div> </div>Historically, no, magical object types from different gamelines are mutually incompatible. (A Dedicated Tool is not a magical object in the first place.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-23T02:30:14-07:00","id":1512417,"title":"","content":"Most of these should undergo mechanical revisions, but I love many of the Affinities from Book of the Deceived. In particular those that tamper with the deeper metaphysics: <i>Syllables of the Broken Word</i>, <i>Blessed of the Black Stars</i> and <i>Ever-Dying Name</i>. I'm also fond of the concept behind <i>Forge of Falsehoods</i> Utterance from the Rio supplement, even if its Tiers swing between too broadly useful and too situational.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>~<span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">\u266b</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7593-teatime","name":"Teatime","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7593_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"750"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T12:02:32-07:00","id":1513097,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1512298#post1512298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The verbiage seems to indicate the former rather than the latter.<br /> That is the definition of an Open Rite, yes.<br /> Historically, no, magical object types from different gamelines are mutually incompatible. (A Dedicated Tool is not a magical object in the first place.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Are non-Sorcerer creators also immune to the curses of Vestiges they create?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-28T13:48:36-07:00","id":1513109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1513097#post1513097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are non-Sorcerer creators also immune to the curses of Vestiges they create?</div> </div> </div> </div>It specifically says sorcerers and gives a page reference for the section on sorcerers, whose subsection on Mechanics specifies that a sorcerer is any character who takes the Ritual Sorcerer Merit, which is a Supernatural Merit and therefore cannot be taken by non-mortal characters without an explicit exception like the Endless have. No.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T13:10:43-07:00","id":1520406,"title":"","content":"What is a purified's dice pool to use Shadow Dominion? Is it only charisma (since they lack the other two stats that would be used by Words of the Dead Dominion)? Can they use it in ephemeral form? If so what is their dicepool then, only power? <br /> <br /> On a second question about the purified, do they gain their rank to all their ephemeral stats, and then their rank again divided as they choose (as per twilight projection &amp; purified power)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27618-shadowcatx","name":"ShadowcatX","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27618_2.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-11T18:32:43-07:00","id":1520421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ShadowcatX</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1520406#post1520406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is a purified's dice pool to use Shadow Dominion? Is it only charisma (since they lack the other two stats that would be used by Words of the Dead Dominion)? Can they use it in ephemeral form? If so what is their dicepool then, only power?</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be my reading; if the Purified didn't already add some or all of their Rank to their Attributes I'd say replace Sekhem with Rank in the dicepool for Tier 2, but as it stands Presence/Power + applicable bonus dots from Rank can generally manage at least the standard four dice = 3/4 chance of success odds with more than starting Rank on singular or plural Gafflings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On a second question about the purified, do they gain their rank to all their ephemeral stats, and then their rank again divided as they choose (as per twilight projection &amp; purified power)? </div> </div> </div>That appears to be the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T08:55:57-07:00","id":1520528,"title":"","content":"A Witness Touchstone can just be an NPC, and an Inheritor cultist can just be an NPC member of your cult, but a Sadikh is supposed to be a special confidante and helper. It makes sense me to model a Sadikh with the Retainer merit; in terms of figuring out how helpful they can be to a Mummy; is that necessary? I suppose if you want to invest in a Sadikh who's both useful and trustworthy it'd make sense to buy Retainer and True Friend for them, and if you don't then it's just up to the Storyteller; do I have that right?<br /> <br /> The sidebar for Dreams of Dead Gods talks about possibly playing as people driven to form a cult and &quot;murder a willing volunteer&quot; to resurrect a Mummy. Playing a Mummy who has to start from scratch seems like a neat idea, but you do need either a surviving canopic jar, a surviving inheritor (or descendent with the Lineal Inheritor merit) or an intact sahu, right? If you're playing as cultists resurrecting a Mummy you don't necessarily need to follow the Mummy rules chapter-and-verse but if you're playing the actual Mummy being resurrected, I don't think murdering a willing volunteer would actually be part of the process unless it's just part of the cult's awakening ritual? Maybe I'm just overthinking it but I'm curious of the &quot;murder a willing volunteer&quot; bit is supported in the rules or if it's just a flavorful start to a variant campaign.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T09:26:27-07:00","id":1520530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1520528#post1520528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Witness Touchstone can just be an NPC, and an Inheritor cultist can just be an NPC member of your cult, but a Sadikh is supposed to be a special confidante and helper. It makes sense me to model a Sadikh with the Retainer merit; in terms of figuring out how helpful they can be to a Mummy; is that necessary? I suppose if you want to invest in a Sadikh who's both useful and trustworthy it'd make sense to buy Retainer and True Friend for them, and if you don't then it's just up to the Storyteller; do I have that right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadikh are pretty clearly written to use a full character sheet, which Retainers don't have since they just use the Merit rating for all their dicepools.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The sidebar for Dreams of Dead Gods talks about possibly playing as people driven to form a cult and &quot;murder a willing volunteer&quot; to resurrect a Mummy. Playing a Mummy who has to start from scratch seems like a neat idea, but you do need either a surviving canopic jar, a surviving inheritor (or descendent with the Lineal Inheritor merit) or an intact sahu, right? If you're playing as cultists resurrecting a Mummy you don't necessarily need to follow the Mummy rules chapter-and-verse but if you're playing the actual Mummy being resurrected, I don't think murdering a willing volunteer would actually be part of the process unless it's just part of the cult's awakening ritual? Maybe I'm just overthinking it but I'm curious of the &quot;murder a willing volunteer&quot; bit is supported in the rules or if it's just a flavorful start to a variant campaign. </div> </div> </div>This may be mistakenly referencing the Twice-Arisen mechanics from 1e, but the example of character creation also frames the host body's becoming the vessel of the mummy as giving his life to the cult, and the cultist does still die with the mummy at the end of the Descent \u2014 the Book of Lasting Death specifies that a mummy can only incarnate into the body of an ephemeral cultist who has Claimed a host, and the ephemeral cultist explicitly does not survive the process.<br /> <br /> tl;dr Whether you consider it &quot;murder&quot; or not, volunteering to become the vessel of an Arisen personality is giving yourself a couple of years to live at best, and that's yoked to the Descent unless the rising of Sothis has been kind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T10:13:25-07:00","id":1520534,"title":"","content":"Thanks for those; I think it'd still make sense to buy True Friend for a Sadikh even if just to signal the Storyteller you'd like a positive relationship with them, even if you don't need to spend points on Retainer. If multiple PCs had Sadikhs it might still make sense to treat them like retainers or otherwise abstract things a little just to simplify the Storyteller's workload.<br /> <br /> Okay yeah, I wondered if there was a holdover from 1e with that sidebar. I'm pretty sure the rulebook also states that the Inheritor being targeted for resurrection doesn't actually have to be willing, which was another reason I was curious. Strictly speaking, if a Mummy got totally wiped out their next Descent would be in a time (or timeline) where they did have something to resurrect from; I don't think Dreams of a Dead God is enough on its own to bring a Mummy back from that kind of setback, I guess that was the crux of my question.<br /> I was also curious about that example from character creation; it sounded as if they'd transplanted the Mummy's heart from its canopic jar into the body of the Hong Kong detective, like a combination of the Inheritor and canopic jar resurrections. Not strictly rules-as-written but not that far-fetched if the Storyteller okays it.<br /> <br /> I think the questions about identity that you get with the Inheritor resurrection are a really cool part of the game, and playing someone who doesn't understand exactly what's happened to them or what they've become sounds really interesting.<br /> Makes me think Bob Howard from the Laundry Files would make an interesting basis for a Mummy character.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u200bOh, and I thought of another question: Mummies get Iremic language at Memory 1: is that the language that they start with or is that considered extra because it's technically tied to Memory? So do new Mummy characters start with a language of the players choice AND Iremic at Memory 1, or just Iremic because you can't really communicate at Memory 0 anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","user":"Niknokk","date":". 08-13-2023, 01:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11959-niknokk","name":"Niknokk","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T11:27:30-07:00","id":1520535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1520534#post1520534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> \u200bOh, and I thought of another question: Mummies get Iremic language at Memory 1: is that the language that they start with or is that considered extra because it's technically tied to Memory? So do new Mummy characters start with a language of the players choice AND Iremic at Memory 1, or just Iremic because you can't really communicate at Memory 0 anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's considered extra, though it's easier to understand if you flip the script a little, that the level of Memory 1 is rooted to the language because so much of what we understand about cognition is wrapped up in linguistics, and particularly the dominant linguistic of your every day life. It's effectively saying that if you don't remember a whole lot about who you are, you're still going to remember your most potent way of interacting with the abstract elements of reality in the same way you'll rely on your senses.<br /> <br /> So at character creation, it goes something like &quot;Everyone knows Iremite, plus one language that's going to be relevant to the story.&quot;*<br /> <br /> *unless your have a story where the opening, at least, is rooted in not being able to easily communicate with the NPC's, but that's a niche.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-13T11:59:45-07:00","id":1520541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Niknokk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1520534#post1520534\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, and I thought of another question: Mummies get Iremic language at Memory 1: is that the language that they start with or is that considered extra because it's technically tied to Memory? So do new Mummy characters start with a language of the players choice AND Iremic at Memory 1, or just Iremic because you can't really communicate at Memory 0 anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that you don't start at Memory 1, the thematic isolation/containment of one's cult described in 1e's Tongues of Ages Past still ringing true, and mummies get not only get the usual three bonus Merit dots as supernatural characters (separate from the free starting dots in Tomb and Cult) but also get 10 starting Experiences and get more out of the Language Merit, it seems appropriate for the character to need to circumvent the language barrier magically or through learning other languages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T07:15:55-07:00","id":1520666,"title":"","content":"I don't know if I am doing this right, but are the judges of mummy the curse based upon the 42 judges of the dead from Egyptian mythology? I feel like they are, but I would like confirmation from someone who knows for sure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T17:11:59-07:00","id":1520724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>evtrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1520666#post1520666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if I am doing this right, but are the judges of mummy the curse based upon the 42 judges of the dead from Egyptian mythology? I feel like they are, but I would like confirmation from someone who knows for sure</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes and no. The inspiration is absolutely the 42 Assessors of Maat that judged a particular sin during the 'weighing of the heart' scenario in Ancient Egyptian mythology. Their specific names are in fact based on a particular scholar's translations of the Negative confessions (I want to say Budge, but don't quote me on that).<br /> <br /> That said, there really isn't much in common between the original mythology and Mummy beyond sharing a name and the sins they judge being somewhat based on the negative confessions from the Book of the Dead (I say somewhat because a lot of those sins are heavily extrapolated and treated with lots of poetic license). I speak from personal experience- doing research on the topic and comparing the two tends be get frustrating. The write ups do what they need to do in the context of the game, but there were some missed opportunities. Most of the judges are obscure and we don't know much about their Egyptian mythology beyond their names. But the ones we do know a lot about are often completely different from their in game counterparts. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-15T17:36:56-07:00","id":1520728,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2244\" data-vbnamecard=\"2244\">nothri</a> that's actually what I was asking. Thanks for confirming that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26173-evtrax","name":"evtrax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T09:47:46-07:00","id":1521597,"title":"","content":"Considering that Nether Khertet is a sort of Death related Twilight, do you think that death related powers (Sin eater senses, Death arcanum, the Medium merit) could perceive and manipulate Shades and Amkhata?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T10:54:23-07:00","id":1521602,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1521597#post1521597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that Nether Khertet is a sort of Death related Twilight, do you think that death related powers (Sin eater senses, Death arcanum, the Medium merit) could perceive and manipulate Shades and Amkhata?</div> </div> </div> </div>Amkhata would be debatable. Shades? Absolutely! The only reason they don\u2019t usually perceive them is because of the Ashen Storm, but get one that isn\u2019t lurking behind that, such as a Shade cultist, and they\u2019re totally fair game. Of course, most wouldn\u2019t realize they weren\u2019t a ghost.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-29T12:40:03-07:00","id":1521612,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>White Oak Dragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1521602#post1521602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Amkhata would be debatable. Shades? Absolutely! The only reason they don\u2019t usually perceive them is because of the Ashen Storm, but get one that isn\u2019t lurking behind that, such as a Shade cultist, and they\u2019re totally fair game. Of course, most wouldn\u2019t realize they weren\u2019t a ghost.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks \ud83d\udc4d<br /> In fact the Amkhata twilight condition confuse me<br /> in what frequency of Twilight they are?<br /> They have the dread power Ghost touch to interact with ghosts, but does this mean that they are already able to see them?<br /> What kind of Affinity could use a Mummy to see the Amkhata?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T12:42:02-07:00","id":1522531,"title":"","content":"About attributes and Sekhem<br /> Trait Maximum column indicates the maximum limit that you can buy with experience, and you lose 6+ trait levels only when you hit Sekhem 5 right?<br /> <br /> About using Pillar points, you can boost an Attribute with ONLY one pillar point per scene, gaining (Sekhem determined) dots? Can you spend a second point on a different physical attribute on the same scene?<br /> <br /> When you boost Favored attributes, each point boost one attribute dot or both?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T18:11:08-07:00","id":1522545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1521612#post1521612\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In fact the Amkhata twilight condition confuse me<br /> in what frequency of Twilight they are?<br /> They have the dread power Ghost touch to interact with ghosts, but does this mean that they are already able to see them?<br /> What kind of Affinity could use a Mummy to see the Amkhata?</div> </div> </div> </div>My best suggestion is to ignore Ghost Touch sitting there. That's just where Mummy puts the list of Dread Powers, which are a semi-universal list of supernatural powers CofD uses for various miscellaneous beings. Some things that have Dread Powers would need Ghost Touch to touch ghosts. Amkhata do not.<br /> All of the ephemeral entities introduced in the Mummy corebook share the same &quot;frequency&quot; of Twilight, which Mummy calls Neter-Khertet. This is the same Twilight &quot;frequency&quot; used by ghosts, the one containing Avernian Gates which open to Geist's Underworld.<br /> <br /> Both the Deathsight and Enlightened Senses Soul Affinities can be used to see and touch Amkhata in Twilight (as well as any other inhabitants of Neter-Khertet). The Jackal's Shade Affinity conferred by the Ashem decree can be used to enter Neter-Khertet yourself, where you can then see and touch Amkhata in Twilight.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1522531#post1522531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About attributes and Sekhem<br /> When you boost Favored attributes, each point boost one attribute dot or both?</div> </div> </div> </div>Each point boosts both Attributes. If your decree is Ashem, you favor Composure and Stamina, and thus spending two points of Sheut gives you +2 Composure and +2 Stamina for the scene.\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-13T19:17:58-07:00","id":1522550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1522531#post1522531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About attributes and Sekhem<br /> Trait Maximum column indicates the maximum limit that you can buy with experience, and you lose 6+ trait levels only when you hit Sekhem 5 right?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you have an Attribute above 5 and your current Sekhem is 5 or lower, for all intents and purposes your rating in that Attribute is 5 until your Sekhem rating equals or exceeds the Attribute rating on your sheet.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> About using Pillar points, you can boost an Attribute with ONLY one pillar point per scene, gaining (Sekhem determined) dots? Can you spend a second point on a different physical attribute on the same scene? </div> </div> </div>Once per scene you can boost a single Physical Attribute by the amount determined by your Sekhem rating. That means one Attribute per scene, no splitting; presumably the difference from 1e is related to the fact that the boosted Attributes aren't explicitly subject to your Sekhem-based Trait limit (and also implicitly aren't subject to it either, because otherwise there'd be no need to specify that you calculate boosts starting from 5 if you have a natural 6+ rating you can't currently access).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-09-14T02:41:19-07:00","id":1522564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1522550#post1522550\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once per scene you can boost a single Physical Attribute by the amount determined by your Sekhem rating. That means one Attribute per scene, no splitting; presumably the difference from 1e is related to the fact that the boosted Attributes aren't explicitly subject to your Sekhem-based Trait limit (and also implicitly aren't subject to it either, because otherwise there'd be no need to specify that you calculate boosts starting from 5 if you have a natural 6+ rating you can't currently access).</div> </div> </div> </div>It could work that way.<br /> But why, at page 122 in the core it states <br /> &quot;Once per scene, spending Pillar points&quot;<br /> instead of &quot;one pillar point&quot; ?<br /> I suspect that using &quot;single attributes&quot; means only that you can t distribute the dots from one boost between more attributes<br /> what do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-07T17:17:30-07:00","id":1523797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I may likely be misremembering, but I swore there was something in Mummy 1st edition about called shots and mummies.</div> </div> </div> </div>A quick search in my 1e core pdf only turns up Nenitu, where called shots to their heads suffer a -1 penalty but inflict aggravated damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-08T17:48:22-07:00","id":1523847,"title":"","content":"This is a lore question. I've been trying to hunt down what happened to the Order of Izft (see Sothis Ascends under the entry for the Byzantine Empire in the third Turn). I think our esteemed Gentleman Gamer detailed on the forum what happened after the fall of Constantinople but I can't find the info. I believe for a time the Order relocated to Moscow (in effect replaying their old rivalry with the First Chorus who had moved to Washington DC through the clash of empires during the Cold War) but then they relocated after the collapse of the Soviet Union. Does anyone remember what they were up to during the Moscow Era and where they ended up in the aftermath?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-18T23:36:51-07:00","id":1524261,"title":"","content":"Is there any way to permanently destroy Shuankshen or Arisen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T12:41:55-07:00","id":1524336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1524261#post1524261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any way to permanently destroy Shuankshen or Arisen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Rearrange the universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-20T18:05:37-07:00","id":1524340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1524261#post1524261\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any way to permanently destroy Shuankshen or Arisen?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thwart them completely at every turn such that their Judge is so furious with their constant and irredeemable failure that it destroys them, as described in the &quot;Escaping the Cycle&quot; sidebar on page 326 of the corebook.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T12:03:44-07:00","id":1524392,"title":"","content":"What happens when a Shuankhsen is fulled with agg damage?<br /> Does it enter a death cycle?<br /> Having no memory rating there is no indication about an eventual return time","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T14:47:17-07:00","id":1524400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1524392#post1524392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens when a Shuankhsen is fulled with agg damage?<br /> Does it enter a death cycle?<br /> Having no memory rating there is no indication about an eventual return time</div> </div> </div> </div>Provided they have any Pillar points, they can engage Body Snatcher to hop into an Invested body or the nearest mortal corpse; this is the equivalent of the mechanic from 1e, which also explicitly happens when the Lifeless mummy's Sekhem runs out or their body is utterly destroyed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T14:57:23-07:00","id":1524401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1524400#post1524400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Provided they have any Pillar points, they can engage Body Snatcher to hop into an Invested body or the nearest mortal corpse; this is the equivalent of the mechanic from 1e, which also explicitly happens when the Lifeless mummy's Sekhem runs out or their body is utterly destroyed.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if they run out of Sekhem or have no Pillar points to Snatch, do they enter in a variant Henet where Ammut chew on them until they are spitted in another time with full 10 Sekhem?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-22T19:22:24-07:00","id":1524409,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1524401#post1524401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if they run out of Sekhem or have no Pillar points to Snatch, do they enter in a variant Henet where Ammut chew on them until they are spitted in another time with full 10 Sekhem?</div> </div> </div> </div>Body-Snatcher specifically says &quot;This may be used automatically before the Shuankhsen loses or spends their last point of Sekhem&quot; and the Rite of Eternal Chains refers to the Fasad being &quot;dismissed into eternal dormancy for eras in between&quot; the times when their masters walk the Earth.<br /> <br /> &quot;They remember everything. Every death and doorway, every love lost, every ounce of flesh torn from their bodies by the Deathless, every painful resurrection thereafter. The crevassed, twisted faces of screaming sorcerers, and the menacing Arisen who brought down the cult 300 years ago, or 20 years from now.\u200b&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Every death leads to [the Devourer], but no death is final.&quot;<br /> <br /> The 2e Shuankhsen mechanics are not terribly detailed, but the intent does not seem to be that they wander in Neter-Khertet or meet Anpu. Given that they are clearly not designed to serve as player characters, the idea seems to be that once they're brought down they're down until they're called up again, which is one more reason for them to lean into the fact that they have an escape hatch that goes away if they spend all their Pillars and don't keep any in reserve.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T04:30:36-07:00","id":1524745,"title":"","content":"About Eternal relics<br /> The first dot of merit is free, and you can probably buy other dots for a more potent Relic.<br /> The book says &quot;Their Power grants eternal life and other strange abilities that immortality might bring.&quot;<br /> What does it mean?<br /> <br /> -It function as a normal Relic, but with a special Power that can affect only its Eternal?<br /> -Every Immortal or Supernatural merits buyed are in fact extra levels of the Relic merit (capped at 5 but you can buy more than 5)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-30T05:29:41-07:00","id":1524751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1524745#post1524745\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About Eternal relics<br /> The first dot of merit is free, and you can probably buy other dots for a more potent Relic.<br /> The book says &quot;Their Power grants eternal life and other strange abilities that immortality might bring.&quot;<br /> What does it mean?<br /> <br /> -It function as a normal Relic, but with a special Power that can affect only its Eternal?<br /> -Every Immortal or Supernatural merits buyed are in fact extra levels of the Relic merit (capped at 5 but you can buy more than 5)?</div> </div> </div> </div>I read that as simply as possible; it's a nod to Eternals having Timeless Merits and Supernatural Merits that are, in-universe, justified as 'strange abilities that immortality might bring' i.e. powers gained by virtue of being an immortal.<br /> <br /> So an Eternal's Relic would remain just a Relic, with its Power assigned according to its dot rating, the only perk being that it's the lifeline of an Eternal. Any other powers are mechanically different things, but in-universe identified as (and for most purposes, <i>are</i> ) powers granted by the relic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-10-31T11:05:37-07:00","id":1524822,"title":"","content":"The first free dot of an Eternal\u2019s Relic makes them Endless, and grants them all the perks that come with it. By increasing the Relic\u2019s rating, you can gain additional abilities for it like any other. Buying a Supernatural Merit grants the capability to the Eternal like any other Immortal with it. So for example, an Endless with Telepathy would gain the ability to read minds whether they were an Eternal or a Blood Bather. If someone stole this Eternal\u2019s Relic, they\u2019d still be able to read minds, but they\u2019d likely be very worried until they regained the Relic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T16:10:56-07:00","id":1525040,"title":"","content":"Regarding the Driven condition only resolves on replenishing Willpower or does it also resolve when retaining Willpower?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Driven</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your character knows they are destined for greatness.<br /> <b>When spending Willpower to enhance a roll, the character<br /> retains the Willpower point on an exceptional success</b>. When<br /> using their final Willpower point to enhance a roll, the char-<br /> acter may find a new reserve of inner strength, resolving this<br /> Condition to fully replenish their Willpower.<br /> Possible Sources: The Trials of Duat<br /> Resolution: Use the Condition for its benefit.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Essentially if you never resolve the condition, are you permanently retaining Willpower points on exceptional successes?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T17:57:04-07:00","id":1525048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1525040#post1525040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the Driven condition only resolves on replenishing Willpower or does it also resolve when retaining Willpower?<br /> <br /> Essentially if you never resolve the condition, are you permanently retaining Willpower points on exceptional successes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Resolves on replenishing, as stated, subject to the usual &quot;a Condition can go away if it ceases to be relevant&quot; caveat, e.g. if you go through the entire story without resolving it and come back to the Trials again with a different outcome. Given that without Inspiration and similar exceptional success threshold-lowered effects the best odds most characters will have of exceptional success is a coin toss and mummies don't need to sleep (and are narratively incentivized not to), most player characters will only regain Willpower from their Balance and Burden.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T18:30:37-07:00","id":1525051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1525048#post1525048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resolves on replenishing, as stated, subject to the usual &quot;a Condition can go away if it ceases to be relevant&quot; caveat, e.g. if you go through the entire story without resolving it and come back to the Trials again with a different outcome. Given that without Inspiration and similar exceptional success threshold-lowered effects the best odds most characters will have of exceptional success is a coin toss and mummies don't need to sleep (and are narratively incentivized not to), most player characters will only regain Willpower from their Balance and Burden.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, could this condition be granted to a non-Mummy? For example Mages using their Praxis exceptional success, or Fate granted Conditions, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-04T20:05:48-07:00","id":1525053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lbeaumanior</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1525051#post1525051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks, could this condition be granted to a non-Mummy? For example Mages using their Praxis exceptional success, or Fate granted Conditions, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's functionally in the same genre of effect as Inspired, so sure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T09:34:01-08:00","id":1525121,"title":"","content":"What happens to the body of a Mummy after it resolves the Memory bleed condition?<br /> It s a blend of the two bodies or it has the appearance of the Inheriror only?<br /> <br /> Also, if the Mummy has Descent 1 in year 50 ad, Descent 2 in 1900 ad, and Descent 3 in 1000 ad where it switch body, what body would it has in Descent 2 ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-06T19:21:47-08:00","id":1525145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1525121#post1525121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What happens to the body of a Mummy after it resolves the Memory bleed condition?<br /> It s a blend of the two bodies or it has the appearance of the Inheriror only?</div> </div> </div> </div>Player's choice. The Condition is specifically resolved by amalgamating the two personalities and the sahu is a magical projection of the character's identity to such a degree that 1e suggested acquiring derangements could physically alter it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, if the Mummy has Descent 1 in year 50 ad, Descent 2 in 1900 ad, and Descent 3 in 1000 ad where it switch body, what body would it has in Descent 2 ? </div> </div> </div>If you mean the sahu, the mummy's self-image is as appropriate for that point in its personal experience of time. If you mean the physical remains they were Called into, it's the remains of the body they incarnated into in Descent 3 unless something else happened in between or a parallel timeline was involved or something else strange happened.<br /> <br /> It's horror logic. Best not to think about it too hard.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T15:43:58-08:00","id":1525389,"title":"","content":"Even as a Mage fanboy, I wouldn't support it. Make an off-brand version? Maybe, but that would probably end up being a Deviant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">Monkish Asexual.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1490057-cauthon-s-homebrew-hub#post1490057\" target=\"_blank\">My homebrew hub</a><br /> <br /> Mostly checked out, there's an uncomfortable amount of condescension in the old guard.</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27258-cauthon","name":"Cauthon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27258_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1780"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-12T19:07:07-08:00","id":1525391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've seen some Mage fans think that an archmage can remake the Rite of Return. I'm skeptical, for a number of reasons including but not just because it's not the best of ideas of another game line can recreate such a game line central aspect of another. But nevertheless, curious as to the thoughts of others.</div> </div> </div> </div>In terms of archspells and Imperium Rites being able to leverage chronicle-spanning activities to change the world, specifically by creating a globe-spanning collection of cults and immortal servitors? Sure, with the obvious caveats that:<br /> <br /> 1. Several godlike beings (including the Exarchs and the Judges) will have Strong Opinions about this and run interference accordingly (and that interference and the nature of Omens means the outcome wouldn't be the same even if you tried for a direct replication), and<br /> 2. Unless the game in which this happens is using it as a starting point for the chronicle, any archmage (or circle thereof) would need to play through the processes necessary to reach that stage (if it's being done by player characters) or be affecting events the players can be aware of and potentially interfere with to some degree (if it's a background process relevant to the chronicle).<br /> <br /> An archmage <i>can</i> destroy the universe, too \u2014 the playbook Imperial Mysteries operates under means nothing is wholly off the table \u2014 but that doesn't mean it's trivial, easy, or practical to do so. The most likely reason one <i>would</i> is for the same reason so many of them have tried to replicate Atlantis (and why the Shan'iatu tried it in the first place): it's their ticket to Heavenly residence.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:10px\">Supplementary caveat that the Rite of Return was given to the architects of the Nameless Empire by the Devourer to suit Her designs and a whole lot went wrong with it by the temakh's standards, so recreating the feat as one of the few beings who isn't magically locked out of trying to perceive the whole picture of Arisen timelines is a bit more than unWise, to boot.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-11-17T03:30:43-08:00","id":1525561,"title":"","content":"In core book, page 326 it states:<br /> &quot;This is a difficult path to walk, as one must prove useless enough to abandon without enraging the Judge enough to destroy them.&quot;<br /> So, what can a displeased Judge do in fact to its Arisen?<br /> Destroy means annhilation or throwing the Arisen to Ammut?<br /> If it s the latter, can Ammut choose to devour the Arisen or turn him into a Shuankhsen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-13T23:05:11-08:00","id":1526794,"title":"","content":"In dark eras2 , scandinavian witch trial chapter, there is a mummy with 2 touchstones.<br /> i ve searched in the core book, but i only found the rules for replacing lost ones, so how do you acquire multiple touchstones.?<br /> You simply add them after some time of interaction?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-12-14T06:05:59-08:00","id":1526804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1526794#post1526794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In dark eras2 , scandinavian witch trial chapter, there is a mummy with 2 touchstones.<br /> i ve searched in the core book, but i only found the rules for replacing lost ones, so how do you acquire multiple touchstones.?<br /> You simply add them after some time of interaction?</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems to be the case, much as you can choose not to start play with a Touchstone \u2014 &quot;Mummies start with one Touchstone, but may acquire more throughout the chronicle.&quot; Presumably new ones are limited to one per story just as declaring replacements is, but given that having them provides potential breaking points and their primary benefit is the ability to gain Reminisce Beats it certainly tracks for there to be no mechanical cost to acquiring them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-01T15:22:57-08:00","id":1527716,"title":"","content":"About boosting physical attributes with Pillar points, it is correct to assume that a Sekhem 10 mummy could spend five points to boost Strenght by 20 levels?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-01-02T01:33:20-08:00","id":1527755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, but you can boost it by 4 with a single point of a Pillar.</div> </div> </div> </div>At page 122 it is written &quot;Once per scene, spending Pillar points raises a single Physical Attribute by a number of dots determined by a mummy\u2019s current Sekhem rating&quot;<br /> <br /> It says points, not a single point or one point.<br /> I think that the possible cases are:<br /> -you can spend multiple points on the same attribute cumulating the boost, but you must spend all the points in one turn<br /> -you can spend multiple points on the different physical attributes giving +4 to each, but you must spend all the points in one turn<br /> -points is a typo, it should be written point<br /> <br /> What do you think?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T09:06:22-08:00","id":1530034,"title":"","content":"Sorry if this question is weird, but would the Arisen are the good guys, the bad guys or neutral as a general rule?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T09:36:54-08:00","id":1530038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1530034#post1530034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry if this question is weird, but would the Arisen are the good guys, the bad guys or neutral as a general rule?</div> </div> </div> </div>Individual Arisen can mean well, show loyalty to the members of their cults, and try to do good for the world. As a group, they are from an ancient people with an authoritarian and theocratic view on life, in thrall to a Curse designed to use them as unquestioning servants to steal life force from the world and issue punishments on behalf of self-righteous gods who wish the world to suffer.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T17:53:41-08:00","id":1530063,"title":"","content":"What would a group of hunters specialized in fighting Arisens have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-05T18:59:30-08:00","id":1530069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Psicose</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1530063#post1530063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What would a group of hunters specialized in fighting Arisens have?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends what you mean by &quot;fighting.&quot;<br /> <br /> Weird sorcery that can suspend the font of vitality giving a mummy their supercharged regenerative powers helps a team plink down the Health of the Arisen in a direct or running battle, as to other ways of bringing them closer to mortality.<br /> <br /> A way with people and the means to ensure people's needs are being met will serve a crew of cult deprogrammers much better in helping cut down on the likelihood that a mummy is summoned in the first place, as will keeping track of occult objects in one's area.<br /> <br /> The Arisen are encountered by hunters as part of a big-picture problem, because they've got infrastructure in place that causes them to become active, and those cults and tombs and collections of relics can be trouble on their own even before the walking corpse wakes up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-06T10:31:55-08:00","id":1530097,"title":"","content":"Are there rules for learning/using Nomenclature as a non-mummy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T14:15:03-08:00","id":1531698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Since the thread doesn't seem to be getting visibility or traction, I'll ask her. Broadly speaking, what would appeal more to you as a player. A power that lets a mummy draw strength from things dying around them, ghostly manifestations etc or one that passively empowers ghosts, shades and other allied beings in the local area of deathly Twilight?</div> </div> </div> </div>I would say the second one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T14:17:57-08:00","id":1531699,"title":"","content":"At page 161 of the core book there is a list of details remembered at various Memory levels.<br /> On recalled descent, at memory 10, it lists Rite of return, what does this mean?<br /> what is the difference with Mortal life, memory 5, death?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-02-28T14:39:48-08:00","id":1531700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1531699#post1531699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At page 161 of the core book there is a list of details remembered at various Memory levels.<br /> On recalled descent, at memory 10, it lists Rite of return, what does this mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Normally you don't remember what happened in Duat. At Memory 10 you clearly remember the events that gave you your Decree.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> what is the difference with Mortal life, memory 5, death? </div> </div> </div>At Memory 5 you remember your friends and family from the Nameless Empire and you remember how you died. This is very different from remembering your audience with the great gods who carve the world apart from chaos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-06T14:14:18-08:00","id":1532110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did the China Mummy/Hunter Dark Eras 2 for 2e ever get the full rules for talismans?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, on pages 239-241 of DE2.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T11:06:43-07:00","id":1532338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Voice of Conscience and it's Vice counterpart Affinity</b>-I haven't used the system that involves Doors too much in my games, but at face value these Affinities seem rather strong, especially when looking at the rest of the mummy power suite involving having better impression levels etc. What has been your experiences with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth remembering that most normal characters will only have two or maybe three Doors before adjusting for Anchors, Aspirations, and breaking points, that the ability to spend Willpower to open all Doors on a successful Social Maneuver is in the specific context of appealing to the target's Virtue or Vice, and that assisting a Touchstone in fulfilling their Virtue or indulging their Vice is a source of Reminisce Beats.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tangent of <b>Scorpion Vein</b>s-given the book kind of poorly has the information that specifies that mummies are not susceptible to non supernatural diseases, how do you run that with toxins? Given they're undead nature and lack of functional physiology like the living, I tend to have them also unaffected by non supernatural poisons by default. What do you usually do in your games? </div> </div> </div>1e didn't have the Arisen immune to poisons (there's a Bane Affinity whose effects include offloading the effects of poison and intoxication onto) and did have them universally immune to disease (and the same paragraph where this is mentioned says that some injuries that logically shouldn't affect them still do).<br /> <br /> Given this, 2e's lack of statement that the Arisen are immune to poison on the same page where it specifies their partial immunity to disease, and the fact that Scorpion Veins leads with &quot;The Arisen is immune to poisons,&quot; plus the practical concerns of not no-selling the main threat of Scorpion-Limbed Amkhata (and the thematic appropriateness of the servants of the Scorpion Empire not having any extra resistance to the main weapon of its symbolic creature), I'd run mummies as not being immune or resistant to poisons by default; their main mechanical effect is mitigated by Arisen regeneration rates anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Fated Soul</b>- Anyone made any house rules in regards to this and Beast Nightmares? </div> </div> </div>The +2 to contested resistance applies, the immunity doesn't; that's pretty much exactly how Beast's section on Nightmares says it would work: &quot;Nightmares function on supernatural creatures just as they do on normal human beings. Even creatures that don\u2019t dream or feel fear can tremble before the power of the Dark Mother. Such beings are, however, better able to resist than human beings.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Blessed is the God King</b>- Do or would you allow tier 2 to be used on supernatural beings? </div> </div> </div>Given that it specifies &quot;mortal,&quot; I'd say no.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Dreams of Dead Gods</b>-Do or would you allow tier 3 to be used on supernatural beings? </div> </div> </div>See previous.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Invoking Tempest's Fury</b> - Is tier 3 in conjunction with other tiers meant to cap at Extreme Environment 3 or 4? </div> </div> </div>3. This is an Utterance themed around wind and thunderstorms, and combining either of the two preceding effects (to say nothing of combining both) already means anyone the mummy might wish to damage can be pulverized by per-turn damage for the rest of the day/night.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Wrathful Desert Power</b>- Is tier 3 when invoking the power by taking a scene meant to create an Extreme Environment, and is the bonus effect meant to make you intangible in the storm? </div> </div> </div>Being substantially concealed applies a -3 penalty to ranged attacks against the mummy, the Sandstorm Tilt penalizes Physical rolls like attacks by -3 along with a scaling penalty to rolls to see anything as well as damaging living characters each turn due to lung damage, and the preceding Tier's bonus effect allows you to reflexively teleport. I would say it's not an Extreme Environment at extended length and the bonus effect doesn't make it impossible to hit you so much as the base Tier already makes you very hard to hit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-10-2024, 05:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-10T15:28:03-07:00","id":1532351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TyrannicalRabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm more interested on if people have found that impactful, and if so, how much. I am aware of what the Affinities do so why you decided to repeat that is.....something.</div> </div> </div> </div>You said they seemed strong. I bring up the constraints and relevance of that strength because the Affinities' applicability to Social Maneuvering specifically in line with a character's Virtue or Vice limits what they can be used to accomplish. Those limits in turn provide incentives to find opportunities to use the tools one has chosen to equip their character with. I would say getting a bonus to specifically convince one of the people you get a limited type of experience from to do things that give you that experience is plenty impactful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not asking or interested in 1e. </div> </div> </div>We have a limited number of books in 2e to contextualize the information the corebook provides and the things 2e has notably changed are larger than &quot;are the paradoxically living-and-dead mummies made of necromancy immune to toxins?&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's no reason why it would list that in the same section for disease, </div> </div> </div>I am referring to the fact that the section for disease is on the same page, which is the start of the section on Sources of Harm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> especially since that section for 2e <i>for </i>disease is so weirdly placed. It's apropos of nothing. Scorpion Veins also mentions mundane diseases even though mummies are immune by default, so it's wording is already off to a bad start. Scorpion Limbed doesn't point in any particular direction, especially as it's a supernatural creature, the idea that somehow it's pointing any way because it would be bad if you couldn't use it on mummies(assuming it's even non supernatural poison) is.....not convincing. I've got no real reason to make undead affected by non supernatural poisons. </div> </div> </div>Okay. You specifically asked for opinions. I provided my opinions. I am not here to argue about the quality of the specific wording of the text being interpreted.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Given the Contagion Chronicles Mind Shield for mages and the notation for it and Nightmares, I'm not really inclined to give much credence to that section. Theoretical for me altogether though, Beasts don't exist in my CofD. </div> </div> </div>Mental Shield protects against Goetic Numina, Influences, and Manifestations, which include things that are not purely mind-affecting phenomena. Nightmares are powers derived from a Goetic being. The line in the PG describes how Mental Shield applies on basically every descriptive level that would be relevant and is referring to a defense that provides its immunity by Clashing with relevant effects.<br /> <br /> You might, if you were so inclined, allow Fated Soul to Clash with Nightmares, but given that the mechanical effects of most Nightmares are not &quot;causes fear&quot; that would seem to open the door for some awkward hair-splitting about other effects. If you're not using Beasts at all I don't know why you're bothering to ask about interactions with their powers in particular.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Neither of those address my question. </div> </div> </div>I answered the first of these questions at the start (&quot;3,&quot; as in &quot;The Extreme Environment scaling for this Utterance effect is capped at 3&quot;) and the second of them at the end (&quot;I would say[\u2026]&quot;).<br /> <br /> A Level 4 Extreme Environment deals enough lethal damage to kill an average mortal in less than a minute, which is out of keeping with a collection of effects that deal bashing damage and are already being extended to the degree where Extreme Environments below the maximum level the system allows would need suboptimal activation timing and/or extremely frail targets to render somebody unconscious.<br /> <br /> Expanding the scope and duration of a Tilt whose effects are mostly penalty-based does not seem likely to translate to the system whose effects are mostly damage-based, nor does a bonus effect that talks about the character's increasing the character's Speed and granting them the ability to fit through small gaps seem likely to mean the character is intangible.<br /> <br /> Unless you have different questions than those that were supposed to be inferred, I have addressed your questions and pointed to contextualizing information. If you have questions about how I arrived at a given interpretation of the text I would be happy to provide it, but I don't think it does much good to answer a response to a request for opinions by immediately arguing with those opinions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 03-11-2024, 02:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-11T23:52:03-07:00","id":1532423,"title":"","content":"The core book states:<br /> &quot;The very sight of the Judges drives madness into the souls of their servants, preventing the Arisen from looking upon them directly.&quot;<br /> <br /> What does this exactly means?<br /> -you can look at them but it s taxing for the mind (1 Willpower per turn for example)<br /> -if you look at them you gain a persistent condition like madness<br /> -one look and your mind is obliterated, the judges speaks from behind a curtain<br /> <br /> The third option seems unlikely, because we have a physical description for every judge but one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T05:31:44-07:00","id":1532431,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1532423#post1532423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The core book states:<br /> &quot;The very sight of the Judges drives madness into the souls of their servants, preventing the Arisen from looking upon them directly.&quot;<br /> <br /> What does this exactly means?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a descriptive statement about how, in the purely narrative space of the Trials, your character will not look at the Judges directly when they are accounting for their actions in the last Descent.<br /> <br /> The nature of the Judges as cosmological entities, particularly in relation to their servants, makes it impossible outside of a climactic point in the entire chronicle, much like Azar speaking out loud will not be an unremarkable part of the Trials experienced by a mummy.<br /> <br /> It's soul-deep trauma. You might as well ask someone to make eye contact with the wood chipper that eats them head-first in all of their worst nightmares.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T09:52:07-07:00","id":1532440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1532431#post1532431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a descriptive statement about how, in the purely narrative space of the Trials, your character will not look at the Judges directly when they are accounting for their actions in the last Descent.<br /> <br /> The nature of the Judges as cosmological entities, particularly in relation to their servants, makes it impossible outside of a climactic point in the entire chronicle, much like Azar speaking out loud will not be an unremarkable part of the Trials experienced by a mummy.<br /> <br /> It's soul-deep trauma. You might as well ask someone to make eye contact with the wood chipper that eats them head-first in all of their worst nightmares.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, so how much clearly do you think a given mummy would know its Judge appearance?<br /> The chapter about the Judges lists a broad description of every one, do you think that those comes from shared recollections of glimpses at the Judge form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-12T12:12:16-07:00","id":1532443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1532440#post1532440\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, so how much clearly do you think a given mummy would know its Judge appearance?<br /> The chapter about the Judges lists a broad description of every one, do you think that those comes from shared recollections of glimpses at the Judge form?</div> </div> </div> </div>The parable of the blind men and the elephant is applicable, yes, as is the general phenomenon of iconography associated with a given Judge.<br /> <br /> The ancient Egyptians didn't think the gods were literally people with animal heads, and the Buddhists don't believe buddhas rendered with a thousand arms have a thousand flesh-and-blood limbs sprouting from normal human shoulders, but symbolic imagery conveys things about the Judge that the Judge itself is too cosmologically significant and painful to directly observe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T09:08:08-07:00","id":1533126,"title":"","content":"Core book states:<br /> &quot;The Nebtet, formed from the tears of Sutek, flows towards the western mountain, Manu, where the river falls through an akhet into Duat, flowing through the realm like the Nile. Guardian Fiends protect this Gate against any entry, slashing at the steady flow of shades descending into Duat. &quot;<br /> <br /> Does that mean that Duat doesn t want the Shades entering but they are simply too many to be stopped by the Guardians?<br /> OR<br /> Duat wants ONLY the shades to enter, but first they have to suffer by the Guardians","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-25T09:29:33-07:00","id":1533127,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1533126#post1533126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Core book states:<br /> &quot;The Nebtet, formed from the tears of Sutek, flows towards the western mountain, Manu, where the river falls through an akhet into Duat, flowing through the realm like the Nile. Guardian Fiends protect this Gate against any entry, slashing at the steady flow of shades descending into Duat. &quot;<br /> <br /> Does that mean that Duat doesn t want the Shades entering but they are simply too many to be stopped by the Guardians?<br /> OR<br /> Duat wants ONLY the shades to enter, but first they have to suffer by the Guardians</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mekharr guard things from all trespassers. Duat is, at least nominally, the domain of gods and greater beings. Its Guardians will attack anyone who gets too close to the thing they're protecting, and it's only through the invocation of Anpu that the Arisen get an exception.<br /> <br /> Shades aren't explicitly souls, they're drawn toward Duat (a storehouse of Sekhem, which they consume for power), and they don't have a free pass for the guards like mummies do; whether they're supposed to be there or not, they don't get the VIP treatment that would allow them to get through the gates unscathed.<br /> <br /> It's up to you what Duat's intentions are as regards shades in your game, but they have no top-level purpose in its functioning that would give the Mekharr at its gates an overarching reason <i>not</i> to treat them like any other intruders.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T07:00:45-07:00","id":1533378,"title":"","content":"I m searching the core book, but i can t find any source of bashing damage for Cults (the same for Krewes of Geist).<br /> What events could cause this kind of damage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-03-30T08:16:28-07:00","id":1533379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1533378#post1533378\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I m searching the core book, but i can t find any source of bashing damage for Cults (the same for Krewes of Geist).<br /> What events could cause this kind of damage?</div> </div> </div> </div>As described, bashing damage to an organization's health represents its membership being distracted from its principles and unity, in contrast to the direct prelude to mutiny that lethal damage represents or aggravated damage representing the group starting to lose membership (whether directly by them running away or spiritually by their having lost enough faith in the cause that they're only nominally part of the cult).<br /> <br /> Deviant's conspiracy systems put bashing damage as being caused by other conspiracies engaging in sabotage (which also consumes one of the conspiracy's conspiracy actions and is mainly contrasted against the lethal damage of direct war), with conspiracies attached to PC Devoted adding basic success on conspiracy surveillance rolls or a Devoted with the Devoted Authority or Devoted Control Condition blocking a conspiracy action relating to a Node they can influence.<br /> <br /> Basically, if it takes the cult's attention away from its Doctrines but doesn't actually make them doubt the cause or the commitment of its leadership, it's bashing damage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T03:47:50-07:00","id":1534581,"title":"","content":"I can t find in the core if Duat s fiends suffer from Essence bleed.<br /> Also, how do you can banish them back to Duat?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-23T06:21:02-07:00","id":1534583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1534581#post1534581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I can t find in the core if Duat s fiends suffer from Essence bleed.</div> </div> </div> </div>They function like Amkhata except where noted, meaning they lose their Rank in Essence per day that they're manifested, then start losing Corpus, then collapse back into Twilight with full Essence, whereupon they can gather Sekhem for another full-body emergence or use their Manifestations to act less dramatically.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, how do you can banish them back to Duat? </div> </div> </div>Same ways as normal ephemeral beings: deprive them of their sustaining Conditions until they run out of Essence and then destroy them, or use magic that banishes them (either them specifically or a category of being that includes them).<br /> <br /> Since every use of the Idol Manifestation creates the Open Condition at the depiction it transports them to and the fiend's other means of gaining Essence require its presence to work, this largely means destroying any depiction of the fiend, beating it down, and kicking it the rest of the way back with rituals or means of attack that hit beings in Twilight to kill it again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T08:13:11-07:00","id":1536255,"title":"","content":"Something been on my mind recently. Which immortals, if any, do you think can survive without food or drink? Logically I assume body thieves and Reborn need to cleave to the same necessities that the rest of us depend on to stay alive but I'm less certain about the others. A patchwork person or a visitor, for instance, I can see being argued either way. Curious how you would treat such in your games.<br /> <br /> (For the curious this question came up in part while I was working on a short story about a Warden (an immortal from the old World of Darkness Immortals rulebook who is essentially chosen by a location or city spirit to guard a certain locale and lives forever as long as they remain in that location- the story involved a remote location in a desert that lacked a easy source of drinkable water, which did not kill the Warden but made eternity extremely unpleasant as he still experienced thirst and hunger despite not technically needing food or drink to live).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T11:58:17-07:00","id":1536270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1536255#post1536255\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Something been on my mind recently. Which immortals, if any, do you think can survive without food or drink? Logically I assume body thieves and Reborn need to cleave to the same necessities that the rest of us depend on to stay alive but I'm less certain about the others. A patchwork person or a visitor, for instance, I can see being argued either way. Curious how you would treat such in your games.<br /> <br /> (For the curious this question came up in part while I was working on a short story about a Warden (an immortal from the old World of Darkness Immortals rulebook who is essentially chosen by a location or city spirit to guard a certain locale and lives forever as long as they remain in that location- the story involved a remote location in a desert that lacked a easy source of drinkable water, which did not kill the Warden but made eternity extremely unpleasant as he still experienced thirst and hunger despite not technically needing food or drink to live).</div> </div> </div> </div>With a steady source of willpower recovery an Eternal could shift the Condition caused by hunger and thirst on his Relic daily if you consider a day as one chapter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T13:38:15-07:00","id":1536271,"title":"","content":"True, although that's gonna be hell on the relic keeping him alive. But two follow up questions-<br /> <br /> 1. Does suffering from the condition or tilt inherently related to starvation/dehydration also imply they can or will die from it if something isn't done to alleviate the situation? <br /> <br /> 2. Do we actually HAVE an official tilt or condition related to starvation or dehydration? I can find ones for sickness, addiction, withdrawal, poisoning, exhaustion, etc but extreme hunger and thirst don't seem to be specifically included (assuming I didn't just miss them while paging through that section of the book).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-25T17:31:57-07:00","id":1536281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1536271#post1536271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. Do we actually HAVE an official tilt or condition related to starvation or dehydration? I can find ones for sickness, addiction, withdrawal, poisoning, exhaustion, etc but extreme hunger and thirst don't seem to be specifically included (assuming I didn't just miss them while paging through that section of the book).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a Condition, but the effects of Tier 2 of the Feast of Ashes Utterance use the same progression of unhealable bashing damage per day as described in the 1e nWoD corebook; considering that the effects described are knock-on consequences of being magically prevented from deriving nourishment from food I think it's reasonable to interpret everything in the Success text between the start of the bulleted list and the description of the Tier's effects on supernatural beings who don't eat normal food as the conventional effects of deprivation in 2e pending supersession by future material.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-05-26T05:31:52-07:00","id":1536291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1536271#post1536271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True, although that's gonna be hell on the relic keeping him alive. But two follow up questions-<br /> <br /> 1. Does suffering from the condition or tilt inherently related to starvation/dehydration also imply they can or will die from it if something isn't done to alleviate the situation?<br /> <br /> 2. Do we actually HAVE an official tilt or condition related to starvation or dehydration? I can find ones for sickness, addiction, withdrawal, poisoning, exhaustion, etc but extreme hunger and thirst don't seem to be specifically included (assuming I didn't just miss them while paging through that section of the book).</div> </div> </div> </div>At page 43 of the first dark eras book there is a chapter dedicated to starvation and thirst rules.<br /> They are no conditions it seems, but penalties associated to unhealing bashing damage, so probably no Immortal of mummy books could survive in this conditions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-06-02T01:35:50-07:00","id":1536691,"title":"","content":"In my games, I think I\u2019d have most of them suffer the penalties associated with starvation and dehydration but lack the mercy of a \u201cquick\u201d death from them. A starving Eternal could be miserably hungry for a very, very long time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T08:53:37-07:00","id":1538205,"title":"","content":"What book does Mummy interact or mention the Underworld from Geist?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-07T09:46:09-07:00","id":1538207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1538205#post1538205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What book does Mummy interact or mention the Underworld from Geist?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Mummy 2e corebook discusses the Underworld as the Caverns of Neter-Khertet.<br /> <br /> Basically, the Arisen can enter open Avernian Gates (and can open Avernian Gates using the Opener of the Way Sheut Affinity) and can explore the Upper Reaches. Anpu prevents them from crossing the Rivers into the Lower Mysteries and opens closed Gates for mummies attempting to leave the Underworld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T11:36:49-07:00","id":1538438,"title":"","content":"How does one determine what supernatural creatures and sorcerers a Mummy PC has in her Cult?<br /> <br /> Can Arisen serving different Judges pool Cult dots for one larger Cult? How does this work with the Judge's Doctrine?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-11T14:32:40-07:00","id":1538448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1538438#post1538438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one determine what supernatural creatures and sorcerers a Mummy PC has in her Cult?</div> </div> </div> </div>Declaratively. Mummy's mechanics for being a sorcerer or a supernatural creature exist largely independent of the cult systems apart from the systems for Investment and creating a Sadikh; the cult's mechanics largely serve as a measure of its ability to act as a force multiplier for the mummy's activities, while sorcerers and supernatural creatures are modeled as individual characters who have the relevant Scorpion Cult Initiation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can Arisen serving different Judges pool Cult dots for one larger Cult? How does this work with the Judge's Doctrine? </div> </div> </div>For simplicity's sake I would assume the answer is yes if everyone is okay with one of those Judges taking the Doctrine slot and potentially poaching the mummies who don't already serve them. Anything more complex should be sorted out by the troupe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-14T12:38:44-07:00","id":1538581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1538438#post1538438\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How does one determine what supernatural creatures and sorcerers a Mummy PC has in her Cult?<br /> <br /> Can Arisen serving different Judges pool Cult dots for one larger Cult? How does this work with the Judge's Doctrine?</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The presence or absence of immortals, sorcerers, or other supernatural creatures is up to each table to decide. I\u2019d base it on the needs of the story.<br /> 2. If mummies serving different Judges have the same Cult, you can either make one primary or have them share it equally. In the latter case, I\u2019d make the Judge\u2019s Doctrine one that combines the interests of all the Judges.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-07-23T21:42:29-07:00","id":1539130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1527755#post1527755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At page 122 it is written &quot;Once per scene, spending Pillar points raises a single Physical Attribute by a number of dots determined by a mummy\u2019s current Sekhem rating&quot;<br /> <br /> It says points, not a single point or one point.<br /> I think that the possible cases are:<br /> -you can spend multiple points on the same attribute cumulating the boost, but you must spend all the points in one turn<br /> -you can spend multiple points on the different physical attributes giving +4 to each, but you must spend all the points in one turn<br /> -points is a typo, it should be written point<br /> <br /> What do you think?</div> </div> </div> </div>My understanding is similar to the first option you mentioned, without the second. Having a physical attribute as favourite for one's decree gives another option of boosting that attribute for the scene. So, if Dexterity is one's favourite attribute, with Sekhem 10 one can spend 5 pillar points on turn 1 to increase Dexterity by 20, and 5 more (from one's defining pillar) on turn 2 to increase it further by 5, but no more. If base Dexterity was 10, that's a total maximum of 35 for the scene.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T12:30:50-07:00","id":1540058,"title":"","content":"Does anyone see a possible link between the Urfader in Denmark story (p.290, MtC2e) and the third origin story for the Gangrel (p.18, VtR2e)? Has either story been expanded upon anywhere? Has any connection between them been published?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T14:05:28-07:00","id":1540062,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1540058#post1540058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone see a possible link between the Urfader in Denmark story (p.290, MtC2e) and the third origin story for the Gangrel (p.18, VtR2e)? Has either story been expanded upon anywhere? Has any connection between them been published?</div> </div> </div> </div>None of Requiem's 2e's allegorical &quot;adjectivally ever after&quot; origin stories for the clans are expanded upon, and apart from Olivia Hill's Tokyo writeups there's little in the way of additional detail provided for any gameline's 2e sample settings outside the corebooks they're introduced in.<br /> <br /> The Urfader is a historic figure that is unambiguously one of the Arisen as far as the book is concerned, being notable for having been found in a bog with his remains in a state where the usual reactive awakening from disturbance has not occurred, possibly because of the binding ritual from his last observed Descent. The Gangrel's fairy tale origin concerns a man who was eaten by beasts and swallowed, then ejected, by the earth, in direct allusion to the clan's power over animals and ability to merge with soil; the general ambiguity of the story means it could concern a man becoming a vampire or a vampire becoming Gangrel, but Mummy 1e was specific that natural animals will not eat the corpse of an Arisen and 2e doesn't describe any abilities of the Arisen that remotely sound like &quot;control animals by feeding bits of yourself to them&quot; either generally or as things attributed to the Urfader.<br /> <br /> You could make something up to connect the two, but with the current text available it'd be quite a reach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T14:39:49-07:00","id":1540064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1540062#post1540062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">None of Requiem's 2e's allegorical &quot;adjectivally ever after&quot; origin stories for the clans are expanded upon, and apart from Olivia Hill's Tokyo writeups there's little in the way of additional detail provided for any gameline's 2e sample settings outside the corebooks they're introduced in.<br /> <br /> The Urfader is a historic figure that is unambiguously one of the Arisen as far as the book is concerned, being notable for having been found in a bog with his remains in a state where the usual reactive awakening from disturbance has not occurred, possibly because of the binding ritual from his last observed Descent. The Gangrel's fairy tale origin concerns a man who was eaten by beasts and swallowed, then ejected, by the earth, in direct allusion to the clan's power over animals and ability to merge with soil; the general ambiguity of the story means it could concern a man becoming a vampire or a vampire becoming Gangrel, but Mummy 1e was specific that natural animals will not eat the corpse of an Arisen and 2e doesn't describe any abilities of the Arisen that remotely sound like &quot;control animals by feeding bits of yourself to them&quot; either generally or as things attributed to the Urfader.<br /> <br /> You could make something up to connect the two, but with the current text available it'd be quite a reach.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are talking about the <i>fourth</i> Gangrel origin story in VtR2e. I'm talking about the third, the one starting with &quot;bogs&quot; (can't quote it at the moment).<br /> <br /> And yes, the Urfader is presented as an Arisen, so it's easier not to change that, therefore it would have to be the Gangrel side of the story to require some work in some direction, if one connects the two stories.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T17:20:52-07:00","id":1540068,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1540058#post1540058\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does anyone see a possible link between the Urfader in Denmark story (p.290, MtC2e) and the third origin story for the Gangrel (p.18, VtR2e)? Has either story been expanded upon anywhere? Has any connection between them been published?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Gangrel story is about something prehistoric from the ice ages settling underneath a bog, demanding sacrifices, and then disgorging one as a thing that feeds on death with bog water in its veins.<br /> The Urfader story is about a mummy who was conveyed to Denmark, and who seemingly ended one Descent through an attempted hanging and being left in a muddy tomb that was found in a bog.<br /> <br /> You could certainly decide to thread these together, but taken on their own merits, they don't share much beyond ancient unliving things being dredged from bogs. The &quot;ice sarcophagus&quot; in the Gangrel story is a figure of speech, not a literal sarcophagus\u2014and besides, Urfader wasn't preserved in ice anyway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-08T23:55:26-07:00","id":1540075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1540068#post1540068\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Gangrel story is about something prehistoric from the ice ages settling underneath a bog, demanding sacrifices, and then disgorging one as a thing that feeds on death with bog water in its veins.<br /> The Urfader story is about a mummy who was conveyed to Denmark, and who seemingly ended one Descent through an attempted hanging and being left in a muddy tomb that was found in a bog.<br /> <br /> You could certainly decide to thread these together, but taken on their own merits, they don't share much beyond ancient unliving things being dredged from bogs. The &quot;ice sarcophagus&quot; in the Gangrel story is a figure of speech, not a literal sarcophagus\u2014and besides, Urfader wasn't preserved in ice anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Urfader story also involves sacrifice, to an unknown end, <i>maybe</i> to help end Urfader's Descent. <br /> <br /> Taken on their own merit, they are indeed two stories of two unliving beings in bogs. There are plenty of bogs and bog bodies in Northern Europe, so they could be unrelated. But it may he interesting to speculate that they are related.<br /> <br /> Bogs may form from drained lakes created by glaciers, so the fact that Urfader wasn't preserved in ice isn't necessarily the case: he may have been and then the place became a bog over time. More importantly, it's not known how Urfader got to Denmark, only that three North African men (who may or may not have brought him there) woke him up, were killed, villages were attacked, and Urfader's Descent ended with him having a noose around his neck and 30 people died in a ritual fashion, presumably at that time (the book doesn't specify that the scientific dating of Urfader's remains corresponds to that of the 30 sacrifices, but it's implied since it's hypothesized they died in an attempt to end the mummy's Descent).<br /> There's also the mystery of why Urfader has slept through the Sothic Turns.<br /> <br /> I think it's unlikely that the Su-Menent, given their powers, would misidentify a mummy, so I keep the idea that Urfader is indeed an Arisen. It makes sense also with the Sekhem and cultist manipulation that are part of his story. But maybe the Sekhem-rich bog has not only produced human cultists over the ages. Maybe at some point it produced something else. Maybe, given the non-uniform origins of the vampire clans, it produced that &quot;first bog body&quot; that only death can nourish, and &quot;preserves some of the dead it swallows, pickling the corpses with the black bog water in its veins.&quot;<br /> <br /> Maybe the Sekhem attracted Shades on the Neter-Khertet side of the bog. Maybe something happened there, perhaps with a complicit Urfader, to produce something new, so linked to the ground that it can melt into it and grant this ability to others by sharing its blood - preserving them forever (which makes me also think of Resilience).<br /> <br /> Maybe Urfader never awoke in the hanged body during the Sothic Turns because he found another way to return, perhaps having invested the first bog body with the Rite of Investment before that body's death, and corrupting it with the influence of the Shades. Basically an invested new vampire then turned into Urfader's body and the first Gangrel. A terrifying vampire-mummy hybrid produced by interaction with the mysterious Shades.<br /> <br /> Or maybe Urfader didn't awake because he traded Sekhem to the Shades for whatever allowed the creation of an Invested new vampire (this time not housing Urfader's soul), so the Shades have been suckling Sekhem on the Neter-Khertet side of the bog, slowing Urfader's resurrection compared to other mummies.<br /> <br /> Last but not least, considering the <i>possibility </i>that a mummy might descend even before the foundation of Irem due to their weird relationship to Time, Urfader might have gotten into the ice that then turned into a lake that then turned into a bog even during or at the beginning of the last Ice Age. But I don't see much point in this from a narrative point of view, it's just weird and quirky, while positing an Arisen-related Gangrel clan origin allows for a meaningful interaction between some Scandinavian Gangrel and Urfader's cultists when he wakes up, bringing an unexpected vampire twist to the stories of the Scandinavian Arisen.<br /> <br /> None of this is necessary - they can be two unrelated story. But the fun thing about CoD is having all these story hooks and unclear origins of supernatural creatures to be able to play around with it all.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T16:39:25-07:00","id":1540187,"title":"","content":"When was Irem founded? And when did it fall?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T18:49:25-07:00","id":1540191,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1540187#post1540187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When was Irem founded? And when did it fall?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Sothic Turn Zero,&quot; when the Arisen were made, is approximately 3832 BCE, four 1461-year Sothic Turns before Mummy's original release year of 2012 (itself core to a lot of apocalyptic beliefs at the time).<br /> <br /> 1e notes that most of the Arisen were created on or within a century of Sothis (aka the Dog Star Sirius) naturally appearing with the first dawn of the Ancient Egyptian year, and obviously no new Arisen were being created after the fall of the Nameless Empire, but we do not otherwise have a concrete timeline for one of the central mysteries of the game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T20:40:19-07:00","id":1540193,"title":"","content":"I think when Irem end is before Egypt civilization start so, maybe after they make the Arisen or at least some years after for most of the Empire thing to dissappear. <br /> Did Irem exist before the Sundering? If not then maybe it start around 4000 BCE.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28270-yumlum","name":"Yumlum","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-11T21:14:07-07:00","id":1540195,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yumlum</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1540193#post1540193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think when Irem end is before Egypt civilization start so, maybe after they make the Arisen or at least some years after for most of the Empire thing to dissappear.<br /> Did Irem exist before the Sundering? If not then maybe it start around 4000 BCE.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sundered World takes place roughly another Sothic Turn prior to the Rite of Return, and the sidebar in that chapter alluding to what's going on with other gameline-level monsters in that Dark Era (in the case of The Sundered World, everything that isn't mages and werewolves) discusses the scheming of material animal-headed beings &quot;far across the sea to the South&quot; of the Vinca culture's Southeastern European location. What Mummy presents of Irem's interaction with the Shadow is firmly unconcerned with the Border Marches as a prehistoric phenomenon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T01:33:27-07:00","id":1540196,"title":"","content":"What options do Deceived PCs have with 2E rules to pretend to belong to another guild when dealing with other Arisen, including powers to hide their true nature from others and power others may have to uncover it? I'm considering whether to allow players to play Deceived characters in a meret loosely loyal to the Judges (though one player already has an Aspiration to take the Judges' place, but we're going to explore that in later chronicles). Character options already include the other minor guilds and mortal, immortal and ephemeral cultists. I'm only unsure about the Deceived.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-12T18:03:31-07:00","id":1540248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1540195#post1540195\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Sundered World takes place roughly another Sothic Turn prior to the Rite of Return, and the sidebar in that chapter alluding to what's going on with other gameline-level monsters in that Dark Era (in the case of The Sundered World, everything that isn't mages and werewolves) discusses the scheming of material animal-headed beings &quot;far across the sea to the South&quot; of the Vinca culture's Southeastern European location. What Mummy presents of Irem's interaction with the Shadow is firmly unconcerned with the Border Marches as a prehistoric phenomenon.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the timeline would seem to be: <br /> <br /> 6754 BCE: previous Sothic Turn, maybe when Aset was fed Azar's parts and sacrificed? Just including it in case someone has some event to pin on it.<br /> 5293 BCE: The Sundered World period Sothic Turn<br /> 3832 BCE: the Rite of Return<br /> 2371 BCE: first Arisen Sothic Turn<br /> 910 BCE, 551 CE, 2012 CE: other Sothic Turns","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-13T16:53:11-07:00","id":1540314,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1540248#post1540248\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the timeline would seem to be:<br /> <br /> 6754 BCE: previous Sothic Turn, maybe when Aset was fed Azar's parts and sacrificed? Just including it in case someone has some event to pin on it.<br /> 5293 BCE: The Sundered World period Sothic Turn<br /> 3832 BCE: the Rite of Return<br /> 2371 BCE: first Arisen Sothic Turn<br /> 910 BCE, 551 CE, 2012 CE: other Sothic Turns</div> </div> </div> </div>We can ignore the 6754 BCE date, since MtC 2e p.63 says that &quot;over 6000 years ago&quot; (that's somewhere before 4000 BCE) the Shan'iatu had not appeared yet. Unless we take that to mean - oddly - any time before 4000 BCE, even 10000 BCE, the Shan'iatu appeared somewhere between 4999 and 4001 BCE (let's give that &quot;over&quot; an arbitrary broad value between 1 and 999 years, so it's over 6000 but not 7000 - I'm obviously not counting the years from 2000 CE to the book's publication, we're not trying to be accurate here).<br /> Interestingly, if the Rite of Return was in 3832, it means the Nameles Empire lasted at best a few centuries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-14T17:30:38-07:00","id":1540395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1540196#post1540196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What options do Deceived PCs have with 2E rules to pretend to belong to another guild when dealing with other Arisen, including powers to hide their true nature from others and power others may have to uncover it? I'm considering whether to allow players to play Deceived characters in a meret loosely loyal to the Judges (though one player already has an Aspiration to take the Judges' place, but we're going to explore that in later chronicles). Character options already include the other minor guilds and mortal, immortal and ephemeral cultists. I'm only unsure about the Deceived.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just read their Affinities in Book of Lasting Death, which directly answers my question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T06:09:00-07:00","id":1540427,"title":"","content":"Can Sadikhs take Supernatural merits or are they considered as having a supernatural template and therefore those merits are off for them?<br /> <br /> EDIT/UPDATE: the Timeless Merit <i>Supernatural Resistance</i> (MtC2e, p.108) seems to suggest Sadikhs can use Supernatural Merits, just like Immortals.<br /> <br /> If creating a Sadikh character, do we follow the Arisen creation rules as a basis, like we do for Immortals, which means getting 10 Experience, or do we follow the mortal creation rules from Chronicles of Darkness, namely no Experience at start? Same question for mortal sorcerers and Witnesses in a cult.<br /> <br /> EDIT/UPDATE: apparently it's up to the ST, since MtC2e says one can create cultists from either that book (which appears to give 10 Experience to new characters) or the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook (which doesn't give Experience). Ephemeral cultists get no Experience at start, as per BoLD pp.46-47. On the one side, it makes sense for Arisen, Sadikhs and Immortals to start with more Experience given their longevity. On the other, given the already large power gap before these character types, I fear a mixed meret would be heavily imbalanced if mortal and ephemeral cultists had zero Experience while Arisen and Immortals had 10 on top of their other advantages. Add to that that mortals created from the Chronicles of Darkness Rulebook also start with 7 dots of Merits instead of 10. I think it's better for balance's sake to give all cultists 10 dots of Merits and 10 Experience, to show that MtC is a game on a higher power level than others anyway.<br /> <br /> Is there any mechanical difference I may have missed between Balance/Burden and Virtue/Vice or have the Anchors just been renamed for thematic reasons?<br /> <br /> EDIT/UPDATE: apparently it's mostly a thematic change, as cultists can choose Virtue/Vice from the Balance/Burden list.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":16965,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","user":"Hermeticus","date":". 08-15-2024, 12:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-15T18:14:27-07:00","id":1540486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1540427#post1540427\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any mechanical difference I may have missed between Balance/Burden and Virtue/Vice or have the Anchors just been renamed for thematic reasons?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can recover one Willpower once per scene by indulging your Vice in a minor way. You can recover all Willpower once per session by acting out your Virtue in a major, dramatic way.<br /> <br /> Both Balance and Burden can recover Willpower in <i>both</i> ways, one Willpower for a minor invocation or all Willpower through a major, dramatic embodiment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T10:48:44-07:00","id":1540517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1540314#post1540314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly, if the Rite of Return was in 3832, it means the Nameles Empire lasted at best a few centuries.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm inclined to assume that in any case. I think it makes a lot more sense with the general timeline around its major events and avoiding some excessively high fantasy vibe of &quot;civilization that lasts for millenia with barely any cultural or aesthetic changes&quot;. <br /> <br /> Besides, it matches up with actual Egyptian history, where any given Kingdom or Intermediate period tended to last something like four or five hundred years. I'd assume Irem got by with about half of that given the priorities of the beings ruling it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T11:15:22-07:00","id":1540521,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1540517#post1540517\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm inclined to assume that in any case. I think it makes a lot more sense with the general timeline around its major events and avoiding some excessively high fantasy vibe of &quot;civilization that lasts for millenia with barely any cultural or aesthetic changes&quot;.<br /> <br /> Besides, it matches up with actual Egyptian history, where any given Kingdom or Intermediate period tended to last something like four or five hundred years. I'd assume Irem got by with about half of that given the priorities of the beings ruling it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's also notable that the fiction from Book of the Deceived suggests pretty directly that part of the reason the Shan'iatu made the decision to sacrifice the Empire was because of the burgeoning mortality of their earthly forms \u2014 one can certainly be immortal and still make plans to cheat their way into the afterlife, but decrepitude and the specter of death without promise of anything after definitely adds some pressure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-08-16T16:50:33-07:00","id":1540533,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1540521#post1540521\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also notable that the fiction from Book of the Deceived suggests pretty directly that part of the reason the Shan'iatu made the decision to sacrifice the Empire was because of the burgeoning mortality of their earthly forms \u2014 one can certainly be immortal and still make plans to cheat their way into the afterlife, but decrepitude and the specter of death without promise of anything after definitely adds some pressure.</div> </div> </div> </div>One wonders whether, had they been just a little more patient, their beings would have changed to the point of having souls and being able to travel to Duat and A\u2019aru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T00:30:54-07:00","id":1541766,"title":"","content":"Do ephemeral cultists get access to the master's decree affinities and/or Utterances like mortal/Sadikh/sorcerer/immortal cultists? I don't think so based on the text in Book of Lasting Death, which gives them separate benefits unique to each ephemeral type instead, but I'm asking in case I missed something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T00:38:00-07:00","id":1541768,"title":"","content":"The Rite of Investment gives mortals access to their master's decree Affinities (plural). Does that mean the bonus Affinity linked to each decree + the Soul Affinities linked to the same Pillar as the decree?<br /> <br /> Ex.: Does an Ashem Arisen master give his mortal Inheritors access to Jackal's Shade plus any Sheut Affinity he knows? Instead, Sadikh Inheritors get access to all the master's Soul Affinities + the bonus Affinity of the master's decree, while Immortals get the decree bonus Affinity, the Soul Affinities for the same Pillar, and the first level Utterances. Is this correct?<br /> <br /> I find it a bit odd, first because of how it's phrased (&quot;Mortal Decree: Invested mortals may use their master\u2019s decree Affinities.&quot; p.204) and second because which Pillar point is invested seems irrelevant to the Affinities gained. The Ashem Arisen above maybe invests a point of Ba, not Sheut, in the Inheritor, yet the Inheritor gets Jackal's Shade and the Sheut Affinities, not the Ba ones, known to the master (and in theory, having no dot in Sheut, had he been an Arisen he would not have qualified for Sheut Affinities). What am I missing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T01:16:42-07:00","id":1541769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1541766#post1541766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do ephemeral cultists get access to the master's decree affinities and/or Utterances like mortal/Sadikh/sorcerer/immortal cultists? I don't think so based on the text in Book of Lasting Death, which gives them separate benefits unique to each ephemeral type instead, but I'm asking in case I missed something.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadikh get the Soul Affinities. Immortals get the tier 1 Utterances. Ephemeral beings are not sadikh or immortals.<br /> <br /> The decree Affinity is a grey area in that the non-mortal invested do all get the decree Affinity in addition to their unique benefits. I don't think it would break anything if you decided to keep this pattern and give the ephemeral beings the decree Affinity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1541768#post1541768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rite of Investment gives mortals access to their master's decree Affinities (plural). Does that mean the bonus Affinity linked to each decree + the Soul Affinities linked to the same Pillar as the decree?<br /> <br /> Ex.: Does an Ashem Arisen master give his mortal Inheritors access to Jackal's Shade plus any Sheut Affinity he knows? Instead, Sadikh Inheritors get access to all the master's Soul Affinities + the bonus Affinity of the master's decree, while Immortals get the decree bonus Affinity, the Soul Affinities for the same Pillar, and the first level Utterances. Is this correct?<br /> <br /> I find it a bit odd, first because of how it's phrased (&quot;Mortal Decree: Invested mortals may use their master\u2019s decree Affinities.&quot; p.204) and second because which Pillar point is invested seems irrelevant to the Affinities gained. The Ashem Arisen above maybe invests a point of Ba, not Sheut, in the Inheritor, yet the Inheritor gets Jackal's Shade and the Sheut Affinities, not the Ba ones, known to the master (and in theory, having no dot in Sheut, had he been an Arisen he would not have qualified for Sheut Affinities). What am I missing?</div> </div> </div> </div>I simply read this as an awkward plural that would have read more clearly as <i>&quot;masters'</i> decree Affinities.&quot; It's plural because the masters are plural because the inheritors are plural, it's speaking of the classes of people as a whole. An individual invested mortal may use his master's decree Affinity. Each mummy only has one decree Affinity to give.<br /> I don't know if this is the written intent. &quot;Decree Affinity&quot; doesn't appear to be a clearly defined category like &quot;Soul Affinity&quot; is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-09T05:53:03-07:00","id":1541774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1541769#post1541769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Sadikh get the Soul Affinities. Immortals get the tier 1 Utterances. Ephemeral beings are not sadikh or immortals.<br /> <br /> The decree Affinity is a grey area in that the non-mortal invested do all get the decree Affinity in addition to their unique benefits. I don't think it would break anything if you decided to keep this pattern and give the ephemeral beings the decree Affinity.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I simply read this as an awkward plural that would have read more clearly as <i>&quot;masters'</i> decree Affinities.&quot; It's plural because the masters are plural because the inheritors are plural, it's speaking of the classes of people as a whole. An individual invested mortal may use his master's decree Affinity. Each mummy only has one decree Affinity to give.<br /> I don't know if this is the written intent. &quot;Decree Affinity&quot; doesn't appear to be a clearly defined category like &quot;Soul Affinity&quot; is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. I get your angle.<br /> A related issue is Inheritors of Akhem-Urtu, Kher-Minu and Maar-Kherit: they don't have a decree, hence they should not have a decree Affinity. They do have a bonus Affinity, a defining Pillar and a Favoured Attribute though.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T04:00:03-07:00","id":1542037,"title":"","content":"After a successful use of Tier 1 WORDS OF DEAD DOMINION, <br /> the target ghost is instantly trasported or must walk to the mummy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-09-13T04:44:56-07:00","id":1542040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1542037#post1542037\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After a successful use of Tier 1 WORDS OF DEAD DOMINION,<br /> the target ghost is instantly trasported or must walk to the mummy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the range constraints of Anchors and the ability to make the ghost immediately Materialize, I'd say they're immediately transported there (entering a Clash of Wills if some supernatural effect would directly keep them from leaving their location as usual for conflicting supernatural powers).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T02:59:38-07:00","id":1543963,"title":"","content":"What do new mummy characters (Memory 3) know exactly of the game's lore after they've recovered from the first scene post-awakening? I can't seem to get a clear picture from MtC2E, and I'm struggling to explain it to my players.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T03:04:13-07:00","id":1543964,"title":"","content":"Kher-Minu and Maar-Kherit mummies don't go into henet like other Arisen. How does their going through multiple Descents and losing and gaining Memory work for them? What about the issue of Descents not being in chronological order?<br /> For example, how should one handle a new Kher-Minu or Maar-Kherit mummy character starting a chronicle in the 21st century?<br /> <br /> Kher-Minu stay trapped in stone, but what happens to Maar-Kherit in between Descents?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T03:05:00-07:00","id":1543965,"title":"","content":"How close must one get to a Maar-Kherit to be affected by their miasma?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T03:09:56-07:00","id":1543966,"title":"","content":"Seba, Neoliths, Ankhs: the chosen vessels of Akhem-Urtu, Kher-Minu and Maar-Kherit in MtC2E. <br /> <br /> Any suggestion for what they do and how they work as relics, since I haven't found a Second Edition explanation of them unlike the relics of the other guilds?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T06:20:33-07:00","id":1543977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1543963#post1543963\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What do new mummy characters (Memory 3) know exactly of the game's lore after they've recovered from the first scene post-awakening? I can't seem to get a clear picture from MtC2E, and I'm struggling to explain it to my players.</div> </div> </div> </div>They know their name, decree, and guild, that they're from the Nameless Empire, and a sufficiently little about Irem that the line between personal experience and academic knowledge is blurry. The breakdown from 1e still largely holds.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1543964#post1543964\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kher-Minu and Maar-Kherit mummies don't go into henet like other Arisen. How does their going through multiple Descents and losing and gaining Memory work for them? What about the issue of Descents not being in chronological order?<br /> For example, how should one handle a new Kher-Minu or Maar-Kherit mummy character starting a chronicle in the 21st century?<br /> <br /> Kher-Minu stay trapped in stone, but what happens to Maar-Kherit in between Descents?</div> </div> </div> </div>There is nothing stating that the Maar-Kherit don't go into henet like most other mummies, and the fact that they get the same free Utterance as standard Arisen suggests that they work the same way while they're out.<br /> <br /> The Kher-Minu's status as tomb guardians combined with their small numbers suggests if you want to play one who is just now awakening in the modern day you are best served treating them as having been subject to one of those quirks of the setting that made them unable to be roused during the preceding millennia. Otherwise, they work the same as they would if you were playing a regular Arisen with no out-of-order Descents.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1543965#post1543965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How close must one get to a Maar-Kherit to be affected by their miasma?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a side-effect of their Sybaris. The causes of Sybaris are described on page 203.\u200b","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83e\udd70","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-16T08:44:06-07:00","id":1543989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1543977#post1543977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They know their name, decree, and guild, that they're from the Nameless Empire, and a sufficiently little about Irem that the line between personal experience and academic knowledge is blurry. The breakdown from 1e still largely holds.<br /> <br /> There is nothing stating that the Maar-Kherit don't go into henet like most other mummies, and the fact that they get the same free Utterance as standard Arisen suggests that they work the same way while they're out.<br /> <br /> The Kher-Minu's status as tomb guardians combined with their small numbers suggests if you want to play one who is just now awakening in the modern day you are best served treating them as having been subject to one of those quirks of the setting that made them unable to be roused during the preceding millennia. Otherwise, they work the same as they would if you were playing a regular Arisen with no out-of-order Descents.<br /> <br /> It's a side-effect of their Sybaris. The causes of Sybaris are described on page 203.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, that helps a lot!<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-17T13:36:23-07:00","id":1544134,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1543977#post1543977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They know their name, decree, and guild, that they're from the Nameless Empire, and a sufficiently little about Irem that the line between personal experience and academic knowledge is blurry. The breakdown from 1e still largely holds.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do they know what the other guilds are? What about the minor guilds? At least two of them used to be major (Akhem-Urtu, Wadjet-Itja) in Irem.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T15:29:56-07:00","id":1544432,"title":"","content":"For Conditions that lists &quot;violating their Judge\u2019s laws&quot; as a resolution, it means every act that causes a Descent roll (as raising Memory score) or the specific transgression of the judge (blasphemous act for Kenemti)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-21T16:17:25-07:00","id":1544435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1544432#post1544432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Conditions that lists &quot;violating their Judge\u2019s laws&quot; as a resolution, it means every act that causes a Descent roll (as raising Memory score) or the specific transgression of the judge (blasphemous act for Kenemti)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Presumably anything that could trigger an emanation or otherwise violate the Doctrine of a cult dedicated to that Judge, particularly given that the only Condition with that resolution criteria is Auspicious Descent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T14:00:02-07:00","id":1544496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1541769#post1541769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I simply read this as an awkward plural that would have read more clearly as <i>&quot;masters'</i> decree Affinities.&quot; It's plural because the masters are plural because the inheritors are plural, it's speaking of the classes of people as a whole. An individual invested mortal may use his master's decree Affinity. Each mummy only has one decree Affinity to give.<br /> I don't know if this is the written intent. &quot;Decree Affinity&quot; doesn't appear to be a clearly defined category like &quot;Soul Affinity&quot; is.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right. <i>Blessed is the God-King</i>, Tier 3, p.135:<br /> <br /> <i>The Arisen may choose one of her Soul Affinities linked to her defining Pillar, allowing the Inheritors to benefit from it as if they possessed it while transformed</i>.<br /> <br /> Therefore Inheritors do not have by default access to the Soul Affinities linked to the defining Pillar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-11-14T09:18:20-08:00","id":1545855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1543966#post1543966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seba, Neoliths, Ankhs: the chosen vessels of Akhem-Urtu, Kher-Minu and Maar-Kherit in MtC2E.<br /> <br /> Any suggestion for what they do and how they work as relics, since I haven't found a Second Edition explanation of them unlike the relics of the other guilds?</div> </div> </div> </div>The only 2E information on them are in the Book of Lasting Death, and sadly there\u2019s not much there. At some point, I should make myself buckle down and write something about them for the Vault, but as it stands right now, those are pretty open design space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Jason Ross Inczauskis</b>, Freelance Writer<br /> Projects: <i>Dark Eras 2</i>, <i>Mummy: The Curse 2e, Book of Lasting Death, DtR The Clades Companion, Pirates of Pugmire,</i> <i>They Came From Beyond the Grave!, </i><i>TC Aeon: Mission Statements</i>, <i>TC In Media Res,</i> <i>DtD Night Horrors: Enemy Action,</i> <i>C20 Anthology of Dreams</i><br /> Masculine pronouns preferred.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/309-white-oak-dragon","name":"White Oak Dragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar309_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-20T18:10:59-07:00","id":1551793,"title":"","content":"This is a first edition heavy question, so be warned. Also something more about interpretation than something number crunchy. Bear with me.<br /> <br /> In the first edition Core book, specifically in the flavor text story which begins the Storyteller's section we get a series of letters exchange between some guy named Wodehouse (still a little disappointed we never returned to who this character and their agenda were, but I'm digressing). They capture a mummy...maybe a Shuankhsen, named Merit. She explains some things about Irem before going into a death cycle. One thing she mentions is something the Shan'iatu found out in the Sahara desert (which if your keeping score is the opposite direction from where Ubar disappeared so unrelated to that city despite its own important connections to the Rite of Return. She's vague about what exactly they found- a black cube, a dead god...but she personally thinks it was a sacred place 'like a mouth, with lips open to the sky and a stomach filled with Sekhem' to paraphrase. Very obvious Devourer overtones there....<br /> <br /> Now fast forward to Book of the Deceived. Their history section describes in first person an encounter in Neter-Khertet where one of the Shan'iatu is drawn to a 'pit of corruption' where he makes a sacrifice and is able to journey deep into Duat (I presume) and has a conversation with the Devourer. Starts them down the road to killing Osiris and founding Irem. <br /> <br /> Anyway, do you interpret these two things to be the same? Is there a big scary demon portal out in the western desert with a direct line straight to the Devourer?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-06-20T20:15:37-07:00","id":1551797,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1551793#post1551793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, do you interpret these two things to be the same? Is there a big scary demon portal out in the western desert with a direct line straight to the Devourer?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this is in the same genre of conflicting reports as Hunter and Vampire have for the events surrounding the Cult of Set and the Cult of the Phoenix becoming vampires and the Ascending Ones respectively; the Deceived narrator describes the place they visit in their dream as a wound in the world made by Ammut, a sign of her hunger and a chasm into nothingness, and Menat's account is of things she's heard, hence the multiple possible things the Shan'iatu's catalyst could have been.<br /> <br /> We know Ammut is limited by the current state of the world in how strongly she can exert her will compared to back in mythic prehistory and that she can be spoken to directly in Duat, and Mummy is far from the first Chronicles gameline to describe paths into Hell as &quot;wounds,&quot; but considering Menat's account exists partially as a demonstration of the effects of The Silence amid large chunks of information (and a probable attempt at preparing to bodyjack Collins' corpse by exhausting her Sekhem) I'd be suspicious of any information given to mortals that points them toward &quot;a gullet of sweet Sekhem and the holiest of stomachs in wait below&quot; \u2014 to borrow a term of analysis once used to describe the clanbooks in Vampire, it smacks of history told &quot;not to inform the listener, but to manipulate.&quot;<br /> <br /> That being said, the tenor of Menat's other examples is rather more material than a chasm in Twilight and a twisty route to Duat, so unless one were to lean hard into the metaphorical description of her &quot;place of power&quot; theory I wouldn't interpret the two as the same thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-26T15:26:28-07:00","id":1552657,"title":"","content":"I think I'll have a lot of those, because it'll take time before I can read any supplements and Mummy Core seems very good at throwing concepts, but never explaining them as well as it should (or in the best places).<br /> <br /> What exactly is Neter-Khertet? Is it a superposition over Twilight, a distinct Twilight, or another realm that links to Twilight? If it is a superposition over Twilight, how does its inhabitants hide there without appearing in normal Deathly Twilight?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-26T17:29:20-07:00","id":1552660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552657#post1552657\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What exactly is Neter-Khertet? Is it a superposition over Twilight, a distinct Twilight, or another realm that links to Twilight? If it is a superposition over Twilight, how does its inhabitants hide there without appearing in normal Deathly Twilight?</div> </div> </div> </div>Neter-Khertet is deathly Twilight with a few additional things the Arisen can see due to their ability to perceive Sekhem. In Iremic thought it's considered another realm, but &quot;a frame of reference that is shared by its denizens that doesn't naturally interact with the material world&quot; and &quot;a separate world whose denizens can sometimes interact with the material world&quot; are very loosely different; there's a sidebar in the Dark Eras Companion (p127) that discusses this a bit.<br /> <br /> As for how their inhabitants hide there without appearing in normal deathly Twilight, the main methodology is the Ashen Storm, an eternal cloud of sand and funeral ash that whirls through the &quot;depths&quot; of Neter-Khertet that can be used to conceal anyone who's aware of it with a basic Stealth roll as though they were in shadows; characters who can perceive deathly Twilight can try to pierce the concealment with a simple Perception roll, but the Storm applies the Sandstorm Tilt, which penalizes Perception rolls more the further away whatever you're looking for is. Most of the things in deathly Twilight that aren't ghosts, like Amkhata, fiends and shades commonly use this tactic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-26T20:33:01-07:00","id":1552667,"title":"","content":"That still makes it hard to understand the difference between Neter-Khertet and &quot;normal&quot; deathly Twilight.<br /> <br /> Like: do ghosts usually perceive Neter-Khertet? If not, how do Shades and Amkhata prey on them?<br /> <br /> If a denizen of Neter-Khertet isn't hiding in the Ashen Storm at the moment, do they become visible for everyone that can perceive <b>only</b> &quot;normal&quot; deathly Twilight?<br /> <br /> Sometimes it seems the only distinction is that whomever perceives Neter-Khertet can notice the Ashen Storm, the two mountains and the gates (to whatever, because while the book eventually says the western mountain has a gate to Duat, it never states anything about the other gates seen in Neter-Khertet).<br /> <br /> Other times it seems that Shades, Fiends and Amkhata do not really inhabit &quot;normal&quot; deathly Twilight at all, only Neter-Khertet.<br /> <br /> Do ghosts perceive Neter-Khertet? Some of them? None of them?<br /> <br /> And what about the Caves? They're described as Avernian Gates, but for some reason they're not called Avernian Gates even though the book does have one or two references to Avernian Gates. Is interacting with an Avernian Gate from Neter-Khertet in any way distinct from interacting with it from regular Twilight or Materialized?<br /> <br /> Just one more unrelated question about Amkhata: after all, they exist before materializing for the first time? In many sections their description indicates they usually begin existence when large quantities of Sekhem are spilled, and remain in Neter-Khertet for most of the time. But their summon rules work as if they only took form when they're given animal parts, and it's not in a sense that the correct animals must be sacrificed, but as if the summoner built the beast.<br /> <br /> What does a never-summoned-before Amkhata looks like? And where does summoned Amkhata come from?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T10:50:40-07:00","id":1552670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552667#post1552667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like: do ghosts usually perceive Neter-Khertet? If not, how do Shades and Amkhata prey on them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shades and Amkhata can be seen by ghosts when they are not hidden. As largely non-communicative shadow-beings and hungry predators, they have ample reason to hide.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If a denizen of Neter-Khertet isn't hiding in the Ashen Storm at the moment, do they become visible for everyone that can perceive <b>only</b> &quot;normal&quot; deathly Twilight? </div> </div> </div>They're not the mountains, so yes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sometimes it seems the only distinction is that whomever perceives Neter-Khertet can notice the Ashen Storm, the two mountains and the gates (to whatever, because while the book eventually says the western mountain has a gate to Duat, it never states anything about the other gates seen in Neter-Khertet). </div> </div> </div>The other akhet is the one mummies go to to return to their remains while undergoing a death cycle. The routing is ostensibly through a metaphysical axis that doesn't correspond to earthly geography, given that you can simply reach them by going far enough to the west or east.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Other times it seems that Shades, Fiends and Amkhata do not really inhabit &quot;normal&quot; deathly Twilight at all, only Neter-Khertet.<br /> <br /> Do ghosts perceive Neter-Khertet? Some of them? None of them? </div> </div> </div>The vast and overwhelming majority of ghosts are not mobile enough to be concerned about the wilderness and tomb-depths of deathly Twilight, but apart from the Storm and more conventional methods of stealth there isn't anything preventing them from seeing the shadow-people and Franken-beasts and escaped hellspawn that the Arisen framework brings to the table. Predation upon their Anchored neighbors is also a handy justification for Tombs and other storehouses of vessels not being full of ghosts.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And what about the Caves? They're described as Avernian Gates, but for some reason they're not called Avernian Gates even though the book does have one or two references to Avernian Gates. Is interacting with an Avernian Gate from Neter-Khertet in any way distinct from interacting with it from regular Twilight or Materialized? </div> </div> </div>Avernian Gates are Twilight phenomena that cannot be interacted with from the material world without Opening them and passageways to the Caverns are the same phenomenon. The Caverns themselves are simply the Upper Reaches of the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just one more unrelated question about Amkhata: after all, they exist before materializing for the first time? In many sections their description indicates they usually begin existence when large quantities of Sekhem are spilled, and remain in Neter-Khertet for most of the time. But their summon rules work as if they only took form when they're given animal parts, and it's not in a sense that the correct animals must be sacrificed, but as if the summoner built the beast.<br /> <br /> What does a never-summoned-before Amkhata looks like? And where does summoned Amkhata come from? </div> </div> </div>The rules for summoning Amkhata don't involve the summoner designing the creature in question; Amkhata nest in relatively safe locations and draw their original forms from whatever dead sacred creatures were nearby when they were created by the spilling of Sekhem, which summoners might leverage to spawn a weak new Amkhat or draw the attention of an existing one. From there, they use the Essence they gain from Sekhem sources to sustain their manifestations and develop more Parts and Dread Powers as they rise in Rank from consuming more powerful beings in Neter-Khertet (presumably taking cues from their prey as an ostensibly guideline for how their forms develop).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T18:16:50-07:00","id":1552677,"title":"","content":"Is there any concrete information on <b>A'aru</b>?<br /> <br /> What is <b>Apotheosis</b>? I didn't really got what it is meant to represent in the fiction, even as a legend, despite having rules for it.<br /> <br /> Are there rules for the other Minor Guilds besides the Shuankhsen? Are there better rules for the Shuankhsen (because I'm under the impression that they're actually pretty weak for Mummies)?<br /> <br /> Decrees are another thing that I didn't quite understood what they are within the fiction. They're related to an aspect of the soul, but what did the Arisen declared, exactly, to the Judges?<br /> <br /> Several times the book aludes to mummies whose Semektet have wildly different durations, from a single day to several decades, <b>by design of their Judges</b>, but outside the Conditions <i>Graceful</i>, <i>Auspicious</i> and <i>Precipitous Descent</i>, which are quite limited in this effect, the rules don't really back this up all that much. Is there any additional rule, or something I didn't notice, that can <u>significantly</u> change the frequency of Descent Rolls?<br /> <br /> The rules from the old <i><b>Immortals</b></i> book are compatible with Mummies (I already know the Endless are basically the same in the fiction, with simplified versions of the original rules, I just want to know if re-reading that book will add something of value)?<br /> <br /> Language-wise, is there any real distinction between Iremic and various-eras Egyptian, aside random proper names? Not a complaint, just a curiosity, I generally enjoy reading Egyptian. And that does mean, curiously, that there is direct continuity between Iremic and modern Coptic.<br /> <br /> Nomes have any rule or relevance tied to them? Because reading the entire book, it seems like a pretty minor idea that's there just for the sake of putting more Egyptian words in the Lexicon (as a curiosity, <i>nome</i> is &quot;name&quot; in Portuguese, so reading this particular word is funny).<br /> <br /> More questions to come in the near future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T19:14:11-07:00","id":1552680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552677#post1552677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there any concrete information on <b>A'aru</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope. It's the Heaven to Duat's Hell vis-a-vis the moral test that the Judges created humanity to administer, and there's a little bit of loose description in Dreams of Avarice, but it's not a Proper Metaphysical Dimension\u2122 that matters to the day-to-day Chronicles cosmology or anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What is <b>Apotheosis</b>? I didn't really got what it is meant to represent in the fiction, even as a legend, despite having rules for it. </div> </div> </div>Apotheosis is reclaiming your Name from the Judges and thus ceasing to be a slave to the Rite of Return, thematically trading the tremendous power of Sekhem and cult backing for the ability to self-determine and live like a mortal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are there rules for the other Minor Guilds besides the Shuankhsen? Are there better rules for the Shuankhsen (because I'm under the impression that they're actually pretty weak for Mummies)? </div> </div> </div>The Shuankhsen are not a Guild at all and all the material for the Minor Guilds in 2e is in the Book of Lasting Death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Decrees are another thing that I didn't quite understood what they are within the fiction. They're related to an aspect of the soul, but what did the Arisen declared, exactly, to the Judges? </div> </div> </div>Your Decree is what Pillar you pin your selfhood on, which informs them as splats as the kind of person who thinks their essential nature, drive, passion, history, or occult knowledge is the most important part of being who they are.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Several times the book aludes to mummies whose Semektet have wildly different durations, from a single day to several decades, <b>by design of their Judges</b>, but outside the Conditions <i>Graceful</i>, <i>Auspicious</i> and <i>Precipitous Descent</i>, which are quite limited in this effect, the rules don't really back this up all that much. Is there any additional rule, or something I didn't notice, that can <u>significantly</u> change the frequency of Descent Rolls? </div> </div> </div>See &quot;Slowing Down the Loss of Sekhem&quot; on p. 202. Also, mummies who awaken during a Sothic Turn don't lose their last dot of Sekhem purely from the passage of time and thus can putter along for as long as they neither die nor blaspheme.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The rules from the old <i><b>Immortals</b></i> book are compatible with Mummies (I already know the Endless are basically the same in the fiction, with simplified versions of the original rules, I just want to know if re-reading that book will add something of value)? </div> </div> </div>If you want to draw inspiration for translating or inventing additional types of immortals into the Endless framework you can certainly do so, but the material in Immortals is written under the assumption that (with the exception of the generalized lifespan-siphoning of the Harvesters) the characters that book allows you to create don't occupy a unified metaphysical or mechanical framework beyond being part of the same setting and using the Storytelling System.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Language-wise, is there any real distinction between Iremic and various-eras Egyptian, aside random proper names? Not a complaint, just a curiosity, I generally enjoy reading Egyptian. And that does mean, curiously, that there is direct continuity between Iremic and modern Coptic. </div> </div> </div>I do not know if there is a linguistic rule applied to Iremic in relation to ancient Egyptian like there is for the First Tongue and Ancient Sumerian.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Nomes have any rule or relevance tied to them? Because reading the entire book, it seems like a pretty minor idea that's there just for the sake of putting more Egyptian words in the Lexicon (as a curiosity, <i>nome</i> is &quot;name&quot; in Portuguese, so reading this particular word is funny). </div> </div> </div>They're the local inter-cult/inter-guild government for the Arisen. In 1e this was partially the domain of the Guild Status Merit, but in 2e that's been supplanted by the addition of one's cult's Dominance to Social rolls dealing with members of their own guild. Narratively they're there to underline the way mummies tend to congregate and coordinate; I'm not sure why the 2e lexicon uses the singular &quot;mummy&quot; in its definition, but it's a similar phenomenon to Caucuses and Consilia in Mage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-27T21:47:28-07:00","id":1552685,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552680#post1552680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Shuankhsen are not a Guild at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, but are there better rules for them? Are they weak in practice, or is it just my impression?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552680#post1552680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your Decree is what Pillar you pin your selfhood on, which informs them as splats as the kind of person who thinks their essential nature, drive, passion, history, or occult knowledge is the most important part of being who they are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but my question is about their role within the fiction, or to be more precise, <b>how</b> the decree itself happens and why. All the effects are perfectly fine as the result of that Pillar being your most essential nature, but what and why do you say anything about this to the Judges?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552680#post1552680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do not know if there is a linguistic rule applied to Iremic in relation to ancient Egyptian like there is for the First Tongue and Ancient Sumerian.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least for the Core book, there isn't.<br /> <br /> First Tongue is basically Sumerian converted through the Grimm's Law (a description of the process through which Proto-Indo-European became Proto-Germanic), with a lot of needed neologisms. So it is a constructed tongue despite based in a real world language.<br /> <br /> Every single word of &quot;Iremic&quot; in the core book for Mummy 2nd ed is just Egyptian, although not necessarily from the same period, the only exception being <i>some</i> proper names, like Azar. But Anpu, for example, is really one name for Anubis, as is Ammut for Ammit. A benbenet is a capstone for pyramids and obelisks in the form of a pyramidion, usually made of stone and covered with copper. A nomes is a province, the 42 Assessors of Ma'at were the gods of the 42 provinces of the unified Egypt, and so on.<br /> <br /> The only major exception from things being Egyptian (or plain English or Greek now and then) is that &quot;Irem of the Pillars&quot; is cited on the Quran, and a lot of debate exists on which city (if any) it actually refers too (although no one seems to think it was in Egypt). It has some variations on spelling, with Iram being more common, but Irem is there. The epithet &quot;The Nameless City&quot; for Irem comes from Lovecraft, and he does use the Irem spelling.<br /> <br /> Oh, and Sybaris was a Greek colony in south Italy.<br /> <br /> I wanted to know if this changes in the supplements, but I'll see it myself then, it's ok.<br /> <br /> __________________________________________________ __________________________________________________ ______________________<br /> <br /> What's the relationship between Ammut and the Judges? And what do the Judges really care about the culture of Irem?<br /> <br /> Is there any hint to the fate of the Shan'iatu (save the ones who became Temakh for the Akhem-Urtu)? Or to what the Judges think of them?<br /> <br /> How does the appearance of the Sahu works, exactly? The book isn't really clear on that. Is the Arisen only able to pass for human at Sekhem 5 or less? Are they human-looking most of the time? Do they cease to cause Sybaris below Sekhem 6?<br /> <br /> Most other things I think I'm getting a better grasp at with a new read on the book. I think a lot of the problems I had was information not being provided in the most intuitive sense, at leas for me, and I hadn't read 1st edition Mummy to have a context for anything at first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T07:08:33-07:00","id":1552699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552685#post1552685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, but are there better rules for them? Are they weak in practice, or is it just my impression?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Better rules&quot; is really pushing the line of Simple Questions, because the only other rules are from the 1e corebook and I don't browse the STV enough to know if someone has attempted to make an alternative 2e conversion.<br /> <br /> And yes, the Shuankhsen are meant to be nominally weak compared to the Arisen; they were slaves given their necromantic shrouds as what the Shan'iatu thought would be a simple up-front cost to Ammut. They're dangerous chiefly because they don't need to worry about losing their memories and they still leverage many of the benefits of the Arisen condition toward corrupting and destroying the works of Irem in service to the Devourer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, but my question is about their role within the fiction, or to be more precise, <b>how</b> the decree itself happens and why. All the effects are perfectly fine as the result of that Pillar being your most essential nature, but what and why do you say anything about this to the Judges? </div> </div> </div>The Judges tested the Arisen during the Rite of Return to decide if they were worthy of eternal service. If you didn't declare a Decree as an exercise of Will, you were obliterated.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's the relationship between Ammut and the Judges? And what do the Judges really care about the culture of Irem?<br /> <br /> Is there any hint to the fate of the Shan'iatu (save the ones who became Temakh for the Akhem-Urtu)? Or to what the Judges think of them? </div> </div> </div>A bunch of this is described in the creation myths in Dreams of Avarice (which I summarized <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1349103-judges-are-they-great-old-ones-or-idigama?p=1350179#post1350179\">here</a>) and to a lesser extent in Book of the Deceived, but long story short, there's two sets of &quot;Judges,&quot; of which the temakh who became the Arisen's original guildmasters are both one set and extensions of the other and created Irem as a white mutiny against their divinely-assigned role of instructing humanity so they were smart enough to sin, then sacrificed it because Ammut maneuvered them into doing so with the claim that the eternal propagation of Irem's cultural and artistic roots would serve as proof that they had done their job and thus might earn the heavenly reward humans were being tested to earn.<br /> <br /> Ammut is considered cosmically necessary by the descendants of her cosmological peers; the Judges of Life were prepared to feed her a tenth of all creation when she threatened to destroy the newly-minted world, and the Judges of Death are the temakhs who broke reality to honor the devil's bargain she offered them when they started to catch mortality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does the appearance of the Sahu works, exactly? The book isn't really clear on that. Is the Arisen only able to pass for human at Sekhem 5 or less? Are they human-looking most of the time? Do they cease to cause Sybaris below Sekhem 6? </div> </div> </div>Sybaris is triggered by the circumstances described on Page 203 of the corebook, only one of which involves witnessing the corpse form of the Arisen and none of which strictly stop being able to happen at any level of Sekhem.<br /> <br /> The sahu is a magically created/maintained corpse-form with an illusion over it that broadly draws from the mummy's self-image, the balance/intention being that at levels of Sekhem high enough to support superhuman Traits the mummy is more overtly supernatural (though it's not clear why in the change from 1e to 2e Sekhem 6-8 changed from &quot;in the last ten years of their life&quot; to &quot;walking mummified body&quot;) and thus more incentivized to either rely on their cult for aid or make quick or careful moves in person leveraging the bigger stick their magical might affords them. 1e had mechanics where the triggering of severe or extreme derangements could physically alter the sahu in ways that could become full Flaws with repeated manifestations, and the Deceived's sahu were likewise warped by the temakh sharing their souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-28-2025, 10:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T08:13:31-07:00","id":1552700,"title":"","content":"On the &quot;better rules&quot; I only meant official material, so that's a no and it's ok. The reasoning is also solid.<br /> <br /> Do the Shan'iatu still exist in modern times?<br /> <br /> So, if I understood, the descriptions given for the levels of Sekhem are for the &quot;illusion&quot; around the Mummy, right? &quot;Below&quot; it the Arisen simply look like, well, a mummy, regardless of the origin of their current body (a cultist, or an entirely new body after the last Semektet ended in full obliteration). And the book also don't explain from where the body comes, I have an idea because I actually know what's a <i>sahu</i> and its distinction from the <i>khat</i>.<br /> <br /> There's something I forgot to ask earlier: what's the limit on Pillar Points? I'm assuming it's the dots in each Pillar, but I don't remember the book ever stating anything about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T09:19:37-07:00","id":1552701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552700#post1552700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do the Shan'iatu still exist in modern times?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shan'iatu are in Duat, having effectively noclipped their way into Hell with no way out due to not being subject to the judgment that would get them into A'aru; they are not subject to the torments of fiends, but neither is it a pleasant existence, and they take a tithe of their mummies' Sekhem to make their divine house arrest more comfortable and on the outside chance that it's possible to buy their way into Heaven with sufficient resources. Duat is outside of time and so it's a little tricky to answer this with an unambiguous &quot;Yes&quot; even before 2e introduced Timelessness into the foreground.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, if I understood, the descriptions given for the levels of Sekhem are for the &quot;illusion&quot; around the Mummy, right? &quot;Below&quot; it the Arisen simply look like, well, a mummy, regardless of the origin of their current body (a cultist, or an entirely new body after the last Semektet ended in full obliteration). And the book also don't explain from where the body comes, I have an idea because I actually know what's a <i>sahu</i> and its distinction from the <i>khat</i>. </div> </div> </div>This is my understanding as well, yes. Timelessness means the precise provenance of the body takes a bit of a backseat to horror logic, but the undisguised form of the Arisen is described rather vividly in 1e as &quot;a simulated corpse made out of congealed necromancy.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's something I forgot to ask earlier: what's the limit on Pillar Points? I'm assuming it's the dots in each Pillar, but I don't remember the book ever stating anything about it. </div> </div> </div>Pillars are capped at a capacity of 5 each, for a total of 25 max; Inheritors can hold another 100 total per mummy overall, with the capacity per Inheritor determined by their level in the pyramid described on pages 83 and 84, as indicated in the Rite of Investment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T10:52:43-07:00","id":1552702,"title":"","content":"In Egyptian cosmology, the Sah or Sahu is a spiritual body formed by the gods after the Judgement of the Heart to contain the relevant aspects of the soul, in substitution of the corpse. So, it can be understood as a body of materialized ephemera, or something similar. While MtC's Sahu isn't exactly the same, a similar concept can be easily applied.<br /> <br /> Now, is there a way to flip the bird to the Shan'iatu and deny them their tithe in Sekhem?<br /> <br /> And yes, I imagined if they were in Duat it wasn't technically modern times, but it's clear enough.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T11:51:15-07:00","id":1552704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552702#post1552702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, is there a way to flip the bird to the Shan'iatu and deny them their tithe in Sekhem?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Apotheosis in a nutshell; 2e provides some alternative methodologies, but the classic route is to reclaim an appreciable chunk of your soul and Memory (maxing out at least a couple of Pillars including your Name and raising Memory to at least 7), forsake their grander gifts (along with access to higher-tier Utterances and the use of any relics that would require greater power), and limit your Sekhem to the one dot that actually belongs to you.<br /> <br /> In exchange, you remember everything that's happens to you in Duat, become functionally invisible to the mystical world with the reclamation of your True Name, gain the ability to create relics yourself instead of simply tracking and consuming Sekhem, use your Memory rating in place of Sekhem for most other mechanical purposes, and can use Pillars and Willpower to heal aggravated damage (which in 1e cost a Willpower point and a dot of Sekhem per aggravated wound). Also, as in 2e, you don't descend to Duat at Sekhem 0 but instead undergo a death cycle.<br /> <br /> You could also just deliberately do bad at your job, but while the Judges are holding your leash that's a plan of attack that doesn't have a very good exit strategy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 07-28-2025, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T17:24:14-07:00","id":1552707,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about something to deny only the Shan'iatu, not necessarily the Judges, but ok. I think I don't have remaining simple questions, except maybe things I'll read in supplements, if and when it happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T18:34:11-07:00","id":1552709,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552707#post1552707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was thinking about something to deny only the Shan'iatu, not necessarily the Judges, but ok.</div> </div> </div> </div>The trouble is that the Shan'iatu <i>are</i> the Judges, both in the metaphysical sense of being sinister extensions of the Judges and in the practical sense of being the ones who the Arisen most directly serve; they are a nesting doll of bastard Demiurges whose vaster selves gave them the finger when they tried to clever-dick their way into a test their relationship to the administrators disqualified them for, and they are cosmic beings whose lesser expressions went rogue trying to invent Kings and Empire to glorify themselves because they got jealous of their students \u2014 students created begrudgingly because the metaphysical Cool Uncle said they couldn't force any part of life to cease completely.<br /> <br /> These are beings who managed to &quot;fuck you, got mine&quot; <i>their own selves</i>, because when an extension of the Judges tries to become a Judge it turns out the response is &quot;I'm already a Judge, you dumbass, do you want me to pass the scepter from one hand to the other? Never in a million years.&quot; The Judges may not have directly devised the Rite of Return and the Nameless Empire from on high, but they absolutely benefit from these things and make no effort to release the Arisen from their servitude. Little to nothing is gained from only denying the Judges' collective left hands, since the Deceived are the only ones for which there is a practical distinction between the Judges and their temakhs, and those folks don't have Decrees and can't get remotely close to entering Duat anyway.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T18:45:03-07:00","id":1552711,"title":"","content":"How much of this is known by any Arisen (assuming Memory 10), how much requires finding arcane knowledge (even to them)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-28T19:32:23-07:00","id":1552713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552711#post1552711\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much of this is known by any Arisen (assuming Memory 10), how much requires finding arcane knowledge (even to them)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Much of this comes from Dreams of Avarice, which is framed as an in-universe document commissioned and distributed by the Heretic. The Heretic himself seems to have gotten some of its lore from old-fashioned occult archaeology and and others from more esoteric means of invoking the gods for testimony, but given that his goal in creating <i>Dreams of Avarice</i> was to spread word of the process of Apotheosis it's not hard to imagine some copies have found their way around the world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-30T23:23:51-07:00","id":1552763,"title":"","content":"Ok, I ended up with another set of simple questions. Is there any errata on the rules for spending Pillar Points?<br /> <br /> It says that you can only spend Pillar Points to increase Physical Attributes once per scene. Is it per Attribute, per Pillar, or at all?<br /> <br /> You can spend from your Decree's Pillar to increase the Decree's Attributes on a 1 to 1 basis, but those increases are for each Attribute, or for both?<br /> <br /> Finally, it isn't clear if showing your <i>Sahu</i> is an effect of any spending, or if it's an optional use of a Pillar Point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T07:26:34-07:00","id":1552770,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552763#post1552763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I ended up with another set of simple questions. Is there any errata on the rules for spending Pillar Points?<br /> <br /> It says that you can only spend Pillar Points to increase Physical Attributes once per scene. Is it per Attribute, per Pillar, or at all?<br /> <br /> You can spend from your Decree's Pillar to increase the Decree's Attributes on a 1 to 1 basis, but those increases are for each Attribute, or for both?<br /> <br /> Finally, it isn't clear if showing your <i>Sahu</i> is an effect of any spending, or if it's an optional use of a Pillar Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rules are not very clear, my interpretation is:<br /> <br /> -At all, but you can spend multiple points to boost the attribute, each point gives the Sekhem boost rating (4 per point at Sekhem 10)<br /> <br /> -For this i consider Gift of the golden ankh as a way to do onto others what you can do on yourself, so i would say that you choose one of the two attributes to boost<br /> <br /> -In the Sybaris chapter it lists as a possible trigger &quot;Witnessing a mummy spend a dot of Sekhem or a Pillar point&quot;, so i assume that in those cases the Sahu reveals for a turn","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T07:42:05-07:00","id":1552771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552763#post1552763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finally, it isn't clear if showing your <i>Sahu</i> is an effect of any spending, or if it's an optional use of a Pillar Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not optional, it's a drawback akin to how Prometheans spending Pyros causes their disfigurements to be briefly revealed; the Arisen can better take advantage of Sybaris than the Created can Disquiet, but Sybaris is still Bad News that can inadvertently summon fiends, curse the area, or put one of their vessels at risk of breaking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-31T18:39:10-07:00","id":1552786,"title":"","content":"The wording on this section is really awful, but I see no reason not to take your word for it in the lack of an errata.<br /> <br /> And I agree that everything points to the <i>Sahu</i> revelation being a drawback, not an option, it's just that in <b><i>this section</i></b> it isn't what's written at all...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-01T11:44:38-07:00","id":1552809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552763#post1552763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, I ended up with another set of simple questions. Is there any errata on the rules for spending Pillar Points?<br /> <br /> It says that you can only spend Pillar Points to increase Physical Attributes once per scene. Is it per Attribute, per Pillar, or at all?<br /> <br /> You can spend from your Decree's Pillar to increase the Decree's Attributes on a 1 to 1 basis, but those increases are for each Attribute, or for both?<br /> <br /> Finally, it isn't clear if showing your <i>Sahu</i> is an effect of any spending, or if it's an optional use of a Pillar Point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe the question about Pillars was asked before on this thread, possibly by me (can't remember very well). If you have a look through the older questions you should find a few posts discussing various interpretations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T19:01:05-07:00","id":1552897,"title":"","content":"According to the core book 2nd edition, Mummies suffer Bashing damage from weapons, but apparently they take normal damage from any other natural source. Is that right, or is there another information in another source?<br /> <br /> The 10 actions that provoke a Descent Roll in page 201 seem to be quite easy to avoid under most circumstances. Is there an expanded list that's more worrisome, or a more strict interpretation in some other canon source, is it easy by design?<br /> <br /> In this same list, one particular item comes to the fore: &quot;Interacting with a Lifeless without obvious enmity&quot;. The book isn't very consistent on what a Lifeless is, if it refers to every non-Arisen &quot;undead&quot;, or only to the Shuankhsen. Are both valid interpretations here, or is it better explained somewhere else?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T19:31:33-07:00","id":1552899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552897#post1552897\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the core book 2nd edition, Mummies suffer Bashing damage from weapons, but apparently they take normal damage from any other natural source. Is that right, or is there another information in another source?</div> </div> </div> </div>Given the tenor of their general imperishability, I would interpret Arisen damage resistance roughly the same as what vampires get; the equivalent section in 1e doesn't differentiate between natural and artificial weaponry and there's little thematic basis for nonmagical animals to be more dangerous to mummies than nonmagical objects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The 10 actions that provoke a Descent Roll in page 201 seem to be quite easy to avoid under most circumstances. Is there an expanded list that's more worrisome, or a more strict interpretation in some other canon source, is it easy by design? </div> </div> </div>It's very easy to avoid pissing off the Judges if you only do the things they want you to and never pursue a life of your own, yes. Things going wrong enough to potentially necessitate cannibalizing a relic is the one that's potentially the easiest to come up in the course of the default gameplay loop, but the 1e version of the list is followed by:<br /> <br /> &quot;That\u2019s it! Other than avoiding certain occult atrocities and paying lip service to the culture that owns her obedience anyway, the only thing that puts an Arisen at risk is being a person. One can be a pretty evil sonofabitch without imperiling one\u2019s status in Duat.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In this same list, one particular item comes to the fore: &quot;Interacting with a Lifeless without obvious enmity&quot;. The book isn't very consistent on what a Lifeless is, if it refers to every non-Arisen &quot;undead&quot;, or only to the Shuankhsen. Are both valid interpretations here, or is it better explained somewhere else? </div> </div> </div>&quot;Shuankhsen&quot; was used in the equivalent item in 1e, but treating other undead with contempt is almost certainly within spec.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T20:39:43-07:00","id":1552903,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552899#post1552899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's very easy to avoid pissing off the Judges if you only do the things they want you to and never pursue a life of your own, yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the exception of raising Memory, I'm not sure that even pursuing a life of your own makes a Descent roll likely.<br /> <br /> I do remember of somewhere it stating that avoiding following the Judge's Mission calls for a Descent Roll, but I can't remember where it is, and it isn't in page 201's list. I don't see blasphemy against the gods and declaring your love for a normal person in Iremic as regular things you do just to be yourself.<br /> <br /> But again, I don't remember where every Descent roll is described. This same section doesn't inform that creating a Sadikh provokes a Descent Roll, for example, and it does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T21:22:58-07:00","id":1552904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552903#post1552903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With the exception of raising Memory, I'm not sure that even pursuing a life of your own makes a Descent roll likely.<br /> <br /> I do remember of somewhere it stating that avoiding following the Judge's Mission calls for a Descent Roll, but I can't remember where it is, and it isn't in page 201's list. I don't see blasphemy against the gods and declaring your love for a normal person in Iremic as regular things you do just to be yourself.<br /> <br /> But again, I don't remember where every Descent roll is described. This same section doesn't inform that creating a Sadikh provokes a Descent Roll, for example, and it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>The books don't outright say it, but 1e makes pretty direct implication that failing to pursue or investigate what it terms the &quot;first purpose&quot; \u2014 the reason the mummy was awakened \u2014 results in accelerated loss of Sekhem; depending on how the ST opts to run it this could be anything from directly ignoring the imperative the Call was used for provoking a Descent roll to simply being more lenient with which timer is being used while they're actively on the job, but the narrative function of it is to emphasize that the Rite of Return instills the Arisen with purpose when they arise outside the auspices of Sothis ascending.<br /> <br /> As for the rest, it's worth remembering that the Judges are counted among the gods of Irem (and that it's still a Descent trigger if someone else does it and you don't correct them), that one of the reasons mummies might divert from their course is due to developing personal connections (and recall that, enhanced capacity for linguistic acquisition notwithstanding, the native language of the Arisen is Iremic, hence the further isolation they experience from their cults and themselves being the main speakers they will encounter), and that developing Memory is not an abstract exercise devoid of emotional context.<br /> <br /> 1e had a sidebar going over the two broad categories of reasons mummies might be diverted from their purpose, and they boil down to pursuit of self-knowledge and occult lore (potentially including Apotheosis) and satisfaction stemming from fixation or loss of faith (throwing themselves into the pursuit of e.g. power, wealth, or love). Touchstones can be based on mortals you once knew, and uncanny resemblances to loved ones you now barely remember is one of the multiple angles this game takes toward motifs of reincarnation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T22:17:13-07:00","id":1552908,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552903#post1552903\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> With the exception of raising Memory, I'm not sure that even pursuing a life of your own makes a Descent roll likely.<br /> <br /> I do remember of somewhere it stating that avoiding following the Judge's Mission calls for a Descent Roll, but I can't remember where it is, and it isn't in page 201's list. I don't see blasphemy against the gods and declaring your love for a normal person in Iremic as regular things you do just to be yourself.<br /> <br /> But again, I don't remember where every Descent roll is described. This same section doesn't inform that creating a Sadikh provokes a Descent Roll, for example, and it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, consider the last one, Telling your true name to an outsider.<br /> This means that you should use a pseudonym interacting with people not of the cult.<br /> But any time you use it, it s a memory breaking point (Lapses, concealing identity)<br /> This means that basic interaction with human outside the mission is always complicated","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-04T22:56:16-07:00","id":1552910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1552908#post1552908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This means that you should use a pseudonym interacting with people not of the cult.<br /> But any time you use it, it s a memory breaking point (Lapses, concealing identity)</div> </div> </div> </div>That depends on interpretation (hence I asked if there are more rigid interpretations elsewhere).<br /> <br /> Using a pseudonym or other alternative name isn't necessarily hiding your identity. Or is using a nickname a deception?<br /> <br /> I think it should only apply when there's an actual intention at deception. Giving the name you chose to use for your current life is quite different from trying to conceal yourself behind a false identity or trying to pass a someone else.<br /> <br /> But yes, depending on interpretation this can be quite hard to deal with, you got it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-08T15:30:38-07:00","id":1553016,"title":"","content":"My take from the core book is that Ammut isn't antagonistic to the Arisen, or at least shouldn't be. Yet, the Shuankhsen are. What's the deal with the Devourer (aside Devouring things)?<br /> <br /> I'm also under the impression that while Relics get more attention, Vestiges are actually more useful. Relics only have their listed powers to go for, and potential Sekhem. Vestiges give you extra Willpower recovery during sleep, and bonus dice to recover Pillars every chapter. Those two benefits seem to me to be better in general than anything else between those items, and the Judges don't seem to care a lot if you keep Vestiges to yourself. Did I miss something here, or is that correct?<br /> <br /> How do Traps and Curses work in a Tomb? At some point it's said that they trigger when a point of Peril is lost, is that it? And for how much time do they take effect?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-08T17:30:12-07:00","id":1553018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1553016#post1553016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My take from the core book is that Ammut isn't antagonistic to the Arisen, or at least shouldn't be. Yet, the Shuankhsen are. What's the deal with the Devourer (aside Devouring things)?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Devourer is universal entropy. She can be patient, given that the laws of reality forbid her from taking Sekhem that does not give itself to her, but her stated end goal is the cessation of all meaningful existence. She is playing the very long game necessary to make that complete in the race against ever-transforming creation, and having a collection of mummies whose vengeful tendencies are turned upon the servants of the Judges with the advantage of her own devouring jaws and memories that don't crumble away between lives like the desert sands are her most direct way to tilt things toward feeding the world into her maw.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm also under the impression that while Relics get more attention, Vestiges are actually more useful. Relics only have their listed powers to go for, and potential Sekhem. Vestiges give you extra Willpower recovery during sleep, and bonus dice to recover Pillars every chapter. Those two benefits seem to me to be better in general than anything else between those items, and the Judges don't seem to care a lot if you keep Vestiges to yourself. Did I miss something here, or is that correct? </div> </div> </div>Vestiges give you extra Willpower recovery <i>if they are resonant with you</i>, and ditto for the bonus dice on Pillar recovery; while this does lend more benefit than is obvious to the Balanced and Overburdened Merits (and to a lesser extent the Virtuous and Vice-Ridden Merits), a narrow subset of all vestiges being notionally more useful in the long term than relics is not surprising, especially given that it's the Sekhem that the Judges want from the relics the Arisen are charged to retrieve. (Also, the resonant benefits are <i>all</i> a vestige in your Lifeweb can provide for the first story after you're awakened thanks to the way the Call works.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do Traps and Curses work in a Tomb? At some point it's said that they trigger when a point of Peril is lost, is that it? And for how much time do they take effect? </div> </div> </div>They're stage hazards that apply their environmental Tilts on anyone who stumbles into them just as they would natural circumstances; the individual Tilts specify how they're ended, with many of them simply lasting for the scene or being permanent qualities of the Tomb.<br /> <br /> The notes about what happens when you sacrifice a dot of Perils or Provisions instead of Geometry just interact with the subsequent note on Attacking Tombs; otherwise, the security and amenities in your Tomb are interacted with as they would in a normal scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-08T23:41:20-07:00","id":1553020,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1553016#post1553016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Relics only have their listed powers to go for, and potential Sekhem. Vestiges give you extra Willpower recovery during sleep, and bonus dice to recover Pillars every chapter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Consider that a Relic can become the Harmonic centerpiece of the Tomb, giving the rating in Pillars every chapter<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-10T18:01:20-07:00","id":1553048,"title":"","content":"Are Open Rites available to anyone (if not stated otherwise), or just to non-splat humans?<br /> <br /> Was the Second Irem in Antarctica ever explored in another book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-10T18:28:59-07:00","id":1553052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1553048#post1553048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are Open Rites available to anyone (if not stated otherwise), or just to non-splat humans?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are the same phenomenon that Geist identifies as equivalent to zero-dot Ceremonies in the &quot;The Root of Power&quot; sidebar in that corebook. Anyone can perform them unless stated otherwise; the first line of the description is there to identify the difference between an Open Rite, a completely mundane action, and a supernatural power. The God-Machine effectively performs Open Rites on a grand scale through the medium of Infrastructure, and some Mysteries in Mage are the result of occult maneuvering or mishap to produce a supernatural outcome without directly casting spells.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Was the Second Irem in Antarctica ever explored in another book? </div> </div> </div>First Edition had no holdings for any of the guilds in Antarctica in Guildhalls of the Deathless. The Second Irem is a sample-setting-based plothook that isn't expanded upon elsewhere much the same as Destroyer Wolf stalking the Shadow of Basra or the city of Adelaide being the territory of reflection-dwelling bunyips who make the place periodically inimical to supernatural existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T05:26:29-07:00","id":1553087,"title":"","content":"According to the core, anyone who ends up in Duat will be tested and eventually seen by the Judges. I'm assuming the most likely outcome for a non-Mummy at that point is to either be fed to Ammut or sent to A'aru, but is there anything about this in other books? Both in general (which will mostly mean Shades) and/or particular kinds of visitors?<br /> <br /> The core has quick rules on Nehu, the Abandoned, and on Apotheosis. Is there somewhere more complete rules, or those are all there is to it? Not complaining, they're not incomplete or anything. But what about Arisen that get hold of the True Name of a Judge, or of Anpu?<br /> <br /> Is there any confirmed splat that can affect the Arisen with Time or Fate effects, besides Demons?<br /> <br /> <b>Precipitous Descent</b> makes the character's Sekhem 1 higher for the effect of Descent intervals and rolls, but what to do at Sekhem 10? Is the character forced to begin Descent below it? I'm personally thinking about making for half the interval of normal Sekhem 10, with an automatic dot loss at the end, no roll allowed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-08-12T06:24:55-07:00","id":1553089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1553087#post1553087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">According to the core, anyone who ends up in Duat will be tested and eventually seen by the Judges. I'm assuming the most likely outcome for a non-Mummy at that point is to either be fed to Ammut or sent to A'aru, but is there anything about this in other books? Both in general (which will mostly mean Shades) and/or particular kinds of visitors?</div> </div> </div> </div>Dreams of Avarice has the most lore on this at the moment, the contents of Duat being largely secret and/or obscure before a chronicle-framing minigame was included in the core systems. Suffice it to be said that the Judges are not interested in <i>anybody</i> attaining the fields of A'aru and the game is thematically more invested in characters acting in the sunlit lands.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The core has quick rules on Nehu, the Abandoned, and on Apotheosis. Is there somewhere more complete rules, or those are all there is to it? Not complaining, they're not incomplete or anything. But what about Arisen that get hold of the True Name of a Judge, or of Anpu? </div> </div> </div>All the options in that sidebar except for Apotheosis are new to 2e and have not yet been expanded on in any subsequent books.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is there any confirmed splat that can affect the Arisen with Time or Fate effects, besides Demons? </div> </div> </div>Same deal as the above; Timelessness is new and the only material that exists are the guidelines described in the same sidebar as says demons' powers work within the rules.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Precipitous Descent</b> makes the character's Sekhem 1 higher for the effect of Descent intervals and rolls, but what to do at Sekhem 10? Is the character forced to begin Descent below it? I'm personally thinking about making for half the interval of normal Sekhem 10, with an automatic dot loss at the end, no roll allowed. </div> </div> </div>I would say it just uses the intervals for Sekhem 10 and rolls 11 dice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-03T14:49:23-07:00","id":1554129,"title":"","content":"Oof, I feel like this question had been answered before, but I can't find the search anywhere, so just gonna re-ask.<br /> <br /> In 2e, can Deceived make a Sadikh, now? In 1e, their Cults were empowered more broadly but they couldn't have a Sadikh. I can't remember if design/intent was that Deceived STILL can't, but limited wordcount didnt cover it.. or if in 2e there was no reason to prevent Deceived Sadikhs and Inheritors, so it works for them mostly the same as for the Judged.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-10-04T03:34:22-07:00","id":1554140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cleverest of Things</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1554129#post1554129\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oof, I feel like this question had been answered before, but I can't find the search anywhere, so just gonna re-ask.<br /> <br /> In 2e, can Deceived make a Sadikh, now? In 1e, their Cults were empowered more broadly but they couldn't have a Sadikh. I can't remember if design/intent was that Deceived STILL can't, but limited wordcount didnt cover it.. or if in 2e there was no reason to prevent Deceived Sadikhs and Inheritors, so it works for them mostly the same as for the Judged.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pag 14 of the book of lasting death says that when you create a Deceived you use normal Mummy rules apart from 3 listed exceptions, and none of these are about Sadikhs","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T14:05:10-08:00","id":1556808,"title":"","content":"Is Anpu actually described anywhere? Not metaphysically, just like roleplay-wise.<br /> <br /> I've been working my way through the 2e core, and it's struck me that despite turning up in a good few places, I don't really have a clear idea of how Anpu is supposed to be played. Even basic stuff like whether he talks would be helpful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T14:58:14-08:00","id":1556809,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1556808#post1556808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Anpu actually described anywhere? Not metaphysically, just like roleplay-wise.<br /> <br /> I've been working my way through the 2e core, and it's struck me that despite turning up in a good few places, I don't really have a clear idea of how Anpu is supposed to be played. Even basic stuff like whether he talks would be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don t remember where, but it s written that it rarely talks, and when it do so it s always mysterious and phrophetic like","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-18T15:07:29-08:00","id":1556810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1556808#post1556808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Anpu actually described anywhere? Not metaphysically, just like roleplay-wise.<br /> <br /> I've been working my way through the 2e core, and it's struck me that despite turning up in a good few places, I don't really have a clear idea of how Anpu is supposed to be played. Even basic stuff like whether he talks would be helpful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dreams of Avarice and Book of the Deceived are the main examples of dialogue from Anpu.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-19T00:02:24-08:00","id":1556827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1556808#post1556808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Anpu actually described anywhere? Not metaphysically, just like roleplay-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>He's Anubis.<br /> <br /> Anpu is just another name of Anubis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-19T14:19:27-08:00","id":1556843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1556827#post1556827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He's Anubis.<br /> <br /> Anpu is just another name of Anubis.</div> </div> </div> </div>I meant personality-wise. Like, I get he's a big(?) guy with a jackal head, but that's not a character, that's a physical description.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-12-24T18:22:03-08:00","id":1556975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1556843#post1556843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I meant personality-wise. Like, I get he's a big(?) guy with a jackal head, but that's not a character, that's a physical description.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know, while we don't have many surviving myths that would help to get a sense of Anubis' personality, his <i><b>is</b></i> one of the most consistent depictions across pop culture for ancient gods, even Egyptian gods. Silent, patient, deliberate, slow moving, focus on the job, the works. Not universal, but unusually regular, that's why I posted that.<br /> <br /> Other than that, I don't think it would be a positive thing to describe him further. As someone who'll actually interact with the PCs on a regular basis and possibly have a huge impact on the game by default, I think it's better to have him as this placeholder character with a clear-ish function, but open for the ST to put whatever they want.<br /> <br /> Princes and whatnot are characters that need good characterization because they color particular settings, the Judges color a very particular moment where they fulfill a very specific narrative role (and even then we don't really have that much on particular personalities), but Anpu/Anubis will pop out every now and then and interact up close, it's personal. This shouldn't be decided for the ST as it can mess with a lot of dials for the chronicle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-20T14:30:08-08:00","id":1557789,"title":"","content":"Do Shuankhsen resurrect in the same way as the Arisen? Specifically, if you invade the space a Shuankhsen considers to be her tomb is there a danger of them rising up and attacking the way the Arisen do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-20T14:45:23-08:00","id":1557791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1557789#post1557789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Shuankhsen resurrect in the same way as the Arisen? Specifically, if you invade the space a Shuankhsen considers to be her tomb is there a danger of them rising up and attacking the way the Arisen do?</div> </div> </div> </div>The 2e corebook's sample character's writeup seems to suggest as much from the last line of its Storytelling Hints.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-20T18:01:35-08:00","id":1557792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1236140-ask-a-simple-question-get-a-simple-answer-mummy-edition?p=1556843#post1556843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I meant personality-wise. Like, I get he's a big(?) guy with a jackal head, but that's not a character, that's a physical description.</div> </div> </div> </div>Closest thing would be a small part on the Dark Eras Companion, an example of something that irritates Anpu (mages attempting to transport Arisen to anywhere they\u2019re not supposed to be). And <i>perhaps </i>the bits of Dark Eras 2 that mention that Anpu is another aspect of Death Wolf for some cults.<br /> <br /> <br /> If you think Goetic Anubis is representative of Anpu's character, then you could use the Mage 1ed Astral Realm book description as a guideline, I would say this is a big <i>maybe</i>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4967,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","user":"lbeaumanior","date":". 03-13-2026, 10:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4967-lbeaumanior","name":"lbeaumanior","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4967_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-08-01T19:24:16-07:00","id":1562452,"title":"","content":"So I'm working on a antagonist that has a higher than usual Willpower pool because of dark magic allowing him to drain mental fortitude from victims. I want to provide an edge to offset the many advantages Arisen will have over this character as a Sorcerer but as Willpower is a more critical and powerful resource in 2nd Edition I wanted some advice on how much will make for a more formidable opponent over an overpowered enemy. Any recommendations on a proper range?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:"